Oddar Meanchey Provincial Administration Celebrates the 112th Anniversary of International Women's Day March 8
(Oddar Meanchey): On the morning of March 9, 2023, Oddar Meanchey Provincial Administration celebrated the 112nd Anniversary of the International Women's Day on March 8 under the theme "Women Together for Peace for Development in the Digital Age".
The ceremony was attended by Mr. Pen Kosal, Governor of Oddar Meanchey Province, and Mrs. and Mr. Siprasit, Chairman of the Provincial Council, with the participation of provincial councilors, deputy governors, district governors, government officials from various relevant units.
Mr. Pen Kosal said that this day is held every year on March 8 to celebrate the achievements of women throughout history and around the world, especially to show that women have the same rights as men for 365 days. Likewise, we should join in the celebration, celebration and stand together for women's rights throughout the year, not just one day.
He said that this celebration is an important event to show the participation of our Cambodian compatriots with a strong will to encourage thinking, action to respond to practical needs, improve the economic, political and economic situation. Society, including the promotion of morality, dignity and human values.
Mr. Pen Kosal stated that the message of Her Majesty Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, the Queen Mother of Cambodia in Freedom, Dignity and Happiness, shows that much progress has been made to protect and promote women's rights. Recently, especially in eliminating discrimination against women and focusing on helping women to have full and equal participation in global development should also be proud.
But at the same time, there are still a number of challenges that need to be addressed, including domestic violence, rape, trafficking and sexual exploitation of women and children, and migration issues of concern. Seriously affect the economy and society.
