Deputy Governor of Kampong Speu Province: Garbage Disposal Severely Affects Sanitation and Environment
(Kampong Speu): Deputy Governor of Kampong Speu Province, Mr. Kao Sonnarith, said that the dumping of garbage or all kinds of waste in the field is not in accordance with technical standards, it will seriously affect the hygiene and the environment.
This statement was made at a workshop to disseminate laws, regulations and related issues related to the environmental protection sector, which was attended by representatives of employers, factories, enterprises, handicrafts in the province and the three garbage collection companies on March 9, 2023.
Mr. Kao Sonnarith said that littering in the open field really has a negative impact on the lives of people, especially can lead to serious damage to public health, damage to the beauty of the city or town of the province. All of these issues also affect the economy, society and tourism when sanitation and environment are unclean.
He advised local authorities in all districts and companies responsible for garbage collection to set appropriate guidelines to be submitted to the people, business owners and local handicraft factories to determine how to manage. Proper packaging, distribution or separation of solid and liquid waste and facilitate the operation, cleaning, collection, transportation and storage of garbage.
At the same time, the Deputy Governor strongly expects and believes that this outreach workshop will change the attitude of the people and workers in stopping the dumping of garbage or all kinds of waste in public places and especially to Escapes fines, including legal punishment.
Please also note that solid and liquid waste disposal in the city, the law stipulates that for those who do not comply with the packaging, segregation or distribution and storage of garbage on the streets is not appropriate at the time set for disposal. Littering in public places on the streets, improper burning of garbage in public towns will be fined from 10,000 to 200,000 riels, depending on the type of garbage.
For owners or managers of markets, business locations, companies, enterprises, etc. that do not have proper bins, packaging mixed with industrial waste or hazardous waste will also be fined. In the case of a person who fails to pay the fine on time, the fine will be increased two to three times, and if not paid within 90 days, the authorities will file a complaint to the court.
