Minister of Commerce delivers keynote address at High-Level Roundtable on Promoting Participation of Least Developed Countries in Regional Integration and International Trade
(Doha, Qatar): On the morning of March 7, 2023, Minister of Commerce Pan Sosak delivered a keynote address at the High Level Roundtable on Promoting the Participation of Least Developed Countries (LDC5) in Regional Integration. And international trade.
As part of the speech, Minister Pan Sosak thanked the Government of Qatar for hosting this important meeting and outlined Cambodia's regional integration and international trade strategy through access. ASEAN members and the WTO, as well as Cambodia's important role in these frameworks, are an important part of helping Cambodia achieve significant economic growth.
He added that Cambodia is also looking for potential trade partners to increase trade cooperation and establish bilateral free trade agreements to increase export markets and attract more investment.
He noted challenges related to development and trade, such as the loss of technical assistance, trade-related assistance measures, as well as the loss of trade preferences after leaving the LDC rating.
The Minister highlighted the important role of development partners in seamlessly integrating transitional strategies into the national aid and development programs of countries leaving the LDC before and after leaving.
At the forum, the meeting noted the priorities and needs of LDCs and countries preparing to leave the LDC category, and the chairperson will report these results to the member states during the adoption of the Doha Political Declaration and the closing session. Slovenia expresses intention to strengthen cooperation with Cambodia in trade, investment, health, water resources ...
