Ministry of Tourism and Kampong Thom Provincial Administration led the planting of more than 100 trees on the occasion of the 7th River Festival
(Kampong Thom): On the occasion of the 7th River Festival in Kampong Thom Province, the Ministry of Tourism and Kampong Thom Provincial Administration led the planting of more than 100 trees at the wedding garden in Trapeang Chambok Village, Trapeang Russey Commune, Kampong Svay District, Kampong Thom Province to promote And actively planting trees, protecting forests, and participating in preventing deforestation and forest crime.
The above tree planting activities took place on the morning of March 8, 2023 in the presence of Mr. Top Sopheak, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism and Mr. Un Bot, Deputy Governor of Kampong Thom Province, with the participation of civil servants of both ministries and institutions. Around the provinces, Khans and Sangkats, Fisheries Administration, Youth Scouts, UYFC Youth, a total of 2,200 AMT students.
On that occasion, Mr. Deputy Governor Un Bot said that planting trees on this occasion is an activity to show love for the environment, love the community. Planting a tree today is a huge savings for the next generation.
"Today's tree planting activities will be a driving force to encourage the public to continue planting trees and participating in the protection of existing forests for now and in the future," said the deputy governor.
Mr. Un Bot also mentioned the importance of forests as an invaluable resource that provides both social and economic benefits both now and in the future. Forests help reduce environmental pollution, reduce erosion, maintain water and air quality, trees add a special aesthetic, help maintain a balanced climate.
At the same time, Secretary of State Top Sopheak said that Cambodia is a country rich in cultural heritage, natural resources that are conducive to the development of ecotourism potential as an attractive destination and tourism product.
He encouraged the people, especially the newlyweds, to come and plant a tree in this wedding garden, because planting trees is not only for tourists, especially for the newlyweds, can be planted after preparation. After that, come and take care of it, grow it, save it for the next generation, and cultivate the spirit of planting trees to protect the forest.
"Trees can lack people, but people can not lack trees," he said, "wherever we need trees, even offices. He also called on the people to take part in the protection work if they did not take part in planting trees.
He added that "trees help attract tourists to visit and promote the community economy better. Where there are trees, there are tourists."
