Sin Chanserivutha, Undersecretary of State and Civil Aviation spokesman, said that the new Siem Reap-Angkor International Airport project will be completed by the end of March 2023 and ready for pilot testing during May or June. Officially launched in October 2023. As of March 5, 2023, construction is about 86% complete.
If nothing changes, the inauguration of the new Siem Reap-Angkor International Airport will be presided over by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and senior Chinese government officials.
He also said that after the opening of the new airport, the old Siem Reap Airport will be completely closed due to the new airport has the capacity to accommodate up to 7 million passengers per year.
He confirmed that the location of the old Siem Reap Airport after the closure has no plans to do anything, depending on the decision of the management.
According to Mr. Sin Chanserivutha, the new Siem Reap-Angkor International Airport is a Class 4E International Airport that can accommodate large and long-haul aircraft and can accommodate 7 million to 10 million passengers per year. It also has a warehouse of up to 100,000 tons per year.
The capital for the construction of the airport has reached more than 1,100 million dollars due to various crises, which caused the construction cost to exceed the original plan under an investment of about 880 million dollars.
