(Kampong Thom): To strengthen the quality of tourism services to celebrate the 7th River Festival in Kampong Thom Province, the Inter-Ministerial Commission for the 7th River Festival and the Ministry of Tourism have organized a workshop to disseminate and guide the owners and representatives of tourism businesses. Participate in strengthening the quality of tourism services for tourists.
In order to celebrate the 7th River Festival and to implement the content of the message of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, Permanent Secretary of State Tith Chantha requested all tourism businesses to strive to provide quality customer service. It is better not to raise the service fee too much, which can cause a bad image and not affect the tourist destination of Kampong Thom province.
He went on to advise tourism businesses to improve the quality of tourism services, as services must be good, up to standard and confident for tourists in line with the "one service, one standard" campaign. At the same time, all businesses also need to strengthen their competitiveness, starting from the daily practice and meet the needs of current customers like clean, good service, quality and hygiene.
In addition, Mr. Tith Chantha requested the Kampong Thom Provincial Administration, authorities at all levels and all private parties to work together to maintain security, public order, public toilets and the beauty of the city on the occasion of the river festival, based on Stung Sen Chea. The winner of 2 romduol flowers of the National Clean City Competition Movement in the past.
Please be informed that the 7th River Festival in Kampong Thom Province will be held from March 8-10, 2023 with the official opening ceremony presided over by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprittbandit.
According to the workshop, the River Festival aims to inspire the masses to participate in the conservation and development of sustainable river resources and to participate in achieving tourism diversification strategies by creating new tourism events for river provinces in Cambodia since. 2014, as specified in Sub-Decree No. 265, dated October 11, 2012 on the River Festival.
Cambodian-Chinese female engineers assemble grain to show solidarity on International Women's Day
(Phnom Penh): A group of Cambodian and Chinese female engineers from a Chinese construction company put together five types of grain to put together a picture to show the solidarity between Cambodian and Chinese female engineers.
This event was held on the morning of March 8, 2023 to celebrate the 112nd International Women's Day.
The five grains used in this picture include rice, soybeans, yellow beans, black beans and red beans. These five grains originated in the Tang Dynasty, a glorious reign in China. The combination of the five grains now symbolizes the prosperity and prosperity of the Cambodian and Chinese peoples.
On the occasion of International Women's Day, March 8, a group of Cambodian and Chinese women engineers selected grains from Cambodia to put together a drawing to express their expectations for harvesting them with good harvest. Good and wish yourself, friends and company prosperity.
Ms. Yu Qingxia, Project Team Leader, encouraged the female employees to write down their wishes and put them in a box, then the company will try to fulfill those wishes.
Ms. Cham Chanthy, the designer for the FTB Bank project, said that today's celebration of International Women's Day is the most special event she has ever had.
Ms. Chanthy stated, "I gained a lot of experience from working with engineers from different countries and projects through activities organized by a warm company."
This grain-painting event created a cultural exchange platform for Cambodian and Chinese female engineers and contributed to strengthening the friendship between the staff of the two countries and encouraging women to hold hands and use their great strength in Construction industry.
