The Legal Council held a meeting to summarize the work results for 2022 and set work directions for implementation in 2023.
(Phnom Penh): The Legal Council on March 7, 2023 held a meeting to review the work results for 2022 and work directions for implementation in 2023 under the chairmanship of Dr. Binh Chin, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister in Charge of the Office. Council of Ministers and Chairman of the Council of Jurists.
The meeting was held at the Friendship Building of the Office of the Council of Ministers with the participation of Excellencies, Lok Chumteavs, Ladies and Gentlemen and all officials of the Legal Council.
The Council of Jurists was established in 1994 and has been actively acting as a mechanism to accompany the Office of the Council of Ministers of the Royal Government in coordinating the work of drafting and reviewing and advising on draft laws and regulations to contribute to Strengthening the rule of law, ensuring legal security and legal coherence in line with the political, economic and social developments of Cambodia.
The meeting to review the work results for 2022 and work directions for the implementation of 2023 of the Council of Jurists ended smoothly and successfully.
