Ms. Tri Dana recently accused the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts of making it difficult for her to organize a traditional costume show at Angkor Sankranti, which she plans to spend about $ 100,000 on.
This reaction was also clarified by the Ministry of Culture that the Ministry does not intend to cause difficulties or hinder the intention. But what led to the delay in the response is that the Ministry needs to verify that the display of costumes is not in line with the form and procedures of Cambodia. The ministry confirmed that the dress code that Tri Dana wanted to show was flawed and needed to be corrected.
In a voice message broadcast this morning, Samdech Techo supported the action of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts. Samdech Techo emphasized that the correct verification of the form of clothing to avoid confusion when wearing to show in public during Angkor Sankranti.
The Prime Minister added, "If the Ministry allows the appointment to be different from the original image, the Ministry will be responsible to both the Royal Government and the National Assembly." "Do not forget that in our law, ministers are accountable to the Prime Minister and to the National Assembly."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructed Ms. Try Dana to accept the instructions and adjust according to the regulations of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts. If it is not acceptable, the appointment will not be allowed.
Samdech Techo emphasized that "the exhibition is good to promote the new culture, but if any exhibition is different from the Khmer art form, it is tantamount to destroying the Khmer culture." So no appointment is better than appointment. Therefore, let Ms. Try Dana cooperate closely with the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts.
In this audio message, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also reminded of Samdech's reaction regarding dressing in a Khmer movie in the past. Samdech Techo said that through these reactions, one can see that the leadership of Samdech is not negligent to lose the tradition and the original culture of the Khmer nation.
