(Phnom Penh): Phnom Penh Municipal Authority has summoned about 400 hotel owners, apartment owners and condominium owners to a meeting to promote the management of foreign labor in order to better manage foreigners in Phnom Penh to avoid committing crimes. Illegal at their place of residence.
This outreach meeting was held on the afternoon of March 7, 2023 in the presence of Mr. Huot Hay and Mr. Hun Surithy, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, representing Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh.
Mr. HUOT HAY stated that by inviting the owners or occupants of hotels, apartments and condominiums in Phnom Penh to this meeting, the authorities intend for all owners or occupants of hotels, apartments and condominiums to manage foreigners well in their locations. In particular, together fight all forms of human trafficking, prevent all forms of online gambling and prevent money laundering.
"As a first step, we are only disseminating the law, with the Phnom Penh administration giving the owners or owners of hotels, apartments and condominiums three months, April, May and June," Huot Hay said. After three months, a team with both types of law enforcement forces, local authorities, the Ministry of Interior and the Ministry of Labor will inspect your business location.
"Foreigners who come to do business and stay in Cambodia must understand the laws of Cambodia and apply them well to avoid committing any crimes other than Cambodian law," he said.
Mr. Hun Sorithy said that for this work, there are three stages that the owners or owners of hotels, apartments and condominiums need to know, including:
* First, the authorities must guide and disseminate so that you know the law and apply it so that you do not commit illegal acts until you are punished * Second: Implement administrative measures by inspecting the location * Third: Legal measures.
However, the two Deputy Governors of Phnom Penh asked all business owners to cooperate with the authorities so that we can jointly eliminate and prevent all kinds of crimes. The Director General of the International Peace Cooperation Office of the Council of Ministers of Japan recognizes and respects Cambodia for sending troops to actively participate in peacekeeping missions under the UN umbrella
(Phnom Penh): Mr. KANO Takehiro, Director General of the Office of International Peace Cooperation of the Council of Ministers of Japan, recognized and respected Cambodia for sending troops to actively participate in peacekeeping missions under the United Nations umbrella. Nations in countries affected by the fires of war since 2006.
This statement was made by the Director General of the Japan International Peace Cooperation Center on the occasion of his courtesy call on General Sem Sovanny, Director General of the National Peacekeeping Center, on the afternoon of June 7. 2023 at the National Peacekeeping Center.
General Sem Sovanny expressed his deep gratitude to the Japanese friends for the good cooperation and continued good relations for a long time.
Meanwhile, as Cambodia prepares for infrastructure to prepare for hosting the Tripartite Project in 2024, General Sem Sovanny expects Japan to participate in the Cambodia-Japan-UN tripartite operation, including the provision of equipment and training courses locally. And abroad to Cambodia.
General Sem Sovanny also requested the Japanese friends to open training to remove and destroy explosives and continue to provide short-term, medium-long engineering training as practiced in the past.
