Iran's top leader considers poisoning of schoolgirls to be unforgivable after public outrage
Tehran: Iranian state television reported on Monday that the country's top leader on Monday said polluting students was an "unforgivable" crime that should be punishable by death if intentional. Public anger. This is according to the publication by the AFP news agency on Tuesday, March 7, 2023.
According to Iranian state media and officials, since November 2022, more than 1,000 girls have fallen ill after being poisoned by some politicians blaming religious groups that oppose girls' education. The poisoning began in Qom and spread to 25 of Iran's 31 provinces, prompting some parents to take their children out of school and protest.
The school poisoning case comes at a time when Iran is protesting across the country, starting with the death of a young woman at a police detention center for allegedly violating the dress code.
