Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said this in an interview with reporters in the program "Celebrate 3 years, personal special number" on March 7, 2023 at Wat Botum Vatey Park, Phnom Penh.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said: "The use of electric vehicles in Cambodia is very much increased today, there are more than 700 (nearly 800 units), but every year more than 10 times the registration of vehicles. "The use of electricity has increased a lot every year."
Regarding the increase in the number of electric vehicle users, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said that the Royal Government has issued a sub-decree for the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to set up an inter-ministerial commission to develop a strategy on the use of electric vehicles.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol stated that Cambodia will encourage the use of electric cars more, while the average fuel vehicle will be taxed at 120 percent, while electric vehicles will be taxed at 60 percent. The state encourages a 50 percent discount on the tax rate.
According to the vehicle registration management system of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, the number of registered electric vehicles as of January 31, 2023 was 794, of which 408 were cars and 355 were tricycles. There are 31 units and motorcycles. Compared to the registration of electric vehicles in 2022 (662 units) and 2021 electric vehicles (63 units), an increase of about 951%.
In January 2023, 62 electric vehicles were registered with the Ministry of Public Works and Transport. Compared to January 2022, we saw a 124% increase in registered electric vehicles.
