Following the Prime Minister's order, the Minister of Labor chaired a meeting with factory owners to provide $ 70 subsidy to workers who will be suspended from April (Phnom Penh): Workers who have been suspended from their employment contracts will receive cash support from April. 2023 onwards, receiving $ 40 from the government and $ 30 from the factory, a total of US $ 70 per month during which they were suspended by the factory.
This support was reiterated in an inter-ministerial meeting with the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, the Ministry of Economy and Finance, and employers' associations involved in the garment, footwear and travel products and bags sector, chaired by Mr. Ith Sam Heng. Minister of Labor and Vocational Training on the morning of March 7, 2023 at the Ministry of Labor.
The meeting was held to discuss how to co-organize the opening of allowances for workers whose factories were suspended during the global economic crisis, as well as to follow the recommendations of Samdech Techo Prime Minister Hun Sen.
Minister Ith Sam Heng stated that the meeting agreed on the scenario of implementing the intervention to provide cash to workers who have to suspend their employment contracts from April 2023 onwards, as implemented by the Ministry during the crisis. Kovid-19 to facilitate the living conditions of workers.
"During the suspension of the employment contract, the Royal Government will contribute US $ 40 and the factory sponsor US $ 30, a total of US $ 70 per month," he said.
Representatives of the private sector thanked Samdech Techo Prime Minister for always giving high consideration, facilitating the private sector to be able to maintain the balance of its production business and help workers to maintain their jobs and income to solve the living time. There is a crisis.
After the representatives of the relevant parties raised the situation, challenges and solutions, Mr. Ith Sam Heng accepted the request that the private sector is facing difficulties to discuss and resolve with the relevant ministries and institutions.
The Minister thanked the private sector, especially the employers' association partners, for their good cooperation during the implementation of the last 10 rounds of government measures during the Kovid-19 crisis.
