(Kampong Chhnang): Mr. Sun Sovannarith, Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province, always asked the media in the province to help point out the illegal fishing activities in Kampong Chhnang, lest there be a gap between the authorities and professional officials.
In order to cooperate, he asked the media to help monitor and report to him personally or report to professional officers to jointly prevent and take effective action in accordance with the order of the head of the Royal Government, as well as together to conserve our fish species. To survive as well.
With the permission and the green light from the provincial governor, on the morning of March 6, 2023, a group of six journalists traveled in two ferry boats to a protected area called " Fish Breeding Conservation Area (Boeung Pra) ”which is a large fish species conservation area in Kbal Konlong village, Peam Chkork commune, Choul Kiri district, according to reports from the people living there.
Separately, near the above protected area, there is also a fishing community factory (Kbal Konlong) owned by Mr. So Thorn, the head of the fishing community, guarding the nearby protected area, which is not far from the crime scene, but there is still a lot of fishing crime in Widespread in the conservation lake near the guardhouse. Illegal fishing activities in the conservation area (Boeung Pra) above are in the pumpkin, wearing a shell, three palms, etc.
Please note that after the team reported and shot to Mr. Ngin Hun, Director of the Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries via telegram to ask the police to crack down and intervene in response to the report of the above journalists, we check There were 2 Peam Chkok fishing commune authorities, 6 officials led by Mr. Thmey, Peam Chkok fishing commune chief came down to crack down.
Regarding the case of cracking down on the above fishing crimes, Mr. Ly La, Director of Kampong Chhnang Fisheries Administration District, also confirmed to the media by phone that if the crackdown is not over today, tomorrow he will order the police to crack down more completely. .
Separately, Mr. Ngin Hun, Director of the Provincial Department of Agriculture, when he saw the picture of the fishing crime above, he said that when he saw the picture of the crime in such a protected area, he did not understand at all what the local officials were doing. He also confirmed that he will gather more forces to go down to crack down on the above crimes to not be left.
Residents in the area confirmed that all these fishing crimes, such as the installation of mosquito nets, the closure of canals, the closure of lake lakes and barricades in the protected areas, have been active for a long time. For a long time, small people like them did not dare to protest.
But today, they also rejoiced when they saw the working group and the authorities to crack down. At the same time, they also request more through the media to ask the leaders to help monitor regularly so that no fishing offenses like this occur in the fish species conservation area (Boeung Pra). In the years to come, to keep the fish species alive for the benefit of all of us.
In connection with this fishing crime, the media also received pictures of the activities of four fishing camps that people sent from Kampong Preah Korki commune, Baribo district, where the criminals were fishing all day on March 5. 2023 ago.
In response to the high recommendation of the Head of the Royal Government regarding the case of preventing and cracking down on fishing crimes, Mr. Sun Sovannarith, Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province, also committed to follow the orders of the Head of the Royal Government by striving to strengthen the strict implementation and Assign all these tasks to the local level to continue to be responsible at each local level.
He warned that district governors, deputy district governors, inspectors in charge of the Fisheries Commission, if they do not commit fishing crimes in their jurisdiction, must be held accountable before the Royal Government as well as the people. Also.
