Samdech Techo Hun Sen made this request during the celebration of the 112nd International Women's Day on March 8, the morning of March 7, 2023 at the Peace Palace.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo requested all relevant ministries, institutions, authorities at all levels, the private sector and all people to support and implement gender mainstreaming and empower women on the following priorities:
1. All ministries and institutions continue to pay attention to and promote gender mainstreaming into the national program policy framework, including reform programs, national frameworks, social protection, climate change and green development programs.
2. Continue to promote women's participation and leadership in the public, political and private sectors.
3. Ministries, Institutions, Private Sector and Relevant Partners Increase Investment in Empowering Women in the Digital Economy and Green Economy through the Development of Women's Entrepreneurship, Promoting the Women's Family Economy, Supporting the Well-Being Economy and Promote work-life and family balance programs.
4. Increase the participation of women and girls in digital science, technology, engineering, creative arts and mathematics (STEAM) to close the gender gap in the digital sector and expand vocational training programs for youth and women.
6. Continue to prevent all forms of violence against women and girls through the implementation of the National Action Plan on the Prevention of Violence against Women, expanding the scope and quality of multidisciplinary response services, assisting victims, providing free legal services and Strengthen the implementation of relevant laws and regulations.
7. Continue to promote social morality, values of Cambodian women and families by expanding the scope of parenting programs and educating children in a positive way and expanding a culture of non-violence and building a harmonious family.
8. Continue to implement environmental protection measures by expanding the scope of the implementation of the national social protection framework for vulnerable and disadvantaged groups in society, both in and out of the economic sector, and support maternal and child welfare to ensure Achieving universal health coverage aims to ensure equitable access for all citizens.
