Key remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of presiding over the celebration of the 112th International Women's Day on March 8
(Phnom Penh): On Tuesday morning, March 7, 2023, Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen presided over the celebration of the 112nd International Women's Day on March 8 at the Peace Palace.
The International Women's Day on March 8 is celebrated every year around the world to commemorate the struggle and heroism of women in demanding freedom and freedom from oppression.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen delivered a speech for more than 1 hour and 40 minutes, the following are the main contents of Samdech:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised and highly commended the Ministry of Women's Affairs, the Cambodian National Council for Women, relevant ministries, institutions, the private sector, civil society and national-international development partners who have contributed to the promotion of women's rights, status, role and welfare in Cambodia. As on the international stage.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen supports the theme "Women together to keep the peace for development in the digital age", which is really meaningful and important in the context of Cambodia needs to maintain peace and political stability, which is a necessary precondition and It is a solid foundation for the development of the nation in all fields and ensuring the well-being and living of the people in harmony.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls on philanthropists to help build dormitories for female students in Phnom Penh and other provinces.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen noted that after Samdech's call, the rift between the divorced couple on social media decreased.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen continues to call on spouses who are separated not to tear each other's reputations on social media, to honor each other, especially children.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that some foreigners do not talk about insulting Samdech and his wife, but instead protect the insulting group. Samdech Techo Hun Sen asks foreigners to respect the dignity of the Cambodian people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen decides to provide allowances to approximately 32,000 workers when the factory is suspended to receive the same benefits as during the Kovid 19 era.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the new mandate does not change the candidates for the Ministry of Women's Affairs and the Ministry of Culture.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that a study found that women have higher support for Samdech than men.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the women for their support of Samdech's leadership.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked Samdech Kittipritthbandit and claimed that what he had today could not be without his wife's participation.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen requested all relevant ministries, institutions, authorities at all levels, the private sector and all people to support and implement gender mainstreaming and empower women on eight priority issues.
