(Phnom Penh): After the people in Prey Lvea village, Sangkat Choam Chao II, Khan Por Sen Chey, many families reacted and protested against the non-signing of the transfer letter, on the morning of March 6, 2023, the governor of Por Sen Chey district, Mr. Sak Chan Kanharith, together with the officials, opened a public forum and solved the problems that have arisen for the people.
The ceremony was attended by officials from the Office of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction, Land and Cadastral, officials from around the district, as well as about 100 people who bought plots of land from the company "Yeap Sovanna" and they received only the title deed (soft title) ) The company has not yet divided the land.
On that occasion, the district governor allowed the people to express their opinions to all the questions and concerns that they have and kept it in mind, so the people asked many questions as they were asked. Residents inquired about the procedure for the transfer of real estate rights and the division of land with title deeds (hard title deeds), especially asking why the district governor did not sign the transfer letter for them to sell, etc. .
Mr. Por Sen Chey, the district governor, explained to the people that the reason why he refused to sign the contract was because the transfer letter had a hard title deed and the plot had not been divided yet, so the signing would be against the Ministry of Land Management. Land. He did not sign all the power of attorney, if the power of attorney was not related to the hard copy, he had already signed it.
The district governor explained the procedure for subdivision of plots, payment of title deeds and payment of stamp duty when delisting. He assigned officials from the Office of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction, Land and Cadastral Affairs to measure and divide the land for the people from March 6 onwards to issue the title to the people to use.
He said that the survey will take only two weeks, moreover, will be open, and the abbreviation will take about two months to complete, and he will help to accelerate and use the procedure. Provide details to prevent future problems.
Finally, the district governor advised all citizens who need to be transferred to take the documents to the OWSO by themselves, do not rely on the runners, which leads to a lot of money and even delays. Also. Acting Head of State issues Royal Decree appointing Chhim Serey Phuon as Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Interior
