Dr. Kin Phea: Samdech Techo Hun Sen is a Veteran Professional Diplomat, Top Negotiator and Father of Peace of Cambodia
This video clip reminds us of a long negotiation process that took place in almost every corner of the globe, including France, Thailand, Indonesia, North Korea, China, Japan and New York for peace. And national unification in Cambodia. The road to peace and national unity is a long one, and it is too long for the suffering of the Cambodian people.
The historic meeting between Prince Norodom Sihanouk and Samdech Hun Sen on December 2-4, 1987 in the French city of Ferdinand, opened the way for further negotiations until a peace agreement was solemnly signed in the city. Paris to address a wide range of political issues for the restoration of peace in Cambodia.
Of course, the Paris Peace Accords have not yet brought complete peace, as the Democratic Kampuchea or Khmer Rouge parties withdrew from the agreement and continued their rebel activities until the end of 1998. But the win-win policy, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, led Cambodia to achieve full peace and true national unity in December 1998, unprecedented in Cambodia's more than 500-year history.
