(Phnom Penh): On the morning of March 5, 2023, Dr. Osman Hassan, Senior Minister in charge of Special Mission and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group for Russey Keo District, presided over a gathering to celebrate the 112th Anniversary of International Women's Day. March 8, 2023 under the theme "Women together to keep the peace for development in the digital age" at the Modern 5 Center, Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh.
The event was attended by Ms. Touch Sarom, Permanent Member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian Women's Association for Peace and Development and Vice Chairperson of the Royal Government Working Group, Russey Keo District, Phnom Penh National Assembly Member and Royal Government Member, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh and Ladies and Gentlemen, All members of the ceremony, a total of 660 people.
In his welcoming remarks, Mr. Ek Khun Doeun, Governor of Russey Keo District, stated that the theme of this year's 112nd Anniversary Celebration is to continue to highlight the invaluable value of women's participation in maintaining peace. As well as actively participating in accelerating development in all areas, especially in this digital age.
He said that women and girls now have more access to education, income generation to help the family economy, while some women are working in both the public and private sectors.
In particular, Khan and Sangkat authorities must prioritize the implementation of gender mainstreaming and empowerment of women in order to create a conducive environment and opportunities for women and girls to continue to fully participate, exercise their rights and benefit from development in all generations of society. With peace and development in line with the digital age.
On that occasion, Dr. Osman Hassan said that women are important players in the development of society, they have many roles in the family and participate in various jobs in both the public and private sectors, in some parts women Can do better than men too.
He said that in the past, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has always encouraged all institutions, when there are appointments, to increase the appointment of women to reach 30 percent in ministries, institutions and departments.
He added that the Senate currently has 62 members, including 12 women. The National Assembly has 125 members, of which 26 are women, or nearly 21%, while in other institutions the number of women has also increased.
Finally, Dr. emphasized that women are now actively participating in social development in all fields and are indispensable players in the development of the country, and he encouraged women to continue their efforts to participate. With the government as well as participating in maintaining peace to get development in the future.
