Save the Children celebrates 6th Cambodia Hearing Day to highlight the importance of mainstreaming ear and hearing care
(Phnom Penh): The Save the Children Foundation celebrates the 6th Cambodia Hearing Day under the theme "Take care of your ears and hearing for all" to highlight the importance of mainstreaming ear and hearing care on the 5th March 2023.
The 6th Cambodia Hearing Day was attended by Dr. Chea Serey, Co-Founder of Save the Children Foundation, Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi, Co-Founder of Save the Children Foundation, Ms. Yim Chhay Linh Hun Many, Honorary President of the Medical Union of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, Mr. Em Chan Makara, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation and Secretary General of the Disability Action Council, Mr. Chhim Kim Hean, Founder of Food Cambodia.
"Ear and hearing health problems are the most common problems in the community, with more than 60 percent identified and intervened at the care level," he said. In primary health care services rely on training and capacity building at this early level, in which people will receive many benefits as well as help the country towards achieving the goal of global health care.
According to the World Health Organization, more than 1.5 billion people suffer from hearing loss, of which one in three is in need of hearing care and 80 percent. Living in low- and middle-income countries
According to the World Health Organization (WHO), 401 million people in the region have a hearing loss, and by 2050, 666 million will suffer from hearing loss. Nearly 80 percent of people with hearing loss live in low- and middle-income countries, and most do not have access to screening and treatment services.
Dr. Chea Serey stated that accelerating the implementation and investment in ear and hearing care to achieve the goal of 2030, including: Goal 1: Increase the examination and hearing of newborns by 20%. .
Goal 2: Increase the use of hearing technology in young people with hearing loss by 20% Goal 3: Reduce the incidence of hearing loss and hearing loss in children aged 5-9 years by 20%.
Dr. Chea Serey expressed his deep gratitude to Food for Cambodia for its hard work in humanitarian activities by visiting the places of ear, people, boys and girls in the provinces in Cambodia and would like to thank All the team who took the time, energy and precious time to make this day run smoothly.
Ms. Yim Chhay Linh Hun Many said that the Cambodian Hearing Day was organized with the financial support of the Save the Children Foundation, co-organized by Food for Cambodia. Hear in primary health care, an essential element of global health.
"As we have all received leaflets on ear health, hygiene and primary hearing, we can all understand the symptoms of ear disease, avoid and prevent hearing loss as individuals, do not include," she said. Anything in the ear, use earplugs and earplugs from loud noises and in noisy places, in case of any problems with the ear, consult a doctor immediately.
She said that when you become a person with a hearing loss, you face access to information, discrimination, difficulty communicating with others, poor education and job loss.
