Mr. HUN Many: It is right that young people continue to express their gratitude to the Cambodian People's Party for helping to liberate them from the Khmer Rouge regime
(Kampong Speu): Speaking on the occasion of the inauguration ceremony of the CPP members in Preah Nipvan commune, Kong Pisey district, Kampong Speu province, on the afternoon of March 5, 2023, Mr. HUN Many paid high attention to the words of commitment of the new member representatives. .
"Of course you did not go through the same experience as your parents, but it is fair that you still use this sentence of commitment, even though we are three generations apart, we go through history," he said. Only one. ”
This statement was made after hearing the commitment of new members who expressed their commitment to join the party and thanking the Cambodian People's Party for helping to liberate them from the Khmer Rouge regime until their current freedom. This.
In addition to the above, he also went on to explain to members that even if you do not go through the tragedy itself, it is right that you continue to use this sentence in the determination, because you also suffer negative influences. From that tragedy, because we went through the same history.
"You too are a victim because your parents went through the tragedy of our history," he said. He added that the continuation of the tragedy of the dark pages in history is to emphasize the unforgettable suffering of the Cambodian people who suffered under that regime, even though we are the younger generation and Surviving in a phase of complete peace.
With this historical basis, every young person of the next generation must continue to be committed to safeguarding the current peace that will continue forever and will absolutely prevent the recurrence of the genocidal regime in Cambodia.
Taking this opportunity, he also highlighted the development that brings local employment, the development of infrastructure and the progress in all areas that occur under the political program of the Cambodian People's Party under the shadow of peace and stability.
