A fire has engulfed the Rohingya refugee camp in Bangladesh, displacing thousands of people. A fire has engulfed the Rohingya refugee camp in Bangladesh, displacing thousands of people.
(Dhaka) - A huge fire broke out in a crowded Rohingya refugee camp in southern Bangladesh on Sunday, a fire official and the United Nations said on Sunday. This has evacuated thousands of people. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Sunday, March 5, 2023.
Over the past several decades, more than 1 million Rohingya refugees have fled Myanmar to Bangladesh, with about 740,000 starting to cross the border in August 2017 when the Myanmar military opened up. Brutal repression.
The situation in Myanmar has worsened since the military coup in 2021, and attempts to repatriate them have failed.
