At the opening ceremony under the chairmanship of Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the Army on March 5, 2023, Lt. Gen. But Sopheap stated, “We missed the two-year examination. This year, we see that you are motivated to apply for exams and have a lot of interest in the defense sector, confirming that under the leadership of Samdech Hun Sen has made young people very interested in the defense sector.
In addition, Lt. Gen. But Pheap emphasized that a large number of young men and women who have volunteered to participate in the competition within the ranks of officers, they all trust the leadership of the Royal Government.
"The number of applications for military service in 2023 has increased significantly compared to previous years, as there were more than 6,000 applications in just 15 days," he said. In 2019, there will be more than 8,000 applications per month. ”
The director of the Active Officers' Office confirmed that the recruitment process for the new generation of officers was accurate, transparent and uninterrupted, even without the Anti-Corruption Unit (ACU) observers. Stuck. If an individual is found to be interfering, the candidate will not have to change the subject.
In addition, Lt. Gen. But Pheap added that the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) 2023 recruitment exam will take 5 days, from March 4 to 8, 2023, there are 4 general knowledge and language examination centers. Overseas and a center for fitness exams in Phnom Penh. Unlike previous years, we have examination centers in the provinces and four other regional armies.
"All of you, he sees that the defense sector is a priority for our nation under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, a peaceful country, national defense must be a priority to protect the nation to survive, this is my view." . This is the additional emphasis of Lt. Gen. But Pheap.
For the opening ceremony, two examinations were held at Chea Si Santhor Mok High School, which was presided over by General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander of the Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, and second: Bak Touk High School. Under the chairmanship of Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Commander of the Army and Chairman of the Sub-Committee on Selection Examinations.
