Khmer Krom Youth Leader for Unity Supports Kem Sokha's Verdict (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Khmer Krom Youth for Unity has expressed strong support for the Phnom Penh Municipal Court's sentencing of Kem Sokha. They see this as a process of law enforcement and also a step towards preventing the color revolution movement leading to disaster in Cambodia.
Mr. Soeung Sotheany, President of the Khmer Krom Youth Group for Unity, emphasized that "believe in the trial court with facts and clear law."
Mr. Soeung Sotheany also emphasized that the legal action of the Cambodian authorities and courts against Mr. Kem Sokha is to prevent acts of treason as well as the color revolution movement that will lead to disaster for Cambodia.
"Thanks to the efforts of the Royal Government, we have been able to maintain peace and development for more than 40 years. "If the color revolution happens again, the nation will suffer another disaster." This is what Mr. Soeung Sotheany said.
Mr. Sotheany called on young Cambodians everywhere to support the Royal Government to maintain development and peace.
It should be noted that after more than 5 years of trial, the case of Mr. Kem Sokha's treason was announced on Friday morning, March 3, 2023.
Kem Sokha was sentenced to 27 years in prison for conspiracy with foreigners or conspiracy with foreigners committed in Cambodia and elsewhere between 2010 and September 3, 2017 as a criminal offense. And shall be punished in accordance with the provisions of Article 439 and Article 443 of the Penal Code.
He was also sentenced to an additional sentence, with the final revocation of the right to vote, the right to stand for election and the right to engage in other political activities under Article 450 of the Penal Code.
Mr. Kem Sokha was also prohibited from leaving the premises of the residence No. 97, Street 313, Village 7, Sangkat Boeung Kak II, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh, except with the permission of the Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
He was also prohibited from meeting with any person, both Cambodian or foreign, directly or indirectly through technology other than family members, except with the permission of the Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, subject to the necessary requirements.
The verdict against Kem Sokha has the support of the Cambodian people everywhere and in all walks of life.
