The document states that 19 applications, or 8% of the total, were rejected and 31 license applications were returned to the applicant company without action.
Republican Rep. Michael McCaul, chairman of the House Foreign Affairs Committee, released the license figures Friday after saying in Congress Tuesday that the licenses are worth more than $ 23 billion. Approved for suppliers to companies under the "Department of Commerce (Blacklist)" of the United States Department of Commerce in the first quarter of 2022.
