The US Department of Commerce defended its decision.
The Ministry of Commerce said in a statement: "All licenses contained in this data relate primarily to the export of low-tech ... and other goods that do not raise concerns about "National security ... is closely monitored." The ministry explained that the decision was made by the Ministry of Commerce, the Ministry of Defense and the Ministry of Energy. According to Reuters.
