For this purpose, the Sihanoukville Provincial Administration will organize a competition to select the winners of the production of a short video that educates the general public about the maintenance, protection and sustainability of the coastal environment and contributes to attracting national and international tourists. More and more international tourists visit Cambodia, especially in the coastal area of Sihanoukville.
This morning, the Ministry of National Defense opened the 2023 New Generation Officers Recruitment Exam with more than 6,000 candidates participating in the exam.
Lt. Gen. But Pheap emphasized that the fitness and sports exam program will be held on March 6, 2023 for the 25th generation of active duty officers, and March 7 for the 13th generation of Army officers. And on March 8, there will be the 14th round of officers and the military technical officers. For the exam location at the Special Forces Command.
For the opening ceremony, the exam was held in two districts: at Chea Si Santhor Mok High School, which was presided over by General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander of the Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, and second: Bak Touk High School. Under the chairmanship of Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Commander of the Army and Chairman of the Sub-Committee on Selection Examinations.
(Pursat): A man decided to end his life with his 4-year-old son, abandoned his wife because he was upset about kidney failure and could not afford further treatment.
This incident caused a surprise on the morning of March 4, 2023 in Dangkar village, Sangkat Phteah Prey, Pursat city, Pursat province.
Authorities confirmed that a man committed suicide with his son Hong Chamroeun, 35, while his 4-year-old son Chamroeun Panha. After examining the body, the authorities handed it over to the family for a traditional ceremony.
Ending his life with his son, the man also left a handwritten note stating why he decided to think short and apologize to his wife and family.
The letter stated that the end of life was due to the inability to treat kidney damage, which doctors require dialysis 2-3 times a week. Only 61 days left! Cambodia to host 32nd SEA Games
(Pursat): Mr. Khoy Rida, Governor of Pursat Province, and Ms. Ang Socheata Khoy Rida, Honorary President of the Cambodian Women's Association for Peace and Development on March 3, 2023, met with nearly 500 women on the occasion of the celebration. 112nd Anniversary of the International Women's Day, March 8, 2023 under the theme "Together to keep the peace for development in the digital age" organized by the Department of Women's Affairs, Pursat Province.
Khoy Rida said that women are working in all fields such as health, education, education from kindergarten to higher education, working in law, trade, economics, business, agriculture, industry and the armed forces. Testimony shows that Cambodia has achieved complete peace throughout the country due to the win-win policy of Samdech Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia.
He stressed that our people are very difficult to have peace like today. Therefore, we must work together to preserve peace, no matter what the cost, to fight back against the ungodly people who intend to bring our Cambodia back to the flames of war like in the past. Without peace, Cambodia will not be able to develop in all areas.
He added that in 2003, the Royal Government of Cambodia, as well as the Ministry of Women's Affairs, disseminated the theme "Together to Keep the Peace for Development in the Digital Age" on the occasion of the International Day of March 8, in order to highlight the value of women in participating in all activities. Invaluable in maintaining peace as well as actively participating in accelerating development in all areas.
In response to the above theme, the Royal Government of Cambodia promotes and continues to promote the implementation of gender equality policies, recognizing women as the backbone of economic and social development, and gender mainstreaming as a cross-sectoral work to ensure Sustaining peace and accelerating national development in the digital age and building the infrastructure towards achieving the vision of Cambodia as a high-income country by 2050.
Taking that opportunity, he also informed about the work to organize the aesthetics and development in the province to make it more attractive for national and international guests to come and visit more and more, because in the future, the border checkpoint The stone will be installed as an international gateway and O'Som commune will also become an attractive tourist city.
Please note that after the program, souvenirs were distributed as a gift from Mr. Khoy Rida, Governor of Pursat Province and Ms. Aing Socheata Khoy Rida, Honorary President of the Cambodian Women's Association for Peace and Development to the participants at that time.
