Greece completes search operation at train crash site as grief turns to rage
(Athens): Greek rescuers continue to dig for debris at a train crash that killed 57 people before ending their search operation on Saturday. This is according to the publication by the AFP news agency on Saturday, March 4, 2023.
The train crash in central Greece has sparked outrage and protests across the country, as well as a strong focus on the safety standards of its rail system. Larissa train station chief arrested as government puts charges on individuals, but rail unions say it is inevitable due to a lack of security and staffing.
The railway workers' union has been on strike for 24 hours since Wednesday, resuming work on Friday, demanding a clear timeline from the Greek government for the implementation of the safety protocol.
