Phnom Penh Administration Finds 5 Solutions to Reduce Traffic Congestion at Monivong Flyover
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, instructed the technical working group to hold an emergency meeting to find a solution to traffic congestion at the construction site of the Monivong flyover (Kbal Thnal).
In the announcement received by Fresh News this morning, March 4, 2023, the technical team found five solutions to alleviate traffic congestion, including:
* First, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration has instructed the construction company to minimize the fence around the construction site as much as possible to keep the traffic flow large.
* Second: Phnom Penh Municipal Police, Khan Police Inspectorate and relevant authorities must increase their regular police force to help solve traffic congestion when traffic is busy.
* Third: Please call on the people who are using the sidewalks for sale to serve their business to stop using those sidewalks, while the people who shoppers should not stop on the chest. No road and the authorities will organize order by taking administrative action for those who still use the sidewalk to do business
* Fourth: The Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh must study the ferry so that people can travel from Koh Nora to Chroy Changvar (Sokha Residence Hotel, Phnom Penh) in addition to the ferry from Koh Nora to Koh Pich.
* 5th: When the traffic is busy, people who can and know how to use APP GOOGLE MAPS, please use it to help check the traffic congestion at the construction site of Monivong flyover when you see traffic congestion, please people People use other roads if they have a choice. Mr. Hav Rattanak issued a petition in full support for the verdict of Kem Sokha, which provides full justice for the Cambodian people
