On that occasion, Lt. Gen. Lim Tong Huot, Director of the Department of Legislation, Education and Rehabilitation of the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, said that when you use drugs, you become addicted, when you are addicted, you become a slave to drugs, dare to do anything Yang (including crime) to get drugs to use, lose love, lose consciousness, become lonely, mentally ill.
Mr. Sot Kimsan also pointed out that the drug problem is a complex issue, the top international crime that has been spreading around the world and has been invading Cambodia, causing many serious disasters to the people. Especially young men and women, which is the concern of the Royal Government and the people, which requires us all to find measures to prevent and resolve in a timely manner.
At the same time, Mr. Sot Kimsan added that as long as the illegal drug trafficking continues, serious consequences will always be present for our country because it has caused many other crimes. Drugs are a dangerous trap for everyone. If someone falls into the trap of drugs, that person will always have consequences for the perpetrator, family, community and society.
He urged parents or guardians to monitor their children's activities, behavior and education, and if there is any suspicion or knowledge that their children are using drugs, they should cooperate and report to the authorities for preventive measures. In addition, students must stay away from drugs when hanging out with friends, be careful, especially to study hard to become good friends, good students, good children and to be a good vine in the future bamboo.
