Cambodia is preparing the third master plan on occupational safety and health of workers
(Phnom Penh): The relevant components of the tripartite have been preparing the third master plan on occupational safety and health 2023-2027 (OSH) to help workers and employers to understand and adapt to emerging risks and improve Occupational safety and health of workers.
In the afternoon of March 3, 2023, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training organized a tripartite workshop to review and decide on the third master plan on occupational safety and health 2023-2027. Cut OSH at Phnom Penh Hotel.
Mr. Chap Rithy, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, said that the main purpose of this workshop was to verify the detailed activities of the leadership and cooperation institutions, budget estimates and output indicators, which are the draft results of the previous workshop. Validate and finalize the third master plan on OSH.
Mr. Chap Rithy stated that occupational safety and health is an important issue in all workplaces, which the Royal Government of Cambodia, especially the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, which is a staff that pays close attention and is included as a core work standard. Of the International Labor Organization.
Mr. Leng Tong, Advisor to the Ministry and Director of the Department of Labor Medicine of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, said that the workshop was attended by a total of 50 participants from state institutions, employers and employees (both local and informal economy). And organizations.
Haruhiro Jono, Representative of the International Labor Organization, praised the process of developing the third master plan, which was interactive, with clear social dialogue from all stakeholders and input. The International Labor Organization also continues to support and implement the implementation of the third master plan. Celebrating International Women's Day, Mr. Kong Vibol made 4 recommendations to promote women in the tax unit
The Minister highly valued all women and praised the ability of the current female tax officers, who are highly capable and especially praised Ms. Kean Ramy, Head of Meanchey District Tax Branch as the Head of Tax Unit. One of the General Department of Taxation, who did her job well as a leader and advised all tax women to follow her example.
On the occasion of the International Women's Day, the Minister accompanied by the Prime Minister outlined the key recommendations aimed at promoting women, including:
1. All units under the General Department of Taxation, especially the Department of Finance and Personnel and the Human Resource Reform Commission, shall examine the possibility of selecting at least one capable and qualified woman to be promoted to the position of Deputy Head of the Department or Branch Deputy. Per unit, especially to increase the position of branch manager to at least 1 person in 2023
2-Give priority to 3 women to become the head of the tax branch 3-Advise all units to pay attention to women who work in the voluntary framework to get a decent salary and uniform and To be named as a contract employee of the General Department of Taxation for other rights and benefits
4: Instruct the Department of Finance and staff to coordinate and change the provincial branch where the contracted woman is working in accordance with the place of residence of her family to facilitate their living as needed.
At the same time, the Minister accompanying the Prime Minister provided respectful guidance for all women to be strong and strive to achieve their goals in life by striving to develop themselves in both knowledge and leadership and In particular, be an initiative person and work hard and proactively to seize the opportunity to become a leader in a organization full of ability and confidence.
The Deputy Prime Minister highly appreciated and thanked all the members who participated in the celebration of the 112th International Women's Day and instructed all male leaders and officials to respect and value. To women.
