Cambodia has plans to build 9 car assembly plants while 3 companies are in the process of assembling cars to supply the domestic market.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Soeun Dara, Executive Director of the Automotive Industry Federation of Cambodia (CAIF), on March 3, 2023, stated that so far, Cambodia has a total of 9 new car assembly plant projects, including 3 companies. Running businesses to supply the local market and six other companies are building factories.
He said that the increase in the number of new car assembly plants in Cambodia due to the good economic growth of Cambodia and the increase in the use of new cars also increased and encouraged investors. In Cambodia from the Royal Government.
He said that Cambodia's economic situation and political stability have improved, making Cambodia a potential country in the ASEAN region, and Cambodia has many opportunities for investors to invest in the automotive sector.
In fact, a decade ago, the volume of new car use was only about 10 percent, but for 2022, it will increase by about 40 percent, and used cars will fall from 90 percent to about 60 percent.
He also said that the installation of new car factories in Cambodia helps increase people's income by creating jobs and replacing the import of completely new cars from abroad and contributing to the national economy with various tax revenues. In addition, it has also increased the capacity of local people to become more skilled.
He added that it also helps to improve the price of new cars and make consumers able to buy new cars, because compared to the whole import, the car is installed locally, the price is better than the whole imported car. Due to receiving a lot of tax incentives from the Royal Government.
