Cambodian Red Cross Conversation with Australian Government Scholarship Winners
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Pum Chantyny, Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross, and her colleagues met with a group of 11 2023 Australian Government Scholarship winners at the Cambodian Red Cross Headquarters on March 2, 2023.
The Secretary General sent a message of greetings from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross to all participating students.
In response, Ms. Heng Vongdalis, Representative of the 2023 Australian Government Scholarship Candidate, expressed her pleasure and deep gratitude for the remarks made by His Excellency Dr. Bun Rany Hun Sen and the Secretary-General. Let the students meet politely now.
Ms. Heng Vongdalis continued that the Royal Government of Australia has been providing scholarships to Cambodian students for 28 years. In fact, in 2023, a total of 45 successful candidates were selected and divided into two groups. The first group of 30 people left to study in Australia in early January 2023, and the second group of 15 people are scheduled to leave to study in June 2023.
The students also thanked the Secretary-General for their experience and good humanitarian activities, which provided the students with a wealth of knowledge and understanding of the humanitarian activities, the statutory rules, the correct financial regulations and There is a 10-year strategy to work to help the most vulnerable and vulnerable people.
Especially under the leadership of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen is to develop institutions in decentralization and financial deconcentration so that the 25 branches of the Red Cross are strong and able to alleviate the difficulties of the people in time.
