* First Alaskan Discovery:
* Alaska from the colony of the Russian Empire to the 49th state of the United States:
After the end of the civil war, talks between the United States and Russia on the sale of Alaska territory resumed, but seemed slow. It was not until April 1867 that the Senate ratified the Alaska Treaty by a single vote.
Why Russia decided to sell Alaska to the United States:
At the time, most Russians probably did not realize that "Alaska is a peninsula of gold and rich in oil resources under the sea." Decided to sell it to the United States like that.
After being bought from the Russian Empire, Alaska was like a street child adopted by a rich man and hated by the landlord's descendants because so few Americans lived far from their homeland. The United States is also very cold, not conducive to longevity, and the government is not yet fully classified as any other state.
* Alaska State and Tourism Potential:
With growing to become the world's number one economic and arms power, Alaska has emerged as one of the most attractive ecotourism destinations as the 49th state is full of natural landscapes such as natural lakes, beaches, and the Midnight of Sun River. Rivers, mountains, ice, wildlife and many other tourist sites.
