The conviction of Kem Sokha has led to a lot of support from leaders in various ministries, institutions, both civilian and the armed forces, as well as the people of Cambodia. Capacity as the government takes seriously the role of women in society
(Phnom Penh): General Soeng Samnang, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Air Force, urged all units under his command to examine the capabilities and request of female soldiers to provide roles according to their abilities and needs. Necessity of the framework as the Royal Government pays close attention to the role of women in various ministries and institutions.
General Soeng Samnang's call was made on the occasion of presiding over the celebration of the 112nd International Women's Day on March 8 under the theme "Women Together for Peace for Development in the Digital Age" on the 3rd This March 2023, at the Phnom Penh Air Force Command.
General Soeng Samnang said that in the sixth mandate, in accordance with the gender strategy in both civil society and the armed forces, the Royal Government has given high priority to enhancing the role of social status of Cambodian women, including encouragement. For women to increase their knowledge capacity in all areas.
The commander of the Air Force added, "All units must monitor and evaluate the actual work, discipline and morality of female soldiers in each unit to provide opportunities for women to get the rank, role appropriate to the capabilities and needs of the framework. Work.
At the same time, the General continued that at the Air Force Command, we must continue to pay attention to the promotion of women soldiers by providing opportunities for learning and participation in all activities so that women can develop their digital skills to fulfill Roles, duties, better professionalism.
General Soeng Samnang emphasized: "Currently, women are highly valued by Cambodian society, as women have played a role in serving the interests of society in all areas, such as: politics, military, economy, the judiciary and become Lead in many other areas.
According to female soldiers serving in the Air Force Command, they are taken care of by the command and are encouraged, especially when women give birth. Donations and financial support, etc., and for the assignment of the role is the command to check the duration of work or according to actual capacity.
At the same time, the female soldiers in the Cambodian Air Force Command emphasized that the women in the army units were sent by the unit leaders to send to the training to increase their capacity, especially in the technical skills that were previously rich. Soldiers are men. In addition, female soldiers have many opportunities to participate in many activities within the framework of military units and other social work.
It should be noted that at the Air Force Command, there are nearly 200 female soldiers with ranks ranging from brigadier general to major.
