Phnom Penh Capital Administration rejects fabricated information about the closure of Chbar Ampov Bridge to prevent traffic shared on social media (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Phnom Penh Capital Administration on the afternoon of March 3, 2023 came out to reject the fabricated information that the authorities decided to close Traffic on the Monivong Bridge (Chbar Ampov Bridge) is closed to traffic and diverts people to cross the river by boat.
Met Meas Pheakdey, spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Administration, told Fresh News that the information shared in connection with the traffic closure on the Chbar Ampov bridge was false information created by unscrupulous individuals with the intention of polluting society.
A spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Administration stated, "The Phnom Penh Municipal Administration would like to completely reject the fabricated information that the authorities have decided to close the Monivong Bridge or the Chbar Ampov Bridge to prevent people from passing through due to heavy traffic congestion." This is not true, the Chbar Ampov bridge is still open for people to travel normally.
At this time, the competent authorities are searching for the owner of the Facebook page who posted this fake information to come in and explain the false information. Battambang Provincial Governor Fully Supports the Verdict of Kem Sokha, Providing Full Justice for the Cambodian People
