Demand for clean water in Phnom Penh will increase to nearly 2 million cubic meters per day (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Master Plan for Water Supply Phase 3 in Phnom Penh, an important tool in determining the water production plan To supply the people in Phnom Penh has been updated again, predicting that by 2030, the demand for clean water in Phnom Penh will increase to 1.8 million cubic meters per day.
Speaking at a seminar to disseminate the third phase of water supply master plan in Phnom Penh from 2021 to 2030, Dr. Cham Prasidh, Senior Minister, Minister of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation, said that the update of water supply master plan is due to expansion. Of the city too quickly beyond expectations, hence the demand for clean water increased significantly.
He said that the demand for clean water is projected to increase to 1.8 million cubic meters per day and the number of customers will increase to 660,000 customers by 2030, which is the result of a combination of major sectors. 4 in Phnom Penh, in Takhmao City, the new international airport area and parts of Khsach Kandal and Lvea Em districts.
At the same time, the budget for investment is projected to be about 1,200 million to 1,400 million US dollars between 2026 and 2031, of which the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority's contribution is about 14 million US dollars for the construction of water treatment plants. 10 with a production capacity of 850,000 cubic meters per day, for the supply and installation of water distribution pipes and technical consulting services.
The third phase water supply master plan (2021 to 2030) was prepared and studied by the Japanese Technical Advisor. The third phase of the master plan update cost about $ 1 million, with the study starting in December 2018 and ending in February 2022.
