Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon: Today, Cambodia has 38.65% female diplomats
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, at the celebration of the 112th Anniversary of International Women's Day on March 8, 2023, stated that Cambodia currently has 38.65% female diplomats. Of total officers.
In order to contribute to the Royal Government in promoting gender equality, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation has always paid attention to encouraging as well as giving equal value to men in accordance with their abilities, seniority and qualifications, both in terms of roles and responsibilities. Positions, including assignments to work abroad.
Mr. Prak Sokhon stated, "So far, we have 288 female diplomats, equivalent to 38.65% of the total 745 officers. "This figure is an indicator of the ministry's efforts and commitment to promoting gender equality."
Minister Mam Bunheng: More than 50% of women working in the health sector show that women really play an important role in contributing to the health sector and the nation.
(Phnom Penh): Professor Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, said that up to now, more than 50% of women who have worked in the health sector, which shows the ability to contribute to the promotion of health, especially maternal health. Infants and children.
This statement was made by Professor Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, at the celebration of the 112nd Anniversary of the International Women's Day on March 8, 2023 under the theme "Women Together for Peace for Development in the Digital Age" at Friendship Hospital Khmer-Soviet on March 3, 2023.
Professor Mam Bunheng said that the celebration of the 112nd International Women's Day on March 8 today is an encouragement to women in the unit and women in the health sector.
In addition, women's health is the work of the family, which requires the attention of the family, because if the woman is healthy, good reproductive health while the husband is healthy, then the children will be healthy, which is the vine Strong bamboo heirloom for the nation.
On the other hand, in implementing the policy of gender equality, the Ministry of Health pays close attention to women's work by giving priority to women who are able to get a suitable position in their work and Provided the opportunity to participate in training courses to continue various skills in and outside the country.
In providing health services, the Ministry has focused its utmost attention on health care for women of childbearing age, and especially mothers, in order to reduce maternal and infant mortality. In fact, according to figures from the Preliminary Health and Demographic Survey in Cambodia, the rate of examination and care of women during pregnancy and childbirth has increased, while the mortality rate of mothers, infants and children has decreased significantly.
The Royal Government of Cambodia, under the wise and wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, has paid special attention to the health of mothers, infants and children by issuing a sub-decree setting February 21 as National Mother, Baby and Child Health Day as well.
