(Phnom Penh): The Criminal Police Department of the National Police General Commission arrested a man and sent him to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on March 2, 2023 in connection with a case of embezzling more than 60,000 dollars by order of the Prosecutor's Office. First, Phnom Penh.
In the arrest warrant issued by Mr. Chreung Khmao, the Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court stated that 31-year-old Hour Tai Chan, a resident of Banlea Set village, Khmuonh commune, Sen Sok district, Phnom Penh, was involved in the case of "non-compliance with the equipment The queue came out tomorrow according to the complaint of Peng Chea Daphurat, 31 years old.
After the arrest, Hour Tai Chan was sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for further proceedings.
According to the press release, after holding 66 debate hearings from January 15, 2020 to December 21, 2022, the Trial Chamber of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court announced its criminal verdict in March 3, 2023, with the following decisions:
Defendant Kem Sokha, male, born on June 27, 1953, Khmer nationality, was sentenced to 27 (twenty-seven) years imprisonment for conspiracy with a foreigner or conspiracy with a foreigner in Cambodia; Other places from 2010 to September 3, 2017 are criminal offenses and shall be punished in accordance with the provisions of Article 439 and Article 443 of the Penal Code.
2. Convict the accused with additional sentences by permanently revoking the right to vote, the right to stand for election and the right to engage in other political activities in accordance with the provisions of Article 450 of the Penal Code.
3. Place the accused under judicial supervision by respecting the following obligations:
* Do not leave the premises of the house No. 97, Street 313, Village 7, Sangkat Boeung Kak II, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh, unless authorized by the Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
* Do not meet any person, both Khmer or foreign, directly or indirectly through technology other than family members, except with the permission of the Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, according to the necessary requirements.
The obligations of the above judicial review measures are effective immediately from the date of the announcement of the verdict until the final verdict.
4. To order the forces of the General Commission of the National Police to exercise their powers and roles as judicial police officers to ensure the implementation of judicial review measures as set out in point 3 of the above decision under the guidance and Coordinated by the Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
5. In case of violation of the obligations of the judicial review measures, the representative of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court must immediately request the competent court to issue the provisional detention measures on the accused.
