(Phnom Penh): Phnom Penh Capital Administration Holds a Health Education Awareness Workshop on Understanding the Benefits of 11 Immunizations for Children to Celebrate the 112th Anniversary of International Women's Day on March 8 Peace for Development in the Digital Age.
The workshop was organized by the Advisory Committee on Women and Children's Affairs of Phnom Penh in collaboration with the Department of Health and the Department of Women's Affairs this morning, March 3, 2023.
Mr. Mop Sarin, President of the Phnom Penh Capital Council, stated that this topic is important in response to the current context in order to continue to highlight the invaluable value of women's participation in maintaining peace, as well as being actively involved in Accelerate development in all fields.
He said that in partnership, Cambodians, both men and women, will participate equally and equally with the people of countries in the region and the world, especially in the digital age and in the post-crisis socio-economic recovery agenda. Kovid 19 as well as building resilience and sustainable development.
In relation to the International Women's Day on March 8, Mr. Mop Sarin said that women have fought successfully to achieve the recognition of women's rights and set out the International Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination against Women (CEDAW), which the General Assembly The United Nations declared the United Nations Day on Women's Rights and World Peace on December 18, 1979.
Cambodia became a signatory to the Convention on November 14, 1992. From now on, Cambodian women are recognized by society, women have equal rights before the law and are protected by law, women have the right to education, the right to work and equal pay for men.
