(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, on the morning of March 3, 2023, led a team of relevant officials to inspect the construction process of a bridge in Ko He Village, Prek Koy Commune, Kang Meas District.
Kampong Cham provincial administration official said that the bridge under construction in the above location is a concrete bridge across the canal, 108 meters long and 10 meters wide, donated by the Royal Government will be completed in early 2024. .
Officials said that the bridge across the canal is very useful for people to cross, especially people in the area can cross or transport agricultural products from one area to another.
Due to the geography at this point, there is a road connected with Cheung Prey district, Batheay district and from Reay Pai commune, Kang Mea district, across this bridge to Kandal province or to Phnom Penh. Therefore, at the geographical point, the bridge under construction can still become a town that provides great benefits to people can create jobs and improve their families' livelihoods as well.
