The World Obesity Federation estimates that 51 percent of the world's population, or more than 4 billion people, will be obese or overweight in the next 12 years.
The report found that obesity rates are rising rapidly, especially among children and in low-income countries.
"It is particularly worrying to see the highest rates of obesity among children and adolescents," she said in a statement.
The report found that childhood obesity could double from 2020 levels by 2020, with 2.6 billion people falling into the disease, or 38 percent of the world's population.
The report also found that almost all countries expected to see the highest rates of obesity increase in the coming years are low- and middle-income countries in Asia and Africa.
