(Phnom Penh): The multi-purpose port and logistics center located in Phnom Tepi area in Keng Ta Sok village, Kampong Hav commune, Kampong Leng district are speeding up the construction and may be used for transportation in the near future.
Establishment of this port and logistics center in order to promote the transportation of land and waterways in the country, as well as transport and export of agricultural products from Kampong Chhnang, Pursat, Battambang, Banteay Meanchey, Siem Reap and Kampong Thom. . The construction of the port and logistics center also provided employment to a large number of people living in Kampong Chhnang province.
After listening to the report of the technical working group, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol instructed all stakeholders to support and promote the development of the multi-purpose port and logistics center in Kampong Chhnang in accordance with legal standards and urge the project to run quickly to National economic interests as well.
The Senior Minister expressed full support for the establishment of this port because it will make transportation in Cambodia more diverse in accordance with the policy of the Royal Government.
Please be informed that KLPT Transport Co., Ltd. is a company that has received permission from the Head of the Royal Government to build a multi-purpose port, a logistics center on a 100-hectare land in Phnom Tepi area, Keng Ta Sok village, Kampong Hav commune, Kampong Leng district. The port will be completed and put into operation to transport products to the market in early April 2023.
