Tobacco and e-cigarettes will not be allowed to be sponsored, distributed or advertised in the SEA Games and the ASEAN Para Games in Cambodia.
This was confirmed by Mr. Hor Sarun, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism and Vice Chairman of the Opening and Closing Ceremony Committee of the National Organizing Committee of the 32nd Southeast Asian Games and the 12th ASEAN Para Games on the afternoon of March 2, 2023. At a press conference on "tobacco-free sports" held at the Ministry of Tourism.
The conference was also attended by Dr. Mom Kong, Executive Director of the Cambodian Movement for Health, Dr. Yil Daravuth, Representative of the World Health Organization.
Mr. Hor Sarun said that in the past, the Ministry of Tourism has also set a number of policies to ban the use, sale, distribution and advertising of tobacco products and e-cigarettes in the National Stadium, sports stadiums and accommodation areas. Eating of sports delegates and accommodation Eating of sports delegates without the support of tobacco companies and e-cigarette companies (Web).
It should be noted that recently, the National Organizing Committee of the 32nd Southeast Asian Games 2023 also issued guidelines on the implementation of the principle of "sport without tobacco" in the 2nd Southeast Asian Games. 32 and the 12th ASEAN Para Games 2023 with instructions such as:
1. Prohibit the use of tobacco products, electronic cigarettes and HTP products (HTPs) in the National Stadium, sports field and dining area of the sports delegation.
2. Prohibit the sale, distribution and advertisement of tobacco products, e-cigarettes and all forms of HTP products (HTP) in the National Stadium, sports field and dining area of the sports delegation.
3. Not to be sponsored by tobacco companies, e-cigarette companies and HTP products (HTPs) in any form or purpose for the competition as well as the media.
4: Include no smoking and e-cigarette signs in promotional materials for the 32nd Southeast Asian Games and the 12th ASEAN Para Games 2023.
5. To promote "sports without tobacco" widely to sports delegates, stakeholders in organizing volunteers and the general public through training, notifications and social media. The Ministry of Public Works and the French Agency for Development (AFD) meet to discuss opportunities for future cooperation
