General knowledge: Why does Mongolia have no sea borders but a navy?
(Phnom Penh): There are many countries that have no borders by the ocean, but still keep the navy, it seems strange. After all, when we know that in addition to the oceans, other waters, such as the closed seas, lakes, and rivers, can also be used to create borders between countries, this kind of thing seems strange.
In general, all of the above countries have good reasons for protecting the waterways in their country, but the reason for having Mongolia's navy is not like that. Mongolia is very far from the ocean, and by size it is the second largest country without borders, just under Kazakhstan.
By the end of the 13th century, the Mongol Empire had disintegrated into several independent states, and eventually, through Chinese aggression, the Mongols were pushed further and further from the coast to the border. Next to the ocean as it is today.
During the Soviet era, the Sukabatar trawler was regularly used for the transfer of oil between the south and north of the lake, later it was no longer used for this purpose, and the Mongolian navy Has lost its goal.
