Remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Opportunity to Meet Nearly 4,000 Artists to Celebrate National Cultural Day on March 3
(Phnom Penh): On Thursday evening, March 2, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, met with 4,000 young and old artists from all walks of life at the International Convention and Exhibition Center. Diamond Island.
The social gathering and solidarity meal between Samdech Techo Prime Minister and the artist has been missed for about 3 years due to the outbreak of Kovid 19 disease. This solidarity meeting and dinner was held not only to strengthen the unity between Cambodian artists, but also to celebrate the National Cultural Day on March 3.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen delivered a speech for nearly an hour, the following are the main contents of Samdech Techo:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he was very happy to meet about 4,000 artists on the National Cultural Day on March 3.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that today's gathering is a valuable meeting to strengthen the closeness between the head of government and artists and to promote cultural values.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the National Cultural Day is an important day of the Cambodian people to commemorate the merits of all generations of Cambodian ancestors who sacrificed their physical, mental, intellectual and life to create, maintain and protect. The rich and priceless cultural treasures are passed on to future generations.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that based on this spirit, since 1999, the Royal Government has always celebrated the National Cultural Day.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in the national process, the youth have played an important role in liberating, restoring and developing the nation to be as prosperous as it is now.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen advised to pay special attention to Khmer literature after many misuse.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructs artists to compose songs to celebrate the SEA Games.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen advised to pay attention to the construction of statues or other statues to be built according to the style.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he was most afraid of the loss of Khmer cultural heritage due to the growth of modern technology.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen proposes to stop claiming ownership of cultural heritage between countries with similar cultures. Samdech Techo Hun Sen wants dialogue between countries with similar cultural heritage to end disputes and claim ownership of those cultural heritage properties.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen wants countries with similar cultural heritage to propose similar cultural properties as World Heritage properties.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expects that the leaders of Thailand and Laos, who have similar cultural heritage to Cambodia, can consider Samdech's initiative.
