Mr. Vongsey Visoth: Cambodia needs to attract more quality investment
The WB forecasts that global economic growth will slow from 2.9% in 2022 to 1.7% in 2023, largely due to tightening monetary policy in response to the rise. Of particular inflation in developed countries and the impact of the Russia-Ukraine war on energy supplies and prices.
Meanwhile, global trade growth is projected to be in line with global economic trends, slowing to 2.5% in 2023 from 4.3% in 2022. However, the US Federal Reserve's softer rate hike than last year, as well as China's recent rapid and full opening of the country, could have some positive consequences for the global economy, the region, including Cambodia. Tourism for the year 2023 and the years to come.
Mr. Vongsey Visoth also said that as a vision for the medium and long term, Cambodia needs to attract quality investment to increase skills, increase decent wages, standard work, good value for money. High and promote economic diversification as well as green investment. Of course, we have done a lot in the past, such as the implementation of new investment laws.
