(Phnom Penh): On Thursday evening, March 2, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will hold a get-together with 4,000 artists from all walks of life at the International Convention and Exhibition Center. Diamond Island.
The social gathering and solidarity meal between Samdech Techo Prime Minister and the artist has been missed for about 3 years due to the outbreak of Kovid 19 disease. This solidarity meeting and dinner was held not only to strengthen the unity between Cambodian artists, but also to celebrate the National Cultural Day on March 3.
This meeting is an opportunity for Samdech Techo Prime Minister to provide recommendations as well as advice to contribute to the promotion of Cambodian cultural values that are of great value.
National Cultural Day is an important day of the Cambodian people to commemorate the merits of all generations of Cambodian ancestors who sacrificed their physical, mental, intellectual and life to create, maintain and protect rich and valuable cultural heritage. Invaluable, passed on to future generations.
At the same time, the National Cultural Day is a valuable opportunity to inspire patriotism, culture, traditions and national identity among all Cambodians in order to ensure sustainable development and environment in line with policy. National on Culture and Political Programs of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
The celebration of "National Cultural Day" with the theme "Youth for National Culture" aims to encourage Cambodians, both inside and outside the country, especially young people who take turns to participate in activities to preserve, promote and develop national culture, such as:
Encourage the responsible participation of young people in the preservation and development of national culture, regardless of political affiliation, religion or color.
* Promote the consciousness and spirit of participation and transfer of knowledge, skills and techniques, arts and culture to promote the preservation and development of national culture as well as multiculturalism of indigenous communities in Cambodia to be stable.
* Increase awareness of the true value of national culture and the richness of cultural heritage as an inexhaustible source of job creation and income-generating opportunities to contribute to socio-economic development through increased services and cultural products for commercial purposes. And Tourism
* Encourage all people, especially young people, to strive to create and increase new cultural works to be more creative on the basis of national identity in order to promote the use of cultural potential to contribute to national economic development and reduce poverty.
Please note that on the National Cultural Day on March 3, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia also issued a circular on the organization of this day.
In order for the celebration of the 25th National Cultural Day on March 3, 2023 to run smoothly, Samdech Techo introduced the following 11 points:
1. The time for celebrating the 25th National Cultural Day on March 3 is set for two weeks (one week before and one week after March 3, 2023). Therefore, all ministries, institutions and stakeholders must examine the possibility of organizing programs and activities to celebrate the 25th National Cultural Day on March 3, both in person and / or on social media at any convenient time within the specified time. This.
3: The Ministry of Information shall organize broadcast programs to celebrate the National Cultural Day on March 3 widely in the national and private media, including: radio, television, newspapers, magazines and related documents to inspire the public to understand and participate more actively in Preservation and promotion of national culture, morality, society and social harmony without discrimination on the basis of political, religious or racial discrimination.
4. The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts must cooperate in disseminating the national culture and the content of the National Cultural Day to students in all public and private educational institutions.
5. The Ministry of Tourism shall promote the national culture and the content of the National Cultural Day to national and international tourists through travel agencies, tour operators, resorts, hotels, guesthouses and restaurants of all kinds.
6: The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation shall instruct all embassies, consulates, honorary consulates of the Kingdom of Cambodia abroad and the Cambodian community abroad to participate in organizing programs and activities to celebrate the National Cultural Day on March 3. Live location on social media and / or by any means available.
7. The Ministry of Cults and Religions must inspire the movement of monks and all believers to organize programs and activities to promote the national culture and the content of the National Cultural Day on March 3 in temples, religious centers, Vipassana centers and other shrines.
8. The Ministry of Interior and the Ministry of National Defense must have a plan to guide the grassroots to maintain security and public order on the occasion of the 25th National Cultural Day on March 3 to be effective and responsible.
10. All ministries, institutions, local administrations, schools, factories, enterprises, homes and Cambodian communities abroad must participate in celebrating and celebrating the National Cultural Day on March 3 by various means, such as raising flags, flags, banners, slogans, paintings, cultural arts and / or Appropriate activities at its location as well as on social media.
11. Participants in programs and promotional activities related to the National Cultural Day on March 3 must dress in the national tradition.
