(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Municipal Court will announce the verdict in the case of Kem Sokha's peace with foreigners on March 3, 2023, after the investigation and the hearing in accordance with legal procedures. What are the possible scenarios surrounding the case of Kem Sokha's treason Chak Chao Smok, try to think of some scenarios that may occur to consider:
In total, the trial of Kem Sokha's treason case has been held 66 times, including the last hearing on December 22, 2022. This last hearing is an important one in which all parties to the case, including civil party lawyers, defendants 'lawyers and prosecutors' representatives, are legally entitled to conclude their respective conclusions. .
The hearing in the case of Kem Sokha's treason was considered by lawyers and observers to be conducted in accordance with Cambodian legal procedures and in a transparent manner, as the trial was held in public and was represented by journalists, A number of civil society organizations, as well as a number of foreign diplomats, were also allowed to attend the trial on a regular basis.
These two scenarios are as follows:
From a legal point of view, in this scenario, the court can sentence Kem Sokha to three options as follows: Option 1: According to Article 443 of the Penal Code, the court can sentence Kem Sokha to 15 to 30 years in prison. Legally, because the crime lasted more than five years, the court could not decide on a suspended sentence for such a sentence.
The action on the case related to national security is also seen by analysts as law enforcement, which is an internal affair of Cambodia, aimed at strengthening national independence and sovereignty against foreign interference in Cambodia's internal affairs. . Moreover, the court's decision in this case does not affect the legal status of any foreign state because:
(1) The foreign state is not the subject of the charges in this case; and (2) the Royal Government's lawyer requested that the court not use the name of the foreign state in the court's verdict to ensure protection. National interests and good relations between foreign states and Cambodia as well.
