Ministry of Environment and partner organizations hold a press conference to launch the "Zero Trap in Cambodia Protected Areas" campaign, the second phase in 6 provinces of the Cardamom Mountains
(Phnom Penh): In order to participate in the protection and conservation of natural resources in Cambodia, the Ministry of Environment, in collaboration with partner organizations, on March 2, 2023, organized a press conference to launch the campaign "Zero Trap in the region." Protecting Cambodia's Nature "Phase 2 in six provinces of the Cardamom Mountains.
The second phase of the Zero Trap Campaign, which will run for five months from March 3 to July 2023, will be implemented in five provinces: Kampong Speu, Pursat, Koh Kong, Battambang, Pailin and Siem Reap.
Through the implementation of this campaign, all stakeholders and partners are willing to work together on the basis of finding common solutions to emerging challenges and threats to wildlife and natural resources in order to achieve their goals. The common denominator is to eliminate the use of all kinds of traps in Cambodia's protected areas and to stop the wildlife trade, which is prohibited by law.
The "Zero Trap Campaign in Cambodia Protected Areas" is consistently implemented with the organization of activities and the use of mixed media to disseminate information to stakeholders and the general public, especially people living near and around protected areas. Consequences of trapping and hunting of wildlife to both Cambodia's precious human and wildlife resources.
The campaign also raised public awareness, in particular to educate wildlife eaters and wildlife traders about the risks to personal and public health that may arise from the consumption and trafficking of animals. These forests to promote change of attitude and encourage participation in wildlife conservation and conservation of Cambodia's natural resources.
