Good news! A newborn baby dolphin was found in Anlong Kampi
According to the experts, the new baby dolphin was born on February 27 or 28, 2023, weighs 9 to 10 kilograms, is 1 meter long and is healthy. The birth of a new baby dolphin coincides with the receipt of a new sub-decree No. 47 dated 27 February 2023 on the establishment of the Mekong River Dolphin Management Area, approved by the head of the Royal Government, Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
The acquisition of this new dolphin is a joint protection effort between relevant institutions and units at both the national and sub-national levels under the full support of the Royal Government of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
For the work ahead, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries will continue to strengthen patrols, educate, promote and change the occupation of fishermen engaged in fishing with nets or fishing rods in the dolphin area to live a new business, because both types of fishing gear have caused Dolphins die one after another.
It should be informed that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on February 27, 2023, issued a sub-decree on the delimitation of Mekong River dolphin management areas in Stung Treng and Kratie provinces.
The designation of the Mekong River Dolphin Management Area is to protect and conserve dolphins, a sacred natural treasure, to effectively participate in the development of ecotourism, improve the economy, society and livelihood of the people, and maintain the balance of the natural environment. For the growth of biodiversity and sustain life of dolphins. Summary of important news events for March 01, 2023
