(Phnom Penh) - General Dr. Mao Hovannal, Minister in charge of the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation, met with a delegation from the Lao Civil Aviation Authority on March 1, 2023 to strengthen civil aviation cooperation between the two countries.
Speaking to Fresh News, Mr. Sin Chanserivutha, Undersecretary of State and Spokesperson for Civil Aviation, said that the purpose of the Lao Civil Aviation Authority delegation to visit to learn about the development and growth of civil aviation in Cambodia.
In addition, the Lao Civil Aviation Authority would like to get some good guidance and experience from Cambodia to implement in Laos, especially good governance and management and control of the civil aviation system.
"Laos wants to understand Cambodia on governance management and work with the private sector on the recent airport development, such as: Siem Reap Airport, Phnom Penh Airport and other airports in a public-private partnership," he said.
Mr. Sin Chanserivutha said that the Cambodian civil aviation sector is also growing in terms of traffic, air traffic control and private companies as a business, so the Lao side wants to find out about Cambodia because Lao civil aviation does not have a private sector to participate. To develop yet.
On that occasion, Cambodia-Laos Civil Aviation also signed an MOU to increase flights between Laos and Cambodia in order to reconnect Laos-Cambodia flights and increase the number of flights.
