The head of the Cambodian diplomatic corps said this at the opening ceremony of the meeting to review the results of 2022 and 2023 goals of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation on March 1, 2023.
According to the Deputy Prime Minister, due to high and stable economic growth for decades in a row, China has caught up with the United States in almost every area. He said China's economic influence in many parts of the world is wide and growing. China is the most important economic and trade partner for almost every country in Asia.
"In a context where the war in Ukraine continues to evolve more complex and dangerous, China's role and decision will be of paramount importance for the future of this war and the future of world order," Prak Sokhon said.
Russia, a friend of Russia, is having a major influence on the Russia-Ukraine war. The United States and the West have warned China not to provide aid to Russia as Chinese diplomats visit Russia, which is believed to be expected to include Chinese President Xi Jinping's upcoming visit to Russia. Well.
Dr. Yong Pov, Secretary General of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that in the war in Ukraine, China has a role to play in mediating and resolving this crisis, as well as participating in the management of world order. This war does not need for either side to win, but for all to win, and only if China acts as an arbitrator can the war be ended.
The world needs a multipolar order for the world order not to be led by the United States alone, it is based on the multipolar, in which China also plays an important role. According to political science experts.
According to Prak Sokhon, in the last five years, the world has continued to evolve into an international system that is global, multi-polar and complex. This development has brought about rapid, difficult, unpredictable and dangerous changes in international relations, both for the Asia-Pacific region and for the world.
Mr. Prak Sokhon said that the eyes of the existing or dangerous tensions continue to cause the international community to worry and spend a lot of time and resources, while crises and wars in some areas lead to the shaking of the global system based on International law seriously affects the peace, security, stability of those areas or beyond.
Prak Sokhon noted that since becoming the world's second largest economy in 2013, China has become more confident in its capabilities, power and influence in regional and global affairs. China declares its firm commitment to building a "modern socialist superpower in all areas" with Chinese characteristics that "no one can stop."
National Cultural Day organized to promote Khmer heritage
(Phnom Penh): The 25th National Cultural Day will be held on March 2, 2023 tomorrow in Koh Pich with the participation of about 4,000 artists under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun. Rany Hun Sen.
Long Pon Siriwat, secretary of state and spokesman for the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, said the 25th National Cultural Day would be held to promote Cambodian heritage throughout the country. "The important message that the ministry sends to all stakeholders, including the private and public sectors, is to promote cultural activities," he said.
A senior official of the Ministry of Culture added that, in fact, the National Cultural Day was set for March 3, 2023, but because this year does not affect the time of artists, Samdech Techo Hun Sen decided to do it one day earlier.
Please be informed that March 3 is a day to commemorate the merits of Cambodian ancestors of all generations who sacrificed their physical, mental, intellectual and spiritual life to create, maintain and protect the rich and valuable cultural heritage for future generations. In 2023, the National Culture Day will be held for the 25th time under the same theme as "Youth for National Culture".
The President of the Khmer Artists Association, Mrs. John Chanleakena, told Fresh News that every year, the Association of Khmer Artists, which has about 700 members, is always invited to celebrate the National Cultural Day, except during the Kovid 19, which is not organized.
She confirmed that the association is now preparing cards for members as well as ready to participate in the 25th National Cultural Day, which will be held on March 2 tomorrow.
March 3 is a day to remember the merits of Cambodian ancestors of all generations who sacrificed their physical and mental strength, wisdom, spirit and life to create, maintain and protect the rich and valuable cultural heritage for future generations.
Pursuant to the spirit of Sub-Decree No. 6, dated January 24, 2006 on the establishment of the National Cultural Day and in line with the slogan "Cambodia: Kingdom of Culture", the Royal Government of Cambodia has set March 3 every year. For the celebration of "National Cultural Day" of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The Ministry of Culture expects the younger generation to gain more knowledge about Cambodian culture when relevant authorities and the private sector set up their own cultural events or through social media to entice them to become cultural lovers. The Royal Academy of Cambodia organizes a roundtable discussion on the "importance of vocational training" to reflect the potential of vocational training for young people
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Academy of Cambodia on March 1, 2023 organized a roundtable discussion on "Importance of Vocational Training" to reflect the potential of vocational training for young people in Cambodia.
The discussion was chaired by Dr. Sok Tout, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia and was attended by guest speakers from relevant ministries and institutions and students.
Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that, of course, vocational training plays a very important role. And working on this is not just a ministry or an institution.
Around this point, Dr. Sok Touch said that for abroad, this vocational training is provided to students since school, and vocational skills must be cultivated in the field of education to provide a strong foundation for young people.
The President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia stated that vocational training is not able to take older people to train, it is necessary to integrate this profession to children and young people to love their favorite skills.
Dr. Yong Pov, Secretary General of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that this vocational training has been around since the war, and that vocational training is the most important part of sustaining the economy. The more developed the economy and society, the more professional skills play a role.
Dr. Yong Pov confirmed that in the past, people, especially young people do not seem to understand the value of vocational training, they often skip. For developed countries, there is a growing need for professionals who have played an important role.
According to Mr. Kith Sopheap, Deputy Director of the Labor Market Information Department of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, for 2021 and 2022, more than 110,000 students have received vocational training, including doctoral training in technology. 31 people as well.
