The body of Lieutenant Colonel Phoeuk Chivoan, who died in the UN operational area under the umbrella of the UN in Mali, has been repatriated.
(Phnom Penh): The body of Lieutenant Colonel Phoeuk Chivoan, Deputy Commander of the Airport Engineering Squadron No. 729, who died in a peacekeeping mission under the United Nations umbrella in Mali, was sent to Cambodia at More than 12 past midnight on February 28, 2023.
The reception for Lt. Col. Phoeuk Chivoan was held in the presence of General Sem Sovanny, Director General of the National Peacekeeping Center, Representative of Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of National Defense, and leaders of the National Peacekeeping Center, parents, wives, children and Many relatives at Phnom Penh International Airport.
The funeral was organized in the traditional Buddhist style as well as in military style with military parades to honor the honor and bravery of the army in the cause of the motherland and the peacekeepers with the United Nations in The country is at war before being sent home in Trapeang Samreth village, Kong Noy commune, Dangkor district, Phnom Penh for a traditional ceremony.
On that occasion, General Sem Sovanny expressed his deepest condolences and condolences to the family of the late Colonel Phoeuk Chivoan, who died while on a humanitarian mission under the auspices of the United Nations. Mali.
In this saddest condolence, General Sem Sovanny, I would like to dedicate my prayers to the body of Lieutenant Colonel Phoeuk Chivoan, to be reborn in the death of all nations, not to be forgotten.
