As of 2023, 11 Cambodian Blue Hat soldiers have died. From 2006 to 2023, Cambodia has sent more than 8,000 Blue Troops to peacekeeping missions in nine countries: Sudan, South Sudan, Chad, Central Africa, Lebanon, Cyprus, Syria, Mali and Yemen.
(Phnom Penh): On Wednesday morning, March 1, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the inauguration of two school buildings and presented diplomas to nearly 5,000 students of the Institute of Technology of Cambodia. The event will take place at the Koh Pich International Convention and Exhibition Center.
According to Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, the Institute of Technology of Cambodia is a public higher education institution that has been playing an important role in training human resources in the fields of science, technology and engineering to contribute to the development of the Cambodian economy.
From 1981 to the present, a total of 14,968 students have graduated from the Institute of Technology of Cambodia, 2,860 of whom are female. These alumni have been working in ministries, public institutions, the private sector, non-governmental organizations and self-employed with high professionalism, excellence, dignity and honor.
According to the Minister, the Institute currently has a management team of 478 civil servants, professors and staff, 148 of whom are female. There are 95 professors with doctorates. This academic year 2022-2023, the institute is training a total of 7,860 students, 2,568 females.
The Institute of Technology of Cambodia in Phnom Penh has a total of 7,747 students, 2,521 of whom are female, and the Institute of Technology of Cambodia, Tbong Khmum Branch has a total of 113 engineering students, 47 of whom are female.
In the last five years, the Institute has published 484 research articles in world-renowned national and international scientific journals. At the same time, the Institute has been implementing technical cooperation projects with development partners, educational and research institutions and international universities to continue to enhance institutional capacity, training and research more effectively, such as:
