Interestingly, a Thai television station continued to broadcast the video and add comments, while Thais came in to insult and humiliate the entire Cambodian community. There are also Thais who say sarcastically, "Thank you for sharing the food of the Khmer people."
In all the videos, the producer always sends a message at the end, citing the content as entertainment and urging the masses to help share and follow his Facebook as well. This means that the video is made for the economic benefit of the producer.
For the production of videos that are selfish, it is considered that it will bring disgrace to the national prestige.
Long Pon Siriwat, secretary of state and spokesman for the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, does not support the production of such videos. He added that Cambodians are not starving to this level. "Culture is the sowing of knowledge, and Cambodian culture has never taught people to make videos and eat like that," he added.
In addition, Mr. Un Chim, a Thai-speaking citizen, expressed his pain when he saw Cambodians insulted through the video above. In spite of the pain, he requested the competent officials to take any action to prevent the video production activities that bring disgrace to the national prestige.
Neak Oknha Kouch Mengly, an expert in the field of education, said that abroad, there is a production of video content that is far different from the production of Cambodian producers. The production of such videos is classified as entertainment and is a free right for people to watch and laugh and reduce fatigue.
He noted that our Cambodians have not yet produced videos that demean the nation. He encouraged Cambodians to open their hearts, but if they understand that the activities in the video are harmful, they can ask him to stop, not condemn him, because judging him with bad words will make him lose his income.
Duke Kouch Mengly stated, "This is a personal story, an entertainment story, a joke, but because of this posting, there are criticisms from neighboring countries that are more influential than us and always scold our citizens in Defamation of our name, then, makes us Cambodians look bad. "But in fact, there is a lot of humor, and this is a joke that, if we talk in Europe, they do not care much."
Chinese Foreign Minister Qin Gang delivers a video address at the 52nd Summit of the UN Human Rights Council
BEIJING, Feb. 27 (Xinhua) - Chinese Foreign Minister Qin Gang attended a video conference of the 52nd Summit of the UN Human Rights Council in Beijing on Friday.
Qin Gang said that at present, the development of international human rights causes serious problems. China will take the following initiatives: First, adhere to the path of human rights development appropriate to the situation of their respective countries; Second, adhere to the promotion and protection of all human rights in all aspects, third, adhere to equality and Justice and fourth, adhere to dialogue and cooperation.
Qin Gang stressed that the development of China's human rights cause has achieved historic results. The key point is that China has followed the path of human rights development in line with the current situation and situation of its country. China will continue to follow this path unwaveringly.
