A total of 7,394 troops from 30 countries participated, including Japan, Singapore, South Korea, Malaysia and Indonesia, while China, India and Australia also participated. In Humanitarian Operation Exercises. Ten countries, including Cambodia, participated as observers, while the other 10 countries participated as multilateral operational planning teams.
Director General: Expansion of water supply capacity boosts Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority's share price
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Long Naro, Director General of Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority, expressed optimism that the share price of Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority, a state-listed entity, will increase further than the current price as the Water Supply Authority strives to expand. Continuing the production system and water supply in Phnom Penh.
He added that currently the production and business capacity as well as water supply of Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority has increased significantly, which can attract investors in the stock market looking to buy this stock.
"People who play in the stock market will look at the management of the water sector, as I see it, is gradually increasing, and now it has risen to 8,000 riel in recent weeks, and I believe that In April, it will rise further after the Water Supply Authority will announce the revenue and profit report recognized by the external audit. Therefore, I believe that in early April, the stock price will rise further.
He added that although the share price tends to rise, the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority has no plans to issue additional shares, as this case is under the decision of the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
According to Long Naro, the money that the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority has received from the stock market in the past has already been repaid to the World Bank in the amount of nearly 30 million US dollars.
He said that at present, the share price of Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority has increased around 8,000 Riel per share, while in 2017 it has dropped below 3,000 Riel per share.
He said the rise was a reflection of investors' reassessment of the stock, as well as an uptrend in the market, which began with more stocks and more investors in the market.
Please be informed that Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority is the first state entity listed on the Cambodia Securities Exchange since April 2012 in the amount of approximately 20 million US dollars.
