As of 2023, 11 Cambodian Blue Hat soldiers have been killed and 15 wounded during missions in various target areas. From 2006 to 2023, Cambodia has sent more than 8,000 Blue Troops to peacekeeping missions in nine countries: Sudan, South Sudan, Chad, Central Africa, Lebanon, Cyprus, Syria, Mali and Yemen.
