The third ring road is about 90% complete and is scheduled for completion in May 2023.
(Phnom Penh): On the occasion of leading the working group to inspect the progress of the construction of the third ring road on February 28, 2023, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, stated that so far The construction of the third ring road is about 90% complete and is scheduled to be completed in May 2023, ahead of schedule.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol stated that for the third ring road, which is more than 50 kilometers long, there are two types, with 48 kilometers of reinforced concrete, 22 centimeters thick, with a width of up to 27 meters for downtown, for out-of-town, 25 meters wide. For the 5 km stretch of road, 9 cm of concrete was poured for a construction cost of 273 million US dollars.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol confirmed that the project to build the third ring road after the Ministry inspected the quality in some places and found that the company did the right technical standards, however, the Ministry will continue to monitor. Ensure that the road is of good quality and durable.
