France to spend 630 million euros to receive Ukrainian refugees by 2022
PARIS (Reuters) - France spent more than 630 million euros last year on hosting nearly 115,000 refugees fleeing France, a French audit firm reported on Tuesday. Russia's invasion of Ukraine. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Tuesday, February 28, 2023.
"Asylum seekers receive" satisfactory "conditions under the" Temporary Protection "plan for unprecedented refugees until 2022, an auditor said in a report.
The program allows them to receive privileges denied to other asylum seekers, including employment, health care, children's education and emergency accommodation.
For each person, the auditor found that Paris spent about twice as much on Ukrainian refugees compared to previous asylum seekers.
In fact, the cost of housing for Ukrainians is about 38 euros per person per day, while the cost of existing refugees is less than 18 euros.
The French Ministry of Housing told AFP last week that Paris was currently spending nearly 8,000,000 euros a month to support the 900 families that had volunteered to host. But the auditors warn that there is no guarantee that these state spending will continue in the future.
