Pursuant to Chapter 10 of the Forestry Law, Wildlife Conservation Article 48 states that all species of wildlife in the Kingdom of Cambodia are state property and a component of forest resources. All of these species are under the control, research and conservation of the Forestry Administration. All wildlife species are divided into three groups: 1: endangered species, 2: rare species, and 3: moderate species.
The peacock, on the other hand, is considered a rare and endangered group.
Please be informed that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, at noon on February 28, 2023, issued an urgent order to the officials in charge of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries who went to catch peacocks at people's homes in Boribo District, Kampong Chhnang Province, returned to its owner at home today.
