Closing Meeting of Svay Rieng Provincial Department of Education, Senior Officials of the Ministry of Education set 7 goals for relevant officials to implement more successfully in the field of education
(Svay Rieng): Mr. Chea Cheat, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, in the closing ceremony of the meeting to summarize the work of education, youth and sports for the academic year 2021-2022 and to raise the work direction for the academic year 2022-2023, set 7 goals for the Department of Education of Svay Rieng Province Apply more successfully.
The closing ceremony was attended by Mr. Touch Poliva, Deputy Governor of Svay Rieng Province, Representative of the Provincial Governor and Mr. Khieu Sam Ol, Director of the Provincial Department of Education, Youth and Sports, Mr. and Mrs. officials of the Department of Education and Mr. and Mrs. Director of the 8 District Education Offices. Schools at all levels, departments around many provinces as well.
The Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Education has instructed the Svay Rieng Provincial Department of Education, Youth and Sports to implement seven points, including:
* First: Promote the revolution of labor, education, youth and sports on a regular basis. Continue to strengthen education services to ensure quality, equity and environment, as well as promote lifelong learning for all and address the learning of students and youth in need.
* Second: Continue to improve the clean environment, good service, continue to maintain, improve, renovate, build school buildings and equip adequate furniture, pay attention to build libraries, laboratories, workshops, home science rooms, gardens, vegetable gardens, biodiversity parks, green environment, sports fields . Continue to promote environmental education, tree planting in school grounds, classrooms and waste management.
* Third: Continue to develop the management and leadership capacity of education officials at all levels, reform the implementation of teacher training, regular professional development of teachers in the motto of good management, good teaching, good learning.
* Fourth: Continue to develop digital education through the integration of digital technology into all levels of educational programs, equipping digital laboratories in educational institutions, enhancing the capacity of digital teachers and disseminating this work widely.
* Fifth: Continue to increase the participation of parents, guardians, communities to help monitor their children's education and help develop the school.
* Sixth: Continue to be more active in the work of scouts and youth by adhering to good deeds in society by inspiring good children, good students, good friends, good citizens, youth volunteer programs in the community with the training of technical skills and soft skills for young people. To respond in a timely manner to job opportunities in society.
* 7th: Continue to improve health and hygiene in educational institutions by paying attention to school sales, exercise, and support students' physical and mental health.
Mr. Khieu Sam Ol said that the discussion in the meeting decided to set out the following recommendations:
* In the school year 2022-2023, there are no new teachers, leaving some teachers to retire and die due to illness. Some schools lack school buildings, some are dilapidated and damaged, requiring urgent repairs. JICA President Invites Leaders of the Ministry of Social Affairs to Visit a Nursing Home in Japan to Experience Cambodia-Japan
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, received Mr. Fumio Yamada, President of the Cambodia-Japan Cooperation Association (JICA) to pay a courtesy call and discuss work on the welfare of the elderly in Cambodia on the 28th. February 2023, Office of the Ministry of Social Affairs.
During the meeting, Minister Vong Soth extended a warm welcome to the President of the organization and praised and appreciated the cooperation of JCIA, which has always supported the welfare of the elderly and other fields.
Mr. Vong Soth emphasized that during the outbreak of Kovid-19, the Royal Government of Cambodia paid close attention to the poor affected by Kovid-19, especially the elderly. From 60 years up through various social assistance programs to support monthly livelihoods as well.
Fumio Yamada says that during the Kovid-19 outbreak, care centers for the elderly in Japan have not been fully operational for three years.
Fumio Yamada added that it was now possible to re-launch as planned. He expects that in the near future, he will send officers to study and train in the care of the elderly in Japan directly and return to work as trainers in Cambodia on the care of the elderly.
At the same time, the President of the organization also asked Minister Vong Soth and his colleagues to visit the nursing home in Japan to learn from each other's experiences between the two countries.
In response, Minister Vong Soth also agreed to the request of the President of the organization and find a suitable time to lead the delegation to visit the nursing home directly to get good experience to ensure the development of the welfare of the elderly. Cambodia.
