(Phnom Penh): Mr. Khuong Sreng said that peace is the only way to develop the country and there are enough opportunities to absorb knowledge and create important human resources. Therefore, we must work together to maintain this peace.
This was stated by Mr. Khuong Sreng, Personal Adviser to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Governor of Phnom Penh, as he presided over the 29th Graduation Ceremony for the Winners of Sen Sok International University on the afternoon of February 25. This 2023.
Mr. Khuong Sreng stated that some unscrupulous people accused the degree of learning and offering in Cambodia of poor quality. Such an allegation is also an unacceptable accusation. This is an insult to our teachers and students who have worked hard to learn.
He said that today is a testament to the efforts of young people to acquire valuable knowledge. You need to know where we came from, we must be grateful for the heroism of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who sacrificed everything, even the lives to save the lives of our people.
He added that we are very lucky to have leaders who are motivated to make the country prosperous, even though Cambodia has risen from zero under the genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
Mr. Khuong Sreng continued that the prince continued to seek peace throughout the country and work to develop the country. It is from these things that we have the opportunity to learn, to gain knowledge, to create this vital human resource.
Mr. Khuong Sreng wants a citizen to be a defender of the truth. Protecting Samdech Techo Hun Sen is protecting the truth. So what do we have to contribute to keep the peace? We can only keep the peace if we vote for the CPP. Voting for the CPP is tantamount to supporting Samdech as Prime Minister.
On that occasion, Prof. Dr. Sabo Ozano, Rector of the International University, emphasized that the International University is one of the first private higher education institutions established on December 16, 2002.
He said that the winning students to receive a bachelor's degree now are intermediate pharmacists, associate degree nurses, midwives, laboratories and dentists, a total of 461, 298 females.
The Rector further stated that in order to improve the quality of education, the International University has cooperated in international frameworks and development partners, as well as various ministries, institutions of the Royal Government and many friendly countries.
He said that so far, 76% of students of international universities are employed, 24% of students are self-employed, 86% of students work in the right field and 14% in the non-specialized field. The university has determined that the quality of education is the only fundamental determinant of the university's sustainability.
The meeting was held with the main goal of disseminating the results and decisions of the Cambodian People's Party in the Extraordinary General Assembly on January 28-29, 2023. The results and decisions of the General Assembly are read and distributed to the participating members.
In addition to the results and decisions shared, Dr. Nop Ratana also highlighted the development of various situations in the political society, as well as the development of the international situation.
Regarding the development of the local situation, Dr. Nop Ratana highlighted some outstanding achievements under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, which are beneficial for the society and the people of Cambodia, and also raised Cambodia's reputation on the international stage.
The success that Dr. Nop Ratana highlighted was the rapid overcoming of the 19 epidemic of Kovid and the success of Cambodia as the chair of ASEAN in 2022. For Nop Ratana, the success of these two things has led to Cambodia's reputation on the international stage.
Mr. Nop Ratana highlighted that "Samdech Techo Hun Sen's work is recognized, Cambodia is recognized as a developed country and a very prestigious country in the world. "The factor that led to this prestige in Cambodia is the fight against Kovid 19 was successful quickly, re-opening the country in the country."
Regarding the fight against Kovid 19, Dr. Nop Ratana presented his successful work on vaccinating Kovid 19 to the people. Dr. stated that Samdech Techo has researched all ways to find a large number of vaccines against Kovid 19 to give people on time and free of charge. Samdech Techo's principles are correct and strict, especially with clear assignments at the national, sub-national and local levels.
"In the fight against Kovid 19, at first there were so many countries that we were left with a weak health and it would be difficult to overcome Kovid 19," he said. "Finally, they can see the small country, the weak country in terms of health, but can protect the lives of the people well, get vaccinated quickly, overcome the epidemic of Kovid 19 quickly, reopen social activities quickly." This is the highlight of Dr. Nop Ratana.
On that occasion, Dr. also highlighted the great success of Cambodia as the rotating chair of ASEAN in 2022. The ASEAN chairmanship in 2022 comes at a time when the regional and global situation is facing many challenges due to the Kovid 19 crisis, geopolitical rivalries and the war crisis in Ukraine.
Dr. Nop Ratana highlighted that "Despite the many challenges, Cambodia can lead this meeting successfully. More than 100 documents have been approved and major regional and global leaders have been invited to attend the meeting in Cambodia. ”
"This success, due to Samdech Techo's diplomatic prowess, has prevented major world leaders from meeting with him to discuss bilateral, regional and global issues," he added.
In addition to highlighting the outstanding achievements of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's leadership, which brought Cambodia's reputation to the forefront on the international stage, Dr. Nop Ratana also highlighted the CPP's defense policy decided at the General Assembly. Also.
He emphasized that the CPP's defense policy is based on four priorities: to continue to protect Cambodia's core interests, to pursue an independent, sovereign and non-aligned foreign policy, to contribute to regional and global action, and to The height of economic diplomacy with friendly countries, both old and new.
On that occasion, Dr. Nop Ratana also highlighted some of the corrupt activities of the opposition party and the contrary propaganda of VOD radio, which led to legal action.
At the same time, Dr. called on party members to increase activities to meet the people and explain to the people to listen and see what reflects the reality in Cambodia. Do not believe in divisive propaganda.
"How to keep the peace," he said. Peace is an easy word to say, but finding peace and maintaining peace is difficult. Therefore, we must work together to maintain peace so that the people can live in peace. "
(Phnom Penh): The owners of two cars were stopped by the authorities and made an education contract after driving in the opposite direction on the expressway, which could cause serious harm to others. After being stopped, educated, instructed and contracted to stop their activities, the two drivers publicly apologized and admitted their mistakes.
The two drivers also appealed to other residents, especially highway users, not to follow suit, as this activity could pose a serious danger to others who do not know.
Through what has happened on the expressway, especially traffic accidents, Lt. Gen. Lim Phan Phea, director of the Central Department of Public Order of the National Police General Commission, noted that what the reversing driver apologized for was a separate matter. But what is the concern of the authorities.
The senior police officer argued that most of the drivers are the head of the family, the mainstay of the family. What is the situation of the family, wife, children waiting for the husband and father at home? And to what extent.
Lt. Gen. Lim Phanpheak noted that the restraint and contract of education can only be done when there is no accident, if he drives in reverse and causes an accident, can the authorities have the opportunity to educate him? Do you drive? This is what the authorities want all public road users, including expressway users, to understand.
