China pushes for peaceful solution to Ukraine crisis as US warns against Russian aid (Video inside) (Beijing): China says it pushes for dialogue and peaceful solution to Ukraine crisis That Beijing could consider supplying weapons to its ally Russia. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Monday, February 27, 2023.
The Chinese Foreign Ministry said it had maintained contact with all parties to the crisis, including Kiev, and its position was clear.
"The main theme is the call for peace, dialogue and a political solution to the crisis in Ukraine," Foreign Ministry spokeswoman Mao Ning told a news conference in Beijing on Monday.
China, which declared a "borderless" alliance with Russia shortly before the invasion a year ago, refused to condemn the attack and last week released a 12-point plan calling for a ceasefire and a ceasefire. Gradual reduction by both sides.
Kiev responded by accepting some aspects of the plan, while emphasizing that there would be no peace without a complete Russian withdrawal.
