(Istanbul): Another earthquake on Monday (February 27) shook the southeast of Turkey, killing one person and injuring 69, causing 29 buildings to collapse, causing horrific work in Rescue some people who are believed to be trapped in the rubble. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Monday, February 27, 2023.
The latest quake had a magnitude of 5.6 and a depth of 6.15 km. It struck three weeks after a major earthquake that killed more than 50,000 people in Turkey and Syria.
The Turkish Disaster Management and Emergency Management Agency (AFAD) on Sunday announced that the death toll in the previous devastating earthquake had risen to 343,374 in Turkey.
The quake is expected to have serious psychological consequences, especially for the most vulnerable children.
