The death toll near the southern Italian coast of Italy has risen to 61 as the search for the missing continues, an Italian official said on Monday. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Monday, February 27, 2023.
Italian media claimed that the boat was carrying more than 100 migrants from Iran, Pakistan and Afghanistan, and that it had been hit by rocks during bad weather at sea.
She added that based on reports of survivors, authorities believed that between 180 and 200 people had boarded the boat involved in the accident.
Italy is a major destination for migrants trying to flee to Europe by sea. The so-called Central Mediterranean route is one of the most dangerous in the world. Since 2014, 20,333 people have been killed or missing in the central Mediterranean.
