First, one should understand the meaning of the word "money laundering". Money laundering means the illegality of making large amounts of illegal money from crimes such as drug trafficking, smuggling of goods and terrorism look like legal money. (Or legal). Criminals use a variety of methods to launder their money.
What are the popular ways to launder money?
Money laundering can be carried out by exchanging currency and bringing cash across borders to exchange foreign currency in other countries that do not pay much attention to money laundering activities. Other ways of laundering money include investing in valuables such as gems and gold and other investments such as real estate and gambling.
Simple Methods There are many ways to launder money, from simple to complicated. One of the simplest techniques is to use a legitimate business. For example, if a criminal runs a business, he can inflate his daily receipt to put that money in the store's account. The money can then be withdrawn as needed.
