The King issues a Royal Decree appointing six Secretaries of State and Undersecretaries of State of the Ministry of Labor and appointing them as advisors.
(Phnom Penh): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, has issued a Royal Decree appointing six Secretaries of State and Undersecretaries of State at the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training. This is according to the Royal Decree obtained by Fresh News on February 27, 2023.
According to the Royal Decree, the positions of Secretary of State and Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training include: * 1: Mr. IN Khemara as Secretary of State * 2: Mr. Som Chamnan as Secretary of State * 3: Mr. Srun Chanthol as Undersecretary of State * 4 : Ms. Chhuon Chandorey as Undersecretary of State * 5: Mr. San Kimhong as Undersecretary of State * 6: Mr. Vit Sovan Udom as Undersecretary of State
At the same time, the Royal Decree also appointed and appointed Ms. Khun Nai Hiek as an advisor to the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training with the rank of Director General.
The following is the Royal Decree: Lt. Gen. Hun Manet holds bilateral meeting with Commander of the Singapore Army
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of February 27, 2023, at the Land Forces Command of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Lieutenant General Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, held a bilateral meeting with Lt. Gen. David. David Neo, Commander of the Singapore Army, is leading an official visit to Cambodia.
During the meeting, the two counterparts expressed pride in the close friendly relations between Cambodia and Singapore since the establishment of formal diplomatic ties in 1965, when Cambodia was one of the first countries to recognize Singapore's independence. And continue to this day, bilateral cooperation in all fields has progressed steadily.
On that occasion, Major General David Neo also expressed his appreciation to the Royal Government of Cambodia for effectively controlling the spread of Kovid-19 disease and also mentioned Cambodia's success in being Hosted by the ASEAN Defense Ministers 'Meeting (ADMM) and the ASEAN Defense Ministers' Meeting Plus (ADMM Plus) held in November 2022.
It should be noted that the current visit of Major General David Neo is the second official visit of the Commander of the Singapore Army in Cambodia, which will be an additional driving force in promoting and enhancing relations between the two armies. The land of the two countries to be more active, deep and strong.
Dry river will be a carbon neutral model eco-tourism destination in Cambodia
(Tbong Khmum): The dry river in the area of Preah Theat Basrey temple in Preah Theat commune, Oreang Ov district, Tbong Khmum province is being transformed into a model carbon neutral natural resort in Cambodia with 1 million plants. Plant trees and use solar-powered electricity, which is renewable energy.
Recently, Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment and Chairman of the National Task Force for Ou Raing Ov District, Tbong Khmum Province, stated that 1 million curtain trees have already been planted at the historical site "Dry River" to give to the gods. The new year is planned to bless the people on the occasion of the traditional New Year and to rule the territory of the Kingdom of Cambodia in the future.
At the same time, the team built infrastructure on the site, which is an important water storage area for people to use for growing crops and planted nearly 1,000 trees. The team has renovated the historic site into a beautiful resort with 50 more solar panels. For people to visit Khmer New Year on weekends and during various festivals.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth added that the preparation of the natural historical site "Dry River" for the benefit of the people, especially to strengthen the community in the area through the development of eco-tourism, land integration and sustainable living.
