The project on "Strengthening Community Financial Security" was launched on 24 February 2023 to improve access to and access to secure official financial services in the community, which will contribute to the promotion of a national policy on villages. The commune is safe.
The project "Strengthening Community Financial Security" will be piloted in Kampong Thom, Kampong Speu, Svay Rieng and Battambang provinces from 2023 and will continue to expand in the following years.
"Public trust in the use of official financial services is a key factor that the National Bank of Cambodia and other stakeholders have continued to work to improve," said Rath Sovannarak, Assistant Governor and Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia. "Financial knowledge and strengthen customer protection in order to maintain the stability of the entire banking system and improve the financial environment in the country."
Mr. Sok Voeun, Chairman of the Board of the Microfinance Association of Cambodia, emphasized that the implementation of this project requires close coordination and cooperation among stakeholders, including citizens and local authorities.
"We will work together to ensure the effective implementation of the project, and we believe it will make a significant contribution to improving financial literacy, rights and consumer protection in Cambodia."
This project will contribute to the improvement of living standards and development in the pilot project area, as well as continue to expand activities throughout Cambodia for long-term goals through existing commune council mechanisms. The project will also strengthen partnerships and resource mobilization to improve the quality of implementation, documentation, evidence and best practice examples to expand the scope of future projects.
