Samdech Techo Hun Sen: The Royal Government wants to turn Cambodia into a powerful cashew processing and export country (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on February 27, 2023 Know that the Royal Government wants to turn Cambodia into a strong processing and export of cashew nuts, because Cambodia currently exports 1 million tons of unprocessed cashew nuts.
This statement was made on the occasion of Samdech Techo Hun Sen presiding over the graduation ceremony for more than 5,000 teachers, technical students and students who successfully graduated from the National Technical Training Institute on the morning of February 27. This 2023.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated, "Going forward, if Cambodia has the ability, Cambodia can become a country that distributes cashew nuts, which will almost become one of the strongest in the distribution, because one year Cambodia exports nuts. 1 million tons of unprocessed cashews ... We have processed very little ourselves to bring to the exhibition for sale.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that in the future, the Royal Government is attracting investors who come to the country with industrial policy, and Samdech always tells foreign friends and foreign investors to focus. For investing in Cambodia.
The Prime Minister said that Vietnam and India are the main exporters of cashew nuts to many parts of the world, but Vietnam is importing cashew nuts from some African countries for processing, and Cambodia is also dependent on the market. Vietnam to export cashew nuts, and India as well, partly grown locally and partly imported.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that Cambodia has raw materials, but the processing is not enough, so Cambodia wants to attract investors to process local raw materials, and the point is that it will create jobs and create. Value added for our production.
Samdech continued that the policy of rice production and export of rice, one of the two successes is the success of the lack of rice-rice to become a country where the emperor of rice-rice, but did not succeed in exporting 1 million tons, exporting between 50 Only 100,000 to 600,000 tons due to lack of processing base related to rice mills, dryers and capital.
In addition, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that Cambodia has a lot of rubber, but not a lot of domestic processing and cassava is exported just cut into wheels, about 20 million tons, especially for processed sugar cane. Domestic sugar, but for the rest, raw materials are exported.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia added that our exports can be processed to the target market as it is distributed to the tourist destinations of the countries in need.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that if Cambodia can attract investment for the local raw material processing industry, it will provide opportunities for farmers to grow and have markets and factories, and solve labor problems and provide value for our products.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also said that during his visit to China, Chinese President Xi Jinping, while eating, raised cashew nuts brought from Cambodia to show at that time. Also.
Please be informed that according to the report of the Cambodian Cashew Association in 2022, Cambodia exported 670,000 tons of raw cashew nuts to the international market, amounting to 1.077 million US dollars, a decrease of 34.65 percent. This decline is due to climate change.
According to the report, almost 100 percent of Cambodia's cashew exports to Vietnam were 660,000 tons, down 37 percent. Dried cashew nuts cost between 5,500 riel and 7,200 riel, depending on the quality of the seeds.
