350 Vulnerable Families in Russey Keo Receive Donations from Saudi Rabita
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Osman Hassan, Senior Minister in Charge of Special Missions and President of the Cambodian Muslim Development Foundation, on the morning of February 26, 2023, met and brought gifts to 350 vulnerable families in Khan. Russey Keo, Phnom Penh.
The event was held at the Jamek Amir Pinya Sear Kilometer 9, Sangkat Chrang Chamres I, Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh, with the participation of members of the National Assembly, Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State, Advisers to the Royal Government and local authorities.
Dr. Osman Hassan said that this donation is a complement of Rabita with the Royal Government of Cambodia to supply vulnerable Cambodians in general.
Dr. said that the Royal Government has been taking care to solve all the concerns of the people of Cambodia in a timely manner, such as during the epidemic of Kovid 19, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia has tried to find a vaccine to give people free. Charge. At the same time, the government has also provided food, basic necessities to needy and vulnerable families.
Dr. Osman Hassan also highlighted the rapid development of road infrastructure and the construction of high-rise commercial government buildings.
On that occasion, he mentioned the achievements and policies of national and religious harmony of the Royal Government under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, especially urged the people who have the name to vote to vote for the Cambodian People's Party. Everyone.
Please be informed that the above donation is sponsored by RABITA of the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia through the Cambodian Muslim Development Foundation and the Cambodian Muslim Youth Association. Japan Provides Over $ 840,000 Grant for Environmental Awareness, Supplementary Education and Development of Higher Education Institutions for Physical Education through Information and Communication Technology
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Japan, through the Embassy of Japan in Cambodia, has continued to sign a grant of US $ 843,946 to three recipients under a grant scheme for a Japanese NGO project to promote Understand environmental issues, the promotion of supplementary education and the development of quality higher education institutions for physical education through information and communication technology.
The grant agreement was signed on February 27, 2023 by Mr. Uno Atsushi, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of Japan to the Kingdom of Cambodia and representatives of the three recipients.
We expect this project to help improve the living environment throughout Cambodia.
Second: Project to promote supplementary education for primary schools in remote areas of Cambodia (US $ 263,656) Recipient: Volunteer Organization (SVA)
And (3) the project to develop a four-year higher education institution for qualified physical education teachers through the use of information and communication technology (first year) (US $ 470,255) Recipient: NGO Golden heart.
In this project, Golden Heart will work with the National Institute of Physical Education and Sports (NIPES) to improve seven key management systems: library operations, the establishment of an international center, internal quality assurance, teacher development, student management, and support for the former. Students and security management using information and communication technology equipment.
Through this project, about 70 staff and 180 trainee teachers in the institute will be able to get a better learning environment for physical education. In addition, we expect more than 1,000,000 students in Cambodia to receive more effective physical education.
Grants for the Japan NGO Project have been in Cambodia since 2002 to support the activities of Japanese NGOs in their efforts to support the development and reconstruction of Cambodia at the grassroots level.
