Israel, Palestine agree on measures to prevent violence (Video inside) (Jerusalem): Israeli and Palestinian officials have pledged to implement agreed measures to mitigate and prevent violence after a round of talks in Brussels. In Jordan. This was released by the AFP news agency on Monday, February 27, 2023.
In a joint statement issued after the talks in Aqaba, Jordan, on Sunday, Israeli and Palestinian officials said the two sides would work closely to prevent Do not let new violence erupt and also affirm the need for a commitment to alleviate today's tensions.
In addition, according to the joint statement, Israel will suspend talks on new colonial settlements for four months and suspend the approval of new colonial settlements for six months. Months.
The joint statement between Israel and the Palestinians came at the end of a roundtable discussion with officials from the United States, Egypt and Jordan amid growing concerns about the possibility of escalation of hostilities. Violence as the month of Ramadan for Muslims approaches.
