Putin says Ukraine war is Russia's battle for survival (Video inside) (Moscow): Russian President Vladimir Putin has described the confrontation with the West over Ukraine as a battle for Russia's survival. And its people and said he was being forced to consider NATO nuclear capabilities. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Sunday, February 26, 2023.
A year after ordering the invasion of Ukraine, Putin increasingly described the war as a time of creation or disintegration in Russian history and said he believed the future of Russia and its people was in trouble.
However, NATO and the West have denied the allegations, saying their goal is to help Ukraine defend itself against Russian attacks.
Putin said the West wanted to break up Russia and then take over the world's largest raw material producer, a move that could lead to the destruction of many Russians, including minorities. Russia as well.
Reuters reports that India wants a joint global effort to address issues caused by cryptocurrencies such as Bitcoin, and the G20 finance ministers are holding a seminar for the state. G20 members to discuss how to create a common framework.
Speaking to Reuters on the sidelines of the G20 summit in Bengaluru, India, US Treasury Secretary Janet Yellen said it was important to implement a strong regulatory framework, but added that the United States The United States has not proposed a complete ban.
"We are not proposing a complete ban on crypto activities, but it is important to have a strong regulatory framework in place," Yellen said. "We are working with other governments."
The government of Indian Prime Minister Narendra Modi has been debating for several years a draft law governing or banning cryptocurrencies, but has yet to make a final decision. The Bank of India has said that cryptocurrencies should be banned because they are similar to Ponzi schemes.
On Thursday, the IMF released a nine-point action plan on how countries should deal with cryptocurrency assets. The IMF said such efforts have become a priority for authorities after the collapse of the cryptocurrency market and some cryptocurrency assets in recent years. According to Reuters.
China's economy expected to recover this year under clear central bank monetary policy
BEIJING: China's economy is expected to recover by 2023 and monetary policy will be clear and strong, the People's Bank of China said. According to Reuters.
The central bank will focus on supporting domestic demand growth and stabilizing economic growth and commodity prices, the People's Bank of China quoted Reuters as saying in its quarterly policy report. Use while avoiding excessive stimulus measures.
However, the central bank said the external environment remained "serious and complex" and that the fundamentals of the domestic economic recovery were "not strong". The report also said that the real estate sector needs time for change as the pressure to balance local fiscal revenue and expenditure continues.
China will closely monitor inflation trends and maintain energy prices and food stability, the report said.
The report does not change much from the previous report, with the market expecting a reshuffle of the government, especially the economic working group, and the announcement of economic and policy targets for 2023 at the annual session of parliament. Starting March 5.
China, the world's second-largest economy, is stabilizing and recovering, but still faces many challenges, Chinese Premier Li Keqiang said at a cabinet meeting on Wednesday. The remarks come after China's economy grew at its slowest pace in half a decade due to tightening sanctions and blockades by 2022. According to Reuters.
