Remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of presiding over the graduation ceremony for more than 5,000 teachers, technical students and students
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Monday, February 27, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the graduation ceremony for more than 5,000 teachers, technical students and students who have successfully graduated from the National Technical Training Institute. .
The ceremony took place at the Chroy Changva Convention and Exhibition Center. According to Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has always been honored to preside over the graduation ceremony for technical teachers and graduates of the National Technical Training Institute. In that, Samdech Techo has already been invited four times.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen delivered a two-hour talk, the following are the main contents of Samdech:
* As a start, Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded that there are only 67 days left until the SEA Games, which Cambodia is hosting, after waiting for 64 years.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded that in 1996, the National Technical Training Institute had only more than 200 students with difficulty finding jobs because the country had not yet finished the war.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded that at that time, when Samdech went to Kratie province, Samdech advised to pay attention to training on boat building.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen recalled that the National Technical Training Institute was established in 1958, originally called the "Kosomak Center" under the leadership of King Norodom Sihanouk.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that technical training had been taken care of by His Majesty the King since the late 1950s but had been destroyed by the war.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the decline of Cambodia's progress was due to the coup d'etat of 1970 and then the fall of Democratic Kampuchea.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded that the establishment of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training was initiated by Samdech and Samdech Krom Preah on Samdech Kar Koun Day.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that technical vocational training is very important to meet local needs and attract investors. No technician can meet the needs of investors.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that there is no investment in a country at war and without peace.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that tomorrow, Samdech will meet with the US-ASEAN Business Council and Samdech will tell them not to look at Cambodia only, Cambodia must look beyond Cambodia, as Cambodia is a member and many trading partners. With regional and global countries.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that due to the high demand for these professional skills in Cambodia, it was decided to set a target to recruit about 1.5 million poor people for vocational training.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in the future, Cambodia may be able to become a strong distributor of cashew nuts. Currently, Cambodia exports 1 million tons of fresh cashew nuts.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the processing of cashew nuts is a priority that the Royal Government wants and strives to attract foreign investors.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen says that Cambodia's rice policy has evolved from a rice-scarce country to a rice-scarce country, but Cambodia has not yet achieved its export target of 1 million tons, only 500,000 to 600,000 tons due to a lack of factories. Dryers and capital.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia needs to invest in cassava flour processing for export.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia's main goal is to attract investment in the processing industry, local products and high-tech industries.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the development of the nation could not be stagnant and that peace provided opportunities for development.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that peace and political stability are essential for investment.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the win-win policy ended in 1998, not in 1998. This win-win policy was implemented and was first successful in February 1996 in Oral district, Kampong Speu province.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reiterated that the UNTAC mission could not end the war in Cambodia in accordance with the Paris Peace Agreement of October 23, 1991.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the guarantee of life, role and ownership of real estate is a condition that leads to a win-win policy.
