The Minister of Labor and Vocational Training reminded that the National Technical Training Institute was established in 1958 as the "Kosomak Center". However, the center was suspended during the genocidal regime of Pol Pot and reopened in 1981 and was renamed.
The institute was transferred from the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports to the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training under the name "National Technical Training Institute". The institute has two main tasks: to train technical student teachers to become technical teachers, to work in technical and vocational training institutions, and to train trainees, students from short to long term, both public scholarship students. And students pay tuition fees.
According to the Minister, the institute has a management team of 258 contracted Cambodian professors and staff, 64 of whom are female. There are 9 PhDs, 108 Master's Degrees, 18 females, 84 Bachelor / Engineers, 28 females, 57 Undergraduates, 18 females.
