Wildlife in Cambodia is divided into three groups: the first group is endangered, such as oxen, elephants, leopards, reindeer, giants, white-winged ducks, the second group, rare species such as giraffes, raccoons, bears, peacocks, peacocks Sek Som, and the third group, the species are moderate, such as wild boar, chhlous, rabbit, sampouch, kok, wild chicken, Tom, Pravek, Sarika, Keo, Tracheak Kam.
