(Phnom Penh): In order to facilitate the flow of traffic and travel of the people, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration has received the high permission of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, to temporarily use the Russey Keo flyover from March 1. This year 2023 onwards. This is according to the announcement received by Fresh News on February 24, 2023.
The Russey Keo flyover in Khleang Saing village, Sangkat Russey Keo, Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh, opened its construction site on January 31, 2022 under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and was constructed by the Overseas Cambodian Investment Company (OCIC). How to take a city, raise a city.
At present, the flyover has a total length of 483 meters and a width of 15.8 meters, which the Overseas Cambodian Investment Company (OCIC) has received the construction policy from the Royal Government, almost 100 percent completed, and only the work of paving and ironing traffic. Which is scheduled to be completed in the next few days.
The Phnom Penh Capital Administration will prepare the remaining construction work for the Russey Keo flyover, such as rubber tapping, carola corrugation, landscaping, and other decorative work to be completed within the next two or three days in order to provide temporary use of the flyover. Russey Keo, 483 meters long and 15.8 meters wide, in order to facilitate the repatriation of people to relieve traffic congestion.
