Dr. HUN Manet stated that as a personal perspective on the partnership between the Royal Government and the private sector and the promotion of the private sector, there are three priority factors:
First, the policy framework: refers to the vision to facilitate the operation and growth of the private sector, and the Royal Government led by the Cambodian People's Party has done a lot of work to serve the growth to this day and will Continue to evaluate and revise policies in order to make the business environment in Cambodia more competitive, convenient and low cost.
Second, the implementation mechanism framework: refers to encouraging the private sector to play a role in direct implementation with the support of the government.
Third, practical implementation: refers to ensuring smooth implementation as a reflection of the drawn-out plan, and this implementation requires clear procedures, simplicity, liveliness and transparency, along with human factors. Understand and have practical experience, especially the balance between government officials and the private sector.
Dr. HUN Manet also asked all entrepreneurs to continue to join the Royal Government in expanding investment in key value-added sectors to contribute to poverty reduction and continue to create additional employment opportunities for people, especially for young people. Government policy.
At the same time, Dr. Hun Manet also encourages all entrepreneurs to increase capacity, strengthen competitiveness and strive to maximize the benefits of policies as well as measures of the Royal Government to the private sector, especially through Invest in priority sectors to receive fiscal incentives, access to entrepreneurship training, skills development, and take advantage of free trade agreements with countries.
In addition to creating wealth and making a profit, all entrepreneurs also need to cultivate the idea of contributing to social work, as well as embracing digital technology in innovative and innovative businesses that can bring higher productivity and greater value. To the national economy. This is the additional confirmation of Dr. Hun Manet.
Dr. HUN Manet also asked the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce to continue to provide close support and cooperation with all stakeholders, especially new enterprises to strengthen and expand the employment network, share knowledge and experience, and contribute to the Royal Government in Building an entrepreneurial ecosystem that is strong, comprehensive, vibrant and environmentally friendly.
