The 2023 Women's Global Summit aims to share perspectives, experiences on women's leadership and solutions to issues such as gender inequality, domestic abuse and political disadvantages. The meeting was attended by participants from more than 100 countries around the world.
Ms. Man Chenda participated as a speaker at the 2023 Women's Global Summit on the role of women in key global trends. She shared peace, harmony, religiousization and development in the Cambodian context and regional and global perspectives on women's economic empowerment.
In addition, Ms. Man Chenda encouraged the community to establish a fund for women to reduce poverty, encourage women to get a higher education so that they can express themselves and participate in social activities. . Women together are a strong force in the hall to gain strength in society.
She stressed that states should consider narrowing the income gap caused by gender differences and sharing innovative means or best practices to reduce women's poverty in developing countries and pave the way. New for women to make changes through their special role in responding to climate change.
On the other hand, women's leadership in parliament and diplomacy encourages women to participate in national and international politics and to serve the community and the nation in a positive way and to take responsibility ethically and sustainably.
Alibaba on Thursday reported higher-than-expected quarterly earnings as the Chinese e-commerce giant benefited from easing measures to prevent Kovid 19. According to Reuters.
Alibaba overcame a weak economy in China, which in December last year scrapped the Kovid Zero policy after three years of implementation.
China's total retail sales fell 1.8 percent in December, while the country's economy will grow 3 percent in 2022, its lowest growth rate in nearly half a century. According to Reuters.
