Total revenue rose 8% from the second quarter to S $ 4.85 billion. According to Reuters.
China boosts coal imports from Australia after two-year hiatus (Video inside) (Singapore): Chinese companies and traders increase coal purchases from Australia in February, boosted by further policy easing And after trading resumed in part last month after a two-year hiatus. According to Reuters.
In early January, Beijing granted permits to four state-owned companies, including steel company Baowu Group and three other state-owned companies, to transport Australian coal, the first sign of easing import bans since late 2020. . The ban comes as relations between Beijing and Canberra have soured over political and public health issues.
A full resumption of trade between the world's largest coal-using country and the world's second-largest coal exporter could support higher oil prices for energy and steel production.
Reuters reported, citing data from shipping data companies Refinitiv and Kpler, that at least 15 ships shipped about 1.4 million tonnes of Australian coal in February to China.
Another senior trader working for a Chinese state-owned company said more than 1 million tonnes of hot coal were reserved for shipment in March.
"Trafficking has increased significantly over the past three days following comments from the ministry," he said.
Last Thursday, in response to questions at a press conference on Australia's coal import process, a Chinese Ministry of Commerce spokesman said it was a normal trade activity and that trade was being carried out through the import license system. Automatic.
She added that it is up to companies to independently decide on coal imports based on their technological needs and market conditions. According to Reuters.
