The decision to remove Cambodia from the "gray list" of the countries at risk of money laundering was made at the FATF General Assembly on 24 February 2023 in Paris, France and was held as a press conference. Official at 10 pm Cambodian time.
In July 2020, Cambodia also issued a law on anti-money laundering and terrorist financing. This law aims to ensure the prevention of money laundering and terrorist financing by defining measures to control, prevent, suppress and eliminate money laundering and terrorist financing.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, also called on the authorities, national and local authorities and all stakeholders, both imperial and religious, to work together to fight corruption so that Cambodia does not become Crime scene, money laundering, human trafficking and other crimes.
