Kampong Chhnang Provincial Governor Inspects AC Road Construction Process and Other Buildings in National Police School Zone 6
(Kampong Chhnang): Mr. Sun Sovannarith, Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province, and the working group of Provincial Hall Administration on the morning of February 24, 2023, inspected the construction process of AC type rubber road donated by the Provincial Administration at the National Police Hall. Zone 6, Chrey Bak village, Chrey Bak commune, Rolea Bier district.
Major General Tong An, Director of the National Police School of Zone 6, said that the road, which was donated by the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Administration, was built on the premises of the National Police School of Zone 6 with a length of 1950 meters and a 600-meter-long drainage system as an AC road. So far, the 403-meter-long paved road has been paved and is being paved, and more than 90% of the drainage system has been completed.
Lt. Gen. Tong An continued that the National Police School, Zone 6 is building many achievements such as student and teacher dormitories, kitchens and school buildings donated by the Governor of Kandal, the Governor of Phnom Penh and the Governor of Kampong Chhnang and other philanthropists. Many other things that make the National Police School Zone 6 more developed, worthy of a training place for human resources of the National Police Force.
On that occasion, Mr. Sun Sovannarith highly appreciated the construction process of the National Police School, Zone 6, especially the buildings and roads in the campus, as well as the structures in the school yard, which were improved to a high standard.
The provincial governor confirmed that in order to ensure the quality of the road on the campus for long-term use, he asked the company that is receiving the construction to do it properly with high quality techniques.
At the same time, the provincial evaluation team must cooperate with the school to continue to inspect the construction process from the foundation construction to the completion of the construction, and the school must continue to plant bamboo trees and flowers to improve the school environment. China has announced its position on resolving the Ukraine crisis politically.
BEIJING, Feb. 24 (Xinhua) - The Chinese Foreign Ministry on Friday announced China's position on resolving the Ukraine crisis politically. Namely:
Third. Stop shooting. In war there is no winner. Stakeholders should maintain integrity and restraint, do not fuel the conflict, do not escalate the conflict, avoid aggravating the Ukraine crisis to the point of losing control, support Russia and Ukraine, move towards the same goal, hold direct dialogue As soon as possible to promote stress reduction and eventually reach a comprehensive ceasefire.
Sixth. Protect civilians and prisoners of war. The parties to the conflict should strictly abide by international humanitarian law, avoid attacks on civilians and civilian facilities, protect women, children and other victims of the conflict, and respect the fundamental rights of prisoners of war. China supports the exchange of prisoners of war between Russia and Ukraine, and all parties should create more favorable conditions for this.
8th. Strategic risk reduction. Do not use nuclear weapons and do not provoke nuclear war. Should oppose the use or threat of using nuclear weapons. Prevent nuclear proliferation to avoid a nuclear crisis. Against the development and use of biological and chemical weapons by any country under any circumstances.
11th Ensure the stability of the industrial chain and supply chain. The parties should firmly support the existing global economic system against the globalization of the political economy, instruments and weapons. Together, reduce the impact of the crisis and prevent disruption of cooperation in the fields of international energy, finance, trade, food and transportation, which will affect the recovery of the world economy.
12th. Promote post-war reconstruction. The international community should take steps to support post-war reconstruction in the conflict zone. China is willing to provide assistance and play a constructive role in this regard.
