(Phnom Penh): At least 60 suspects were arrested in criminal and drug offenses across Cambodia on February 24, 2023 yesterday. This was confirmed by General Khieu Sopheak, spokesman for the Ministry of Interior, to Fresh News on February 25, 2023.
General Khieu Sopheak added that of the 60 suspects, 20 were arrested in 15 criminal cases and 40 were arrested in 14 drug cases.
Minister of Agriculture urges farmers around Kiri Sour dairy farm to consider planting grass to supply their farms
(Takeo): Mr. Dith Tina, Minister of Agriculture and owner of Kiri Sour Dairy Farm in Bati District, Takeo Province, encouraged farmers around the area to grow grass and corn to supply their farms. To make a profit, the farm plans to expand production and breeding to 3,000 dairy cows by 2025.
During a visit to Kiri Sour Farm on February 24, 2023, Mr. Dith Tina noted that the people around Kiri Sour Dairy Farm have many opportunities to benefit from the dairy farm. The largest dairy in Cambodia, using the latest technology, by planting grass to supply the farm and learning the techniques of raising dairy cows in the future.
"Actually, when we go in to check together and study the different needs, we find an opportunity to benefit from this collaboration," he said. "We no longer have land concessions for companies, but other farmers can also participate in the expansion of various production chains by contract farming and maintaining their own assets."
He recommended to the farm to diversify its production process to benefit the people in the surrounding area, the farm should expand the grassland to supply cattle feed by contracting with people with large plots of land.
He added that in the future, he will study where there is potential to visit people in the future to ask people to consider switching from rice to grass, which can be more profitable. But the important thing ahead is to build the confidence of farmers first.
Mr. Chi Sela, co-founder of Kiri Farm, said that if the area where rice is not good should be turned to planting grass because weeds are easy to grow and planted once for up to 5 years, harvested six times a year. Low planting and maintenance costs are also lower.
He said that in the past, he also met with a community in Prey Kabbas district with 800 members to try to cooperate with this community.
According to the farm owner, in the future, he plans to expand to 3,000 dairy cows by 2025 to expand production and supply of various products in the market.
Kiri Sour Dairy Farm, located in Ophasaing Village, Kandeung Commune, Bati District, Takeo Province, has been operating for more than 4 years, from the beginning of construction to the first drop of milk.
In 2020, more than 500 head of cattle raised on the Kirisour farm were airlifted from Australia. To date, cows have produced offspring up to the third generation, bringing the total to more than 1,000.
In one day, Kiri Sour Farm produces about 12,000 to 15,000 liters of fresh milk to meet the growing demand. The farm also sells and distributes its products, including fresh milk and various flavors of yoghurt, in a few thousand supermarkets. Only 69 days left! Cambodia to host 32nd SEA Games
