Cambodia, Thailand vow to continue multi-sectoral partnership for peace and prosperity (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, concludes official visit to Thailand On February 24, 2023, at the invitation of Mr. Don Pramat Vinay, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs of Thailand.
According to a Foreign Ministry statement obtained by Fresh News, the two Deputy Prime Ministers discussed extensively, reviewing and launching new measures for multilateral cooperation for growth and prosperity. Joint between the two countries, including trade and investment, education, tourism, employment, connectivity, security and defense.
Deputy Prime Minister Don Pramat Vinay confirmed the continuation of Thailand's cooperation in the field of education, including the provision of scholarships to Cambodia through the Thai International Cooperation Agency (TICA). In the field of tourism, the two sides agreed to further enhance cooperation in line with the slogan "Two Kingdoms, One Goal" and encourage border provincial authorities to jointly organize events to promote and facilitate the flow of tourism between the two countries.
During the visit, Mr. Prak Sokhon paid a courtesy call on the Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Thailand, General Prayuth Chan Ocha, on which he praised the good relations between the two countries in all fields. And close cooperation between the two Ministries of Foreign Affairs.
The Thai Prime Minister stressed the need for better cooperation and mutual support between the two countries' relevant authorities for the common benefit of the two peoples as well as for peace and development along the border, including The opening of international border crossings at necessary locations and the demining process in border areas.
