The Ministry of Public Works and Administration of Kampong Cham Province continues to seek solutions to some of the impacts of the project to expand National Road 7 from Skun to Kizuna Bridge.
(Kampong Cham): The Ministry of Public Works and Transport and Kampong Cham Provincial Administration on the morning of February 24, 2023, continued to meet to find solutions to the impact of the project to expand National Road No. 7 from Skun to Kizuna Bridge with companies and relevant units. . The meeting was chaired by Mr. Lim Sidenin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, and Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham Province.
In relation to the above road construction project, according to CRBC's study, there are 4 areas with very complex impacts, including:
* First: Located in Skun town, Cheung Prey district, which has a large number of complex impacts and is very complex * Second: Located in Prey Chhor district around the intersection and Street 60 * Third: Located in Kampong Siem district * 4th: Located in Kampong Cham city.
According to the CRBC representative, the National Road No. 7 project is a project to expand and improve the quality of roads from two lanes to four lanes, which is currently in the preparation stage and the project will officially start construction on November 1. 2023. Impact management and other preparation work are important factors that determine whether a company can start construction as planned and carry out large-scale work.
Depending on the urban situation, the project line is very complex and complex, which is a major factor influencing the overall progress of the project. Therefore, in order to ensure the smooth construction as planned after the upcoming rainy season in 2023, the leaders are kindly requested to facilitate and promote the successful work to build the National Road 7 project with high standards and quality.
