Senior Minister Kun Kim praised and commended the Special Forces Command for its hard work in rescuing disasters in the past.
Senior Minister Kun Kim added that the installation of technical equipment at this time is a consideration of Samdech Techo Hun Sen in strengthening the capacity of the rescue team in the event of disasters such as building collapses, natural disasters and other incidents. Both on land, on water and in the air.
The senior minister reminded the disaster relief trainees that disaster relief operations are a battle that requires the highest level of commitment for rescue workers.
Senior Minister Kun Kim added that the lives of the victims in the incidents are the main goals that all rescuers must pay close attention to. The Cambodian Microfinance Association promotes access to financing for water and sanitation services for small and medium enterprises and the general population.
According to the Cambodian Microfinance Association, this partnership aims to strengthen the capacity of Cambodian Microfinance Association members to develop and provide clean water and sanitation credit products to their clients in order to improve the financial environment. Objects and will improve access to clean water and sanitation services in Cambodia.
Lack of clean water and sanitation is a major problem in Cambodia, especially in rural areas. To address this, the collaboration between the Cambodian Microfinance Association and Water.org will focus on building the capacity of member associations to implement clean water credit development programs, in which participating financial institutions will receive Technical assistance in the development and improvement of financial products for water and sanitation.
The implementation of the Water Credit Development Program will also help MFIs to retain their clients and the quality of loans by ensuring business sustainability that supports the development of a sustainable and responsible financial sector. Yes.
