(Phnom Penh): Wing Bank (Cambodia) CCHR on February 24, 2024 inaugurated its newest branch in Royal Group Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone under the chairmanship of Mr. Rath Sovannarak, Deputy Governor and Superintendent of National Bank. Of Cambodia Neak Oknha Kith Meng, Chairman of the Board of Directors of Wing Bank and CEO of Royal Group, as well as many other dignitaries.
To celebrate the opening of this new branch, Wing Bank has launched a special payroll service that allows all employer customers to access the payroll program through Wing Bank's iBanking system for free.
All employees can also withdraw their salary from Wing Agent, Bank Branch, Head Office and Wing Bank ATMs nationwide for free.
Both employers and employees are entitled to a digital loan without collateral, while Wing Bank also offers reasonable interest rates for savings accounts. In addition, customers with a payroll account can apply for a free Wing Visa credit and debit card for the first year.
Han Peng Kwang, CEO of Wing Bank, said: “Royal Group Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone is a major hub for international companies in Cambodia. "We have developed many products as well as services to meet the needs of our customers here."
Following the inauguration of its commercial banking license, Wing Bank has expanded its banking network to nine strategic locations in addition to its headquarters on Monivong Boulevard in Phnom Penh's Boeung Keng Kang III district.
In 2022, Wing Bank opened Sen Sok Branch, Wat Phnom Branch, Toul Kork Branch, Boeung Trabek Branch and Preah Yukunthor Branch, all of which are located in Phnom Penh and the other branch is in Sihanoukville. Last month, Wing Bank just inaugurated another branch in Battambang.
Wing Bank Royal Group Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone Branch also has the same features as other Wing Bank branches, offering a full range of banking products and services such as: Deposit, Business Loan, Money Transfer and more. More.
All Wing Bank branches are beautifully designed with ample parking, comfortable waiting area, delicious cafés and luxurious meeting rooms. Wing Bank has highly professional staff and is ready to serve customers.
The newly launched Wing Bank is located in the Royal Group Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone, located along National Road 4, next to the Toyota Transport and Training Center.
Wing Bank Royal Group Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone Branch offers a full range of banking services and welcomes customers from 8am to 5pm and Monday to Sunday, with all customers able to use leading financial products and services. Many, even on weekends.
Wing Bank Royal Group Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone is equipped with modern ATMs where customers can withdraw money at any time for free.
Preah Sihanouk Provincial Road Traffic Police Increase Inspection and Fines for Users of All Types of Vehicles Who Do Not Wear Helmets and Do Not Wear Belts Day and Night
(Preah Sihanouk): By order of Major General Chuon Narin, Preah Sihanouk Provincial Police Commissioner, the traffic police force led by Mr. Kim Song, Director of the Road Traffic Police Office of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Police continued to increase inspections and fines. Exemption for motorcyclists not wearing helmets or drivers of all kinds of vehicles violating the law both day and night on the night of February 23, 2023.
The move comes after the Sihanoukville provincial administration, led by Kouch Chamroeun, chairman of the Sihanoukville Provincial Administrative Unity Command, launched a campaign using all activities to prevent a series of road accidents that resulted in deaths and injuries. The fatal victim was a motorcyclist who was not wearing a helmet.
Observations show that the travel conditions of some people in the province, most do not respect the law while driving, especially motorcyclists, including allowing young children to ride a motorcycle three to four people. Which are all challenges and dangers.
To put an end to any suspicion, the authorities call on citizens and schools to educate their children or students to ride motorcycles, wear helmets and drive vehicles at all times.
