We must all work together to eradicate the tragedy of landmines, cluster munitions, and explosive remnants of war from Cambodia and the world. Education to reduce the risk of landmines and unexploded ordnance is our role. Boundary dispute in Rattanak Mondul district, Battambang province
(Battambang): The border issue of the people in Rattanak Mondul district, Battambang province, after receiving the order of Mr. Sok Lou, the governor of that province, on the morning of February 24, 2023, all relevant officials went to measure the actual conflict. .
Today's survey was led by Mr. Yim Sieb, Deputy Governor, with the participation of provincial hall officials, provincial cadastral officers, district governors, district chiefs, commune chiefs, forces, village chiefs and many other stakeholders.
Officials who visited the site said that after the measurement and coordination from the relevant officials, the two sides have a lot of understanding that may reach a settlement soon. The official added that the two sides will be scheduled to meet for further talks on March 2, 2023 at the provincial hall to continue to resolve.
Please be reminded that Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Battambang Province, on the evening of February 21, 2023, ordered a Deputy Provincial Governor to inspect immediately after receiving information that the Governor of Rattanak Mondul District, Mr. Kuy Vanno, did not solve the land issue for the villagers. Omlon, Phum Meas commune, Rattanak Mondul district, Battambang province, even used inappropriate words against them.
As there was no such solution, the couple went to the Rattanak Mondul district hall with their plots, then helped the district official to tell the story, but the district official pushed him away. Complain at the provincial hall.
According to the couple, they were willing to open the road in their land so that the party with the land at the back could travel in and out, but the person with the land next to his border (the new owner) Build a fence to encroach on his land without questioning. Ukraine imposes 50-year sanctions on Russia's financial sector
(Kiev): The Ukrainian parliament on Thursday decided to impose sanctions for a total of 50 years on Russia's financial institutions, including the central bank, all commercial banks, investment companies, insurance companies and other enterprises. This was released by the AFP news agency on Friday, February 24, 2023.
Andriy Pyshniy, Governor-General of the National Bank of Ukraine, said: "It is a complete ban on the financial institutions of the Russian Federation from entering the market or using assets in Ukraine. We should weaken Russia by all possible means. "This financial sector is a strategic source of supply for the Russian war in Ukraine."
Arrest and detention of a high school deputy director in Kampong Tralach district in connection with the distribution of pornographic images and violence
(Kampong Chhnang): A deputy high school principal in Kampong Tralach district, Kampong Chhnang province, was arrested by the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Police and sent to the provincial court for legal action in connection with the distribution of pornographic images and violence.
Ms. Soda, Director of the Anti-Human Trafficking and Protection of Minors Office of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Police, told Fresh News this morning, February 24, 2023, that the arrest of the high school deputy director took place after the authorities received Complaint from the victim's family alleging that Nget Sok Kheng, 40, (high school deputy principal) raped his 15-year-old daughter on February 16, 2023.
He said that after the search on February 21, 2023, the police summoned the suspect for questioning at the Police Inspectorate of Kampong Tralach District and with the coordination of the Prosecutor of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Court, the suspect was sent to Kampong Chhnang Provincial Police for further questioning and to build a case to be sent to Kampong Chhnang Provincial Court on February 22, 2023.
However, the deputy principal of the high school in front of the authorities has not yet confessed his guilt, which is likely to confirm that he did not act as charged.
