Cambodian-American stranger kills wife, escapes in Por Sen Chey
(Phnom Penh): A 68-year-old Cambodian-American foreigner took an electric shock, killed his wife, abandoned his two children and escaped on a motorcycle. This incident happened on the morning of February 24, 2023 in Borey KC, Chak Chrouk village, Sangkat Samrong Krom, Khan Por Sen Chey.
According to the victim's mother, she initially heard an argument between the victim and her husband, but after a while, the husband locked out and rode away on a motorcycle. Later, the victim's nephew entered the house and saw the victim sleeping in the bathroom, but thought he was unconscious, so he put it on the ferry and realized that he was dead and caused a surprise.
Colonel Mon Vuthy, police inspector of Por Senchey district, was seen at the scene leading a specialized force to inspect the scene and search for the suspect's husband. The motive for the murder is unknown.
