Ms. O Vandin calls on parents of students to bring their children to be vaccinated against Kovid 19 while the Ministry is in the process of vaccinating students in schools
(Siem Reap): Mrs. O Vandin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health and Chair of the Commission for the 19th Kovid Vaccination, called on parents and guardians of all students to bring their children to be vaccinated against Kovid 19 while the Ministry is The process of vaccinating students in schools and do not have to worry about the side effects of the 19 Kovid vaccine given to them.
At the same time, Ms. O Vandin said that now the Cambodian people are benefiting from the vaccination against Kovid 19, the vaccine has saved lives. The reason why we continue to inject the dose until the sixth dose is because the effectiveness of the vaccine does not last long, that is, only 6 to 8 months, the effectiveness of the vaccine will be reduced.
"Currently, Kovid 19 virus is not far away from us, so if an individual's immune system is weakened, it will make it easier for Kovid 19 virus to attack and get worse," she said. These are the factors that require parents of students to allow their children to receive the vaccine to encourage everyone.
