Today is the 44th anniversary of the reunion between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit with his son Hun Manet!
Samdech Techo Hun Sen recalled that he broke up with his wife on June 18, 1977, two days before he left to lead the struggle against Pol Pot on June 20, 1977.
Please be informed that on the 43rd anniversary of the reunion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen used to post a message telling the story after the reunion of his wife and son Hun Manet, which has the following content:
Manet had just weaned a few weeks before coming to see me. Rany told me that in the afternoon on the day of the ferry crossing Neak Leung on the way to Phnom Penh, Manet saw people selling Manet bread. I came to Phnom Penh with no money or anything to trade for this bread.
Manet, this poor child, just swallowed and looked at his mother who was shedding tears of pity for her child. After dinner and after learning about the bread on the Neak Leung ferry, I found about 10 candies to give to my children. Manet accepts but they throw him away because he does not know candy.
I peeled the candy and gave it to Manet, but he pushed my hand away when I ate the candy, only then did Manet realize that it was something to eat this time. Only nuts because I am afraid my child will have a fever. This is the taste of Pol Pot children who never had food or toys for children.
Please note that my wife and I have five children, never had a nurse, everything we have to do for ourselves for children. Since the story of the son under the full moon is being filmed, I hope that this episode can make some scenes as well.
This Morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Presides Over the Graduation Ceremony of More Than 7,000 Students of the Royal University of Phnom Penh
(Phnom Penh): On Friday morning, February 24, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the graduation ceremony for more than 7,000 students of the Royal University of Phnom Penh after their successful graduation.
Samdech Techo Prime Minister is a leader who pays high attention to education to cultivate human resources to contribute to building Cambodian society. Samdech Techo always takes the time to lead the country, to preside over or present diplomas to students who have graduated from various universities, both public and private.
The invitation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to confer degrees on students reflects the high level of concern for the education sector and encourages the leadership, professors, staff and all students of the Royal University of Phnom Penh to be warm. Climb further under the shadow of peace and development.
Currently, the Royal University of Phnom Penh is a public institution of administration that enables the university to have autonomy in administration, finance, and research. The University has five faculties and two institutes, including the Faculty of Science, the Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, the Faculty of Development Studies, the Faculty of Engineering, the Faculty of Education, the Institute of Foreign Languages, and the Institute of International Studies and Public Policy.
In the future, the university plans to open the "Institute of Environmental Studies", located at the Royal University of Phnom Penh, Mondul 3, near the Victory Monument, which the Royal Government has provided to the Royal University of Phnom Penh.
In addition to training students, the university cooperates with well-known foreign universities to improve the quality of training. For the academic year 2022-2023, the University has signed a Memorandum of Understanding with partner universities and other institutions, both local and foreign, a total of 239 to exchange students and professors with each other on academic work. Teaching, and research work.
At the same time, the university has encouraged and promoted research work from 2008 to the present. The University has published 305 international research articles, 40 local publications, and 86 articles in the Royal University Journal of Phnom Penh.
Since 2016, the university has provided about $ 100,000 annually to strengthen the research work of students and professors. In particular, in 2022, the university has completed 25 research projects and 19 research projects are underway.
The University participates in a number of social programs such as charitable activities, the Red Cross, and community services by sending young people to participate in social activities, donating blood, training on traffic safety, eliminating domestic violence, and Angkor Sankranti program, etc.
In addition, the University operates major centers including: Cambodia-Japan Cooperation Center, Cambodia-Korea Cooperation Center, Cambodia-Japan Digital Production Center, Khmer Silk Center, and Stem Building. The Cambodia-Japan Digital Production Center was officially inaugurated in 2022 and has the role of training human resources in the field of digital production.
The Khmer Silk Center was officially inaugurated in 2019 and is responsible for researching her worms and producing silk threads, as well as distributing her worm eggs and teaching farmers how to raise her worms.
By the end of 2023, the building of the "National New Business Center of Cambodia" will be completed to establish a system to promote trade between universities and industry in Cambodia under a project supported by the Government of the Republic of Korea.
Currently, the Royal University of Phnom Penh is implementing two major projects: the Higher Education Improvement Project, which focuses on learning and teaching, research, and institutional strengthening, and the Swedish-Royal University of Phnom Penh Bilateral Project. Strengthening research capacity, and developing ICT infrastructure at the Royal University of Phnom Penh.
