Hundreds of foreign troops will train Ukrainian troops in Germany, Japan-Cambodia Kizuna Festival: Many Cambodians and Japanese have gained valuable experience in both traditional and modern forms of art.
The event was attended by Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, Mr. Takei Sunsuki, Deputy Minister of Foreign Affairs of Japan, Mr. Chan Ratana, Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, and Ms. Pen Monimara, Secretary of State Ministry of Culture and many other stakeholders.
Dr. Hang Chuon Naron said that since 2012, the Kizuna Festival has provided an opportunity for many Cambodians and Japanese to experience valuable traditional and modern forms of Khmer-Japanese art. Will benefit the audience and explore collaborative learning activities through art and creative arts.
We would like to express our full support and gratitude to "Kizuna Festival 2023" for its contribution to achieving the vision of Cambodia's economic development, strengthening our good relations and it has played a role in bringing Give us all people of diverse cultures, including Cambodian and Japanese students.
This year marks the 70th anniversary of Japan-Cambodia friendship. In the past 70 years, the two countries' strong ties have developed through cooperation in the search process. Peace in Cambodia, National Reconstruction and Socio-Economic Development of Cambodia.
Mr. Takeshi Sunsuki added that recently, Cambodia's remarkable development in the field of economy and infrastructure attracted many Japanese investors, our potential areas of cooperation are being continuously expanded.
Mr. Chan Ratana pointed out that the Kizuna Festival is an annual special event organized since 1992, which includes activities such as cultural performances, exhibitions and workshops.
Mr. Chan Ratana said that the festival has played an important role in encouraging and promoting people-to-people exchanges in the fields of culture and education, as well as the trust and mutual understanding of our two peoples. .
In particular, Ms. Pen Mony Makara said that in 2023, the bilateral relations between the two countries will be deepened, shifting from a strategic partnership to a comprehensive strategic partnership, and people-to-people exchanges. Between the two countries will be further enhanced.
She said that in the past 70 years, the two countries have gone through a lot of common history and have helped each other in all forms to bring back peace, development and prosperity of great benefit. For the people of our two countries. Cambodia and Japan have good relations, good friends who helped each other in difficult times.
Please be informed that the 12th Japan-Cambodia Kizuna Festival was held at CJCC from 23rd to 26th February 2023 with the aim of showcasing Japanese and Cambodian culture as well as helping people to better understand the culture. Cambodia and Japan by participating in various programs in this festival. Tomorrow morning, Samdech Techo Presides Over the Graduation Ceremony of More Than 7,000 Students of the Royal University of Phnom Penh
