Washington: US President Joe Biden has left Poland, but the remnants of the urging of Ukraine to fight to defeat Russia remain in Ukraine's determination. Russian leader Vladimir Putin has also vowed to escalate the war game, which extends into the second year.
The war in Ukraine has clearly revealed who is at war with whom? On the eve of the one-year anniversary of the war, US President Joe Biden held a large rally in Poland, urging Ukraine to fight for victory over Russia.
"I just heard our top military commander say there was an attack," said Russian leader Vladimir Putin in front of an audience of 75,000 who cheered for Putin's presence. Working for our people È. Putin has made it clear that Russian forces are backed by Russian citizens across the country, and that those gathered here are defenders of Russia's homeland.
He thanked the team for gathering in the stadium at this time to support the Russian troops. Vladimir Putin thanked the children for writing their respective letters in support of the Russian military. He told the participants in the stadium that Russia's fight was for the benefit of the nation, its people, its language, its culture and its territory.
"Everyone is a citizen who defends Russian territory and we thank you all from the bottom of our hearts," Putin said as the crowd chanted "Russia, Russia".
Russia considers its battles now like those of the past, the patriotic war of Nazi Germany. Putin said the conflict was caused by the United States and the West using Kiev as a stepping stone to overthrow Russia.
During one year of war in Ukraine, the United States and the West provided billions of dollars in military and economic aid to Ukraine, while Ukraine, which is committed to defending its waters against Russia, used those aid to work. Resist the attack on Russia.
In 2022, Russia declared four eastern territories, Luhansk, Donetsk, Zaporizia and Kherson, to be occupied by Russia, and all four were under strong Russian protection. Some of the four territories were recaptured by Ukrainian forces and some areas were in a state of conflict.
By 2023, Ukraine, which is preparing military equipment, modern weapons of US and Western aid, is ready to launch a campaign to liberate the four provinces. Ukraine's liberation campaign is expected to take place in the coming spring, but battle reports say Russia has launched a campaign to seize the remaining four territories ahead of its large-scale offensive. Ukraine.
Days before the one-year anniversary of the war in Ukraine, the United States and NATO member states met to pledge continued military and economic assistance to Ukraine, which is preparing for a final battle with Russian troops.
East Asia. In addition to deploying Western-backed special forces, Ukraine has proposed equipping US advanced aircraft, such as the F16, and long-range rocket launchers.
"Because his nine countries are the eastern wing of NATO, his country is at the forefront of our common defense," said Biden. "His nine countries know better than anyone in the conflict that we are working not only for Ukraine, but for the freedom of democracy throughout Europe and around the world."
Putin spoke at the outset on economic ties between the two countries. Putin has called for greater trade between Russia and China in the future. Putin said that relations between Russia and China are progressing well as planned and that the two countries have already achieved a lot.
The talks highlighted the good diplomatic relations between the two countries and moved them into a more complex global situation.
Putin stressed that China-Russia cooperation in the international arena is important to stabilize the international situation, and that Russia and China still have a lot of work to do. He said he was looking forward to Chinese President Xi Jinping's visit to Russia.
In the run-up to the 2023 war in Ukraine, the United States and the West have been increasingly concerned about reports that China could intervene to supply arms to Russia amid speculation that a war in Ukraine could escalate. With the help of China, the picture of the hopes of the United States and the West, which wants Russia to lose the war, may be in a different state.
China has denied US allegations that China provided arms to Russia.
The Chinese Foreign Ministry has said that it is the United States itself that is rushing to provide weapons to continue the war in Ukraine, and that the United States does not deserve to bring these allegations to China. .
