Key Remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen Presiding over the Graduation Ceremony for More Than 7,000 Students of the Royal University of Phnom Penh
(Phnom Penh): On Friday morning, February 24, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the graduation ceremony for more than 7,000 students of the Royal University of Phnom Penh after their successful graduation.
On the occasion of Samdech Techo Hun Sen giving a speech for more than an hour, the following are the main contents of Samdech Techo:
* As the beginning of the conversation, Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded that there are only 70 days left until the SEA Games and Para Games, which Cambodia is hosting.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his congratulations to the Cambodian students who graduated and received their degrees today. Samdech Techo considered today's graduates as an important achievement for the nation and the people of Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that this achievement was not an accident or by an angel, but an achievement born of the thinking and efforts of the entire Cambodian nation.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal University of Phnom Penh is still a university that plays an important role in training human resources.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls for strengthening the quality of education. It is not possible to have only training with a degree and no quality.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the opposition group studied under the roof of the Khmer school until they gained knowledge, but instead degraded the training in Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded graduates to continue their studies. Samdech Techo stated that stagnation is equivalent to going backwards or conservative, which is an obstacle to the development process.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that refusing to learn, refusing to understand technology will become an obstacle for work.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the economic growth of Thailand and Vietnam is good for the Cambodian economy.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructed the Minister of Education to talk with Laos to provide scholarships to students in dollars in response to changes in exchange rates.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces an increase of allowance to Samdech's library at the Royal University of Phnom Penh 10 million Riels per month from March 2023.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen wondered that the opposition always said that Samdech did not know, but could not defeat Samdech.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen denies the accusation and demeans Samdech that Samdech pushes his mother and Samdech is the last survivor of his mother.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen confirms that when Samdech's mother fell and broke her bone, Samdech was in Vietnam. Samdech Techo confirmed that Samdech's mother broke her bone due to the shelling on July 6-7, 1997.
