On that occasion, Mr. Tim Seang Leng, Deputy Governor of Chhlong District, warmly welcomed the presence of all development partners, as well as KOICA, Coffee Doc and Chalfan Cambodia, who have been actively caring and contributing. With the Royal Government and the authorities to promote education, which is one of the main priorities of the Royal Government of the 6th legislature.
He added that human resource development is a priority for "Kayaka" and considered education as the highest priority area in the policy for sustainable development in Cambodia under the slogan "Do not leave anyone And even though we all suffered from the Kovid 19 outbreak in 2020, we can still contribute to reducing the dropout rate of children in Chhlong district in the first phase of the project.
Mr. Prasan Verma also expressed his hope that this second phase project will continue to provide children in Chhlong district with the pleasure of learning and continue to provide them with a safe and quality education environment.
The Ministry of Economy presents the results of the 2022 Annual Review Meeting on the Implementation of the Third Phase of Public Financial Management Reform Program
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance on 22 February 2023 held the annual meeting of 2022 of "Implementation of Public Financial Management Reform Program Phase 3" with the participation of the General Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance, and Chairman of the Steering Committee for Public Financial Management Reform.
This is according to the press release of the Ministry of Economy and Finance on February 23, 2023.
In this sacred perspective, the public financial management system is being gradually and deepened to cover all the core components of public financial management by building and improving the system, legal framework, institutionalization and human resources.
In fact, during the last three years of the Kovid Crisis 19, the Royal Government has had sufficient funds to support the implementation of policies and interventions to help stabilize the living standards of the people as well as to stabilize the private sector business that has been Continue to be affected by the Kovid-19 crisis.
