Ms. Ban Srey Mom: Pailin Provincial Administration plays an important role in finding markets for farmers (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Ms. Ban Srey Mom, Pailin Provincial Governor, said that in addition to helping farmers in Pailin directly find markets Facilitate finding markets for all people across the country as Pailin is a province with potential for agricultural output and exports.
Ms. Ban Srey Mom made this statement at a press conference on "Five Years of Success of Pailin Provincial Administration" at the Office of the Council of Ministers, organized by the Government Spokesperson's Unit on February 23, 2023.
She added that the Pailin provincial administration has played an important role in facilitating market access for all people across the country, not just Pailin. In fact, mango growers with some provinces such as Kampong Speu also bring turmeric to sell in Pailin.
She added that despite the Royal Government and the provincial administration trying to find markets for farmers, there are still people taking advantage of farmers, especially mangoes and lentils, with brokers entering into contracts to buy from farmers at below-market prices. Collect, buy. However, the provincial administration and professional officials set out measures to help farmers to the best of their ability to avoid losing the interests of the people.
"Obviously, some of the plantation owners have contacted us, and when we did, we acted as facilitators to get the company in touch with the plantation owners," she said.
Ms. Ban Srey Mom said that at the same time, the Pailin provincial administration also played a coordinating role in finding jobs for all people without having to migrate. Every day, people contact to find jobs, while many factories in Pailin province are in need of manpower.
Please be informed that Pailin Province has 54 silos for buying agricultural products from people all over the province for storage and export. At the same time, Pailin province has an international border gate that can facilitate the exchange of agricultural products between the people of the two countries, Cambodia - Thailand.
(Prey Veng): Ms. Youk Sambath, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Health, on February 23, 2023, led a working group of the Ministry of Health and veterinary officials and local authorities to Roleang village, Romlech commune, Sithor Kandal district, Prey Veng province. A girl died of H5N1 bird flu to educate villagers on how to prevent the spread of bird flu.
Ms. Youk Sambath stated that during the campaign, the working group of the Ministry of Health and local authorities have posted various cards on how to prevent the spread of bird flu, and if there is a case of fever, people should be tested immediately. Also.
"As of the afternoon of February 23, 2023, no villagers have been diagnosed with bird flu, but doctors are still on duty in the village," she said. "People's commune, if people have any doubts, doctors will test immediately."
During the outreach campaign, Ms. Youk Sambath also brought 2 million Riels from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to the funeral of the girl who died of H5N1 bird flu and shared her condolences. Sadly with the family of the deceased.
An 11-year-old 6-month-old girl from Roleang village, Romlech commune, Sithor Kandal district, Prey Veng province, died after being diagnosed with H5N1 bird flu.
The girl became ill on February 16, 2023, with a fever of 39 degrees Celsius, coughing and sore throat. After three days of treatment, the girl became tired and was sent to the National Children's Hospital in Phnom Penh.
Doctors sent the item to the National Institute of Public Health and received the results on February 22, 2023, confirming that there was a positive H5N1 bird flu virus, while the girl died. Ministry of Health issues official press release on the first case of bird flu in humans in Cambodia
