(Phnom Penh): Mr. Prach Chan, Chairman of the National Election Committee (NEC), commented on the question of the German parliamentary delegation on the right to stand for election and whether the NEC How did you prepare for the upcoming election?
Mr. Prach Chan said that the election calendar, master plan and regulations and procedures for the election are ready. The regulations and procedures involve the input of all parties involved in the election before the NEC approves them.
Mr. Prach Chan continued that the election in Cambodia has four major stages:
First, the examination of the voter list and voter registration. The 2022 voter list and voter registration has been completed, with more than 9 million registered voters. Only those whose names are on the official voter list are eligible to vote.
Second: Registration of candidates of political parties. Political parties that are legally registered as political parties at the Ministry of Interior have the right to contest the election. So far, there are 46 political parties legally registered with the Ministry of Interior. The registration of political parties and the list of candidates must follow the rules and procedures of the NEC.
Third: Election campaign. In connection with the election campaign, political parties have the right to conduct various types of election campaigns, such as four public campaign marches, and the right to campaign at home. On the other hand, political parties have the right to campaign equally on state media, where the program is organized by the NEC. In general, political parties have the right to organize their propaganda programs according to the party's capabilities.
The Speaker of the German Federal Parliament also thanked NEC Chairman Prach Chan for taking the time to meet with the German parliamentary delegation.
