China expects strong tourism recovery this year
BEIJING (Reuters) - China expects its tourism market to rebound this year, beginning with a busy summer tourist season as tourists flock to the resort after the government ended a closed Kowidz zero policy. Block people in the house for almost 3 years. According to Reuters.
The number of domestic tourists is expected to reach 4.55 billion by 2023, an increase of 80% compared to 2022, as the number of inbound and outbound tourists is seen to be higher. 90 million people, double the number from 2022 and up to 31.5 percent of the pre-epidemic level.
"The tourism market is expected to recover strongly in the second quarter and summer vacation is expected to lead to a full recovery," the report said.
Travel providers were severely affected during the epidemic. After China lifted its strict anti-Kovid-19 policy, travel across the country increased, especially during the Chinese New Year, which saw an increase in travel. According to Reuters.
