Ms. Youk Sambath, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, told Fresh News that the girl started to get sick on February 16, 2023, with a fever of 39 degrees Celsius, coughing and sore throat. After three days of unrelenting treatment, the girl became exhausted and was sent to the National Children's Hospital in Phnom Penh.
Ms. Youk Sambath said that on February 21, 2023, the doctor took the item to the National Institute of Public Health and received the results on February 22, 2023, confirming that there was a positive H5N1 bird flu virus, while the girl died. Hei performs a traditional funeral in Khang Ley village.
Ms. Youk Sambath, according to sources from the villagers, confirmed that before the outbreak in the conservation lake near the village, there was an abnormal death of wild animals. After the incident, the veterinarian took the analysis on February 17, 2023 and is waiting for the results from the veterinary laboratory.
According to Ms. Youk Sambath, after finding out the case of bird flu, the Ministry of Health's emergency response team worked closely with the veterinary team to investigate and find sources of transmission in both animals and humans, to find suspected cases and those affected. Take steps to prevent transmission to others, both in the community and at festivals. In addition, the emergency response team took action to educate the people.
Ms. Youk Sambath called on the villagers to find the bird flu to pay attention to health, especially not to eat dead animals.
