BEIJING, Feb. 21 (Xinhua) - China officially released a document on the Global Security Initiative on February 21. "This is a document that has received a great deal of attention from the world because it defines the core perspectives of the Global Security Initiative and outlines 20 major cooperation directions." A more detailed roadmap for implementing this initiative.
Over the years, the international community has become increasingly aware that the world is becoming more chaotic and insecure. In particular, the Ukraine crisis, which erupted in early 2022, has left millions of refugees homeless and has had a profound effect on global food and energy supplies.
Security is the right of all countries in the world, but not the exclusive property of some countries. To make the world safer, all countries have a responsibility. The Chinese side expects the parties to jointly participate in global security initiatives to bring more peace and tranquility to the world.
