The Commander of the Land Forces highlighted this during the ceremony of announcing the appointment and change of positions and rank of officers of the Takeo Military Operation Area this morning, February 22, 2023.
Mr. HUN Manet recalled that in connection with the appointment of military officers in the Army, he had been advised to make a voluntary decision to relocate people without going through any complicated procedures or evaluations. . The ground commander confirmed that he could follow the advice, but he never did.
"No one in the world is perfect," said Dr. Hun Manet. Choosing People We cannot find perfect or perfect people. But appointments need an evaluation to ensure fair effect. That assessment must be based on as many angles as possible. Therefore, all work is based on three main principles: first, justice, second, transparency, and third, to uphold common interests.
Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, a military leader who graduated from the US Military Academy, also explained in detail the three principles that apply to military management.
1. Principles of Justice: Mr. Hun Manet explained that the principle of justice is to give priority to individuals who are willing to work and be honest, seniority, ability, responsibility, virtue, morality and leadership, and the main priority is the locals. Outsiders are the next priority and falling from the sky is not easy. The appointment of people outside the unit, except in the unit can not be selected.
3. Principles of the common interests of the unit: The lieutenant general emphasized that providing justice and transparency to individuals is important, but considering the common interests of the organization is a priority over individual interests.
The Commander-in-Chief added that appointments based on common interests should be based on three additional principles, including: internal unity, the efficiency of the unit and the need to do things for the common good.
It should be noted that Lt. Gen. Hun Manet is noted as an army leader who has made many reforms to bring order in the army. Especially after he came to lead the army.
Duke Kith Meng pays courtesy call on Chinese Council for Promotion and International Trade of Hainan Province
On this occasion, a Memorandum of Understanding was signed between the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and the Chinese Council for the Promotion and International Trade of Hainan Province in order to accelerate economic cooperation and increase the scope of trade exchanges between Cambodia and Hainan Province. China.
The President warmly welcomed the visit of the Hainan Provincial delegation to Cambodia on the occasion of the 65th anniversary of Cambodia-China diplomatic relations. The duke highlighted the excellent relations between the two countries in all fields and invited Hainan investors to study, explore and explore investment opportunities in Cambodia.
In recent years, the volume of Cambodia-China trade has steadily increased, exceeding the target set by the governments of the two countries. As for direct investment, China has invested in key sectors such as garments, construction, mining, energy, agriculture and tourism.
The Prime Minister informed the delegation of Hainan Province about the official visit of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, from February 9 to 11, 2023 in the People's Republic of China, and the two governments agreed to establish The Diamond Cooperation Framework focuses on six priority areas: political cooperation, quality and production capacity, agriculture, energy, security and people-to-people exchanges.
Neak Oknha Kith Meng emphasized that the new cooperation framework, along with existing mechanisms such as the Cambodia-China Bilateral Free Trade Agreement, the Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement, the Belt and Road Initiative, and the Mekong-Lanchang Real Cooperation. As providing more business opportunities for the private sector.
On that occasion, the President shared the potential of trade and economic growth that makes Cambodia a land of opportunity and invited Hainan businessmen to visit Cambodia. The duke will lead a Cambodian business delegation to visit Hainan in May.
Qin Honglang, Vice Chairman of the Chinese Council for the Promotion and International Trade of Hainan Province, thanked Duke Kith Meng for warmly welcomed the Chinese delegation to Hainan Province and organized this important meeting. Really contribute to the strengthening of relations between the two institutions and business relations between Cambodia and Hainan Province.
He stressed that the current visit of the Hainan delegation is the first in three years and Cambodia is the first country that the Hainan delegation visited. This proves that Cambodia is a priority country for the Hainan delegation. He also shared the potential of Hainan Free Trade Port as a gateway for overseas investment that will further strengthen export-import volume as well as tourism.
He invited Duke Kith Meng to lead a delegation from the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce to participate in the following major events: the 8th East Asia Business Forum, the 2nd China International Golf and Tourism Fair (Hainan), and the 3rd Promotion Week. China International Innovation Design and 4: China International Maritime Industry Fair. The meeting was held successfully in a friendly atmosphere as a brotherhood.
