Ukraine wants to extend its grain export agreement for another year, including new ports
Ukraine will ask Turkey and the United Nations to begin talks this week on renewing the Black Sea grain agreement, seeking to extend it by at least one, a senior Ukrainian official said on Wednesday. Another year, which also includes the port of Mykolaev. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Wednesday, February 22, 2023.
In July last year, the Black Sea Grain Agreement Initiative, coordinated by the United Nations and Turkey, allowed grain exports from three Ukrainian ports. The agreement was renewed in November and will expire on March 18 if there is no further expansion.
Ukraine has repeatedly accused Russia of delaying inspections of ships carrying Ukrainian agricultural products, causing a drop in shipments and losses for traders. But Russia has denied the allegations, saying it has fulfilled all obligations under the grain export agreement. Ms. Youk Sambath Closes the Meeting to Summarize the Work Results and Proceedings of the National Center for Malaria Control
(Preah Sihanouk): Dr. Yok Sambath, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Health, on the afternoon of February 22, 2023, closed the meeting to review the work results of 2022 and the work direction of 2023 of the National Center for Parasitic Malaria. And lectures held at Sokha Hotel, Sihanoukville.
"Cambodia has achieved great success in achieving the National Malaria Eradication Strategic Plan, which we are almost five years ahead of our ASEAN goals," said the Permanent Secretary.
She said that the successful results were due to the participation of all relevant ministries, local authorities, park rangers, armed forces, support organizations, especially the participation of the people.
"We have been very successful in eradicating malaria, but we must continue to work together to prevent a recurrence of malaria, and we must take good care of our achievements," she said.
Therefore, the Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Health called on the relevant institutions to continue to educate people to be more aware of their protection when entering the forest.
At the same time, Dr. Youk Sambath encouraged and continued to support the National Center for Malaria Control, Parasitology and Bacteriology in achieving complete eradication of malaria by 2025.
In particular, Cambodia will be completely eradicated from malaria by 2025, an initiative and direct approval by the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who is an outstanding national guide in the national way to ensure peace. Full political stability and development of the country, in particular, always consider the promotion of public health as a priority to contribute to reducing poverty and social progress on a global scale.
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of February 21, 2023, Ms. Chhiv Phirum, Director of SVP Law Firm, led a group of lawyers of SVP Law Firm to introduce the first year students on "Sharing Life Experiences as "Law Students" and "Introduction to the Outstanding Law Students Program, HE Ly Chantola."
The lecture was held at the Royal University of Law and Economics, with the participation of nearly 400 first-year law students.
Ms. Chhiv Phirum led a group of lawyers, including: Heng Chanveasna, Cheng Khemara, You Lim Huot, Seng Leng Hong, Mey Usaphea, Neou Socheata, Yim Socheata and Dolin Phany Reach. To share experiences under a number of topics with a single common meaning is to share life experiences as a student.
Taking this valuable opportunity, Ms. Chhiv Phirum introduced the "Outstanding Law Student Program HE Ly Chantola" in order to recruit first year law students to attend this program to provide additional instruction as a classroom instruction and as a follow-up. Direct employment period for law students who are selected to enroll.
The program lasts only 4 years and aims to hold the hands of law students in his studies at the university and make him more capable for a real and effective career in the future. What is special is that this program is free of charge for students.
It should also be noted that the "Outstanding Law Student Program, HE Ly Chantola" has already selected the first generation of students in 2022, which has 39 students.
The war of words between US and Russian leaders erupted on the eve of the one-year anniversary of the war in Ukraine. This week, Biden visited Kiev with a commitment to continue supporting the Ukrainian cause against Russia. The United States has pledged to continue to provide indefinite military assistance, fueling the war to fuel Russia's defeat.
Joe Biden has said the West has no plans to attack Russia, as Vladimir Putin has said. He says millions of Russians are not enemies, they want to live in peace with their neighbors.
On the day of Biden's statement in Poland, Putin on February 21 also addressed an audience of about 1,400 in Moscow, including two parliamentarians, Russia's military commanders. And soldiers. The Russian president blamed the United States and the West for the war game and described Ukraine as a country being used as a slave to Western interests.
The war began on February 24, 2022. The United States and the West have devised a strategy to impose sanctions on Russia to slow the economic process, which is a major source of war funds. But in the past year, the report shows that Russia's economy has shrunk by only about 2 percent, while the plan that wants the Russian economy to shrink by as much as 12 percent.
Analysts say the West's plans did not cause Russia to collapse as expected.
One question is whether one has to talk to Putin or one has to run away from Putin, or, for example, France, which has a vague stance on Russia, despite its tendency to want Russia to lose the war. The European Union should engage with Russia, President Emmanuel Macron said this weekend.
Makrong stated that he wanted Russia to lose the war, but he wanted an end to the war through negotiation at the table, not on the battlefield.
However, in his speech on February 21, Putin called Western sanctions on Russia an "impossible failure". Putin has denounced the West by using gasoline to extinguish the flames of war in Ukraine. In front of many participants, Russian leaders reaffirmed the conclusion of the New Start Treaty with the United States.
As of Wednesday, the Ukrainian war has reached 363 days. This Friday marks the one-year anniversary of the Ukraine War. What will happen next that day, we will wait and see.
