Ms. Gabriel Casamarek remarked this while leading a German parliamentary delegation to pay a courtesy call and discuss work with Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the Peace Palace on Wednesday morning, February 22, 2023.
Gabriel Casamarek had already visited Cambodia in 2009. Returning to Cambodia now, she sees that Cambodia has developed and progressed a lot compared to 2009.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Personal Assistant to the Prime Minister, quoted Ms. Gabriel as saying, "Cambodia has a good economy and development everywhere. In particular, the people of Cambodia have benefited from this economic growth, everyone.
The Speaker of the German Parliament expressed her pleasure at Cambodia's great progress and paid tribute to the leadership of Samdech Techo Prime Minister.
In addition to noting Cambodia's progress, the German parliamentary group leader also paid tribute to Samdech Techo's position, as well as the Royal Government of Cambodia, on Russia's invasion of Ukraine.
In this meeting, Ms. Gabriel Casamarek also informed Samdech Techo about her intention to come to Cambodia now. She said the purpose of the German parliamentary delegation's visit to Cambodia now is to find a reliable cooperation partner and promote a free trade agreement between Europe and ASEAN.
Samdech Techo informed Ms. Gabriel, as well as the German parliamentary delegation, that Cambodia's decision against Russia's invasion of Ukraine was a clear position for Cambodia to maintain world order in accordance with international law.
At the same time, the Prime Minister welcomed Gabriel's goal of free trade between ASEAN and Europe.
Samdech Techo informed the chairperson of the delegation that the ASEAN Community is a community that implements decisions based on unanimous principles. In this sense, in order to promote a successful free trade agreement between ASEAN and Europe, it is necessary to look at the ASEAN community as a whole, not just the individual countries in the ASEAN community separately.
