Permanent Mission of Cambodia to the UN: Cambodia supports professional, accurate journalism, does not infringe on the rights of others and does not distort the truth (Video inside) (Geneva): The Permanent Mission of the Kingdom of Cambodia to the United Nations has released A statement affirming that Cambodia upholds the professional journalism, does not infringe on the rights of others and does not distort the truth.
The statement from the Permanent Mission of the Kingdom of Cambodia to the United Nations came after three Special Rapporteurs made biased and discriminatory comments regarding foreign-funded radio stations.
The Permanent Mission of the Kingdom of Cambodia expressed regret over the comments made by the three Special Rapporteurs. The Permanent Mission of the Kingdom of Cambodia clarified as follows:
1. Administrative action against entities that violate the law does not deserve any concern. What is worrying is the spread of false information and deliberate slander, which is always condemned by all countries. This press unit has been involved in disseminating false information and clarifying Cambodia's internal affairs on humanitarian assistance.
4. Claiming to be an "independent" newspaper is not a license to violate the law with impunity or to evade liability and accountability. Legal action against this unprofessional radio station does not undermine Cambodia's vibrant press freedom, but rather contributes to the strengthening of the journalistic profession.
