98 Cambodian Blue Hat Troops and 2 Hitmin Dogs Go on a Humanitarian Mission in Central Africa
(Phnom Penh): For the past 17 years, the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen has continued more than 8,000 Cambodian Blue Hat troops in peacekeeping missions under the United Nations umbrella in countries devastated by war and Chronic internal conflicts that have achieved a lot of prestige for the nation.
In fact, on the night of February 21, 2023, 98 members of the 98th Explosive Ordnance Disposal Squadron, including 10 women, along with 2 mines and improvised explosive devices, went on a peacekeeping mission under the umbrella of the organization. United Nations Central African Republic (MINUSCA).
The farewell ceremony for the Cambodian Blue Hat Army was presided over by General Sem Sovanny, Vice Chairman of the National Committee and Director General of the National Peacekeeping Center, as well as leaders of several national centers at Phnom Penh International Airport.
General Sem Sovanny stated that he reminded all forces to continue to unite as one and to consider safety first, especially during the performance of duties, not to underestimate any situation and to learn from experience and good lessons. Correct any mistakes that have occurred to achieve success for the motherland, family and yourself.
General Sem Sovanny continued that the peace operation is a global principle and has been playing an important role through the participation of all national and international circles, joint operations to help countries torn apart by armed conflict, fire, war and Join the Commonwealth in restoring peace, stability and development in line with UN principles aimed at building a path to a peaceful and prosperous world.
