Humanitarian donations provided include: 1 mosquito net, 1 blanket, 1 sarong, 1 scarf, 16 sheets of zinc, 30 kg of rice and 4 million riels. In that, the President's own budget is 3 million Riels and the branch budget is 1 million Riels). In addition, the participating philanthropists also donated some money. Putin announces suspension of nuclear deal with US, vows to continue fighting in Ukraine
MOSCOW (Reuters) - Russian President Vladimir Putin on Tuesday announced the suspension of Moscow's nuclear disarmament treaty with Washington in a speech he accused the West of escalating the conflict in Ukraine. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Tuesday, February 21, 2023.
Speaking in front of senior officials, political figures, members of parliament and military commanders of Russia's National Assembly, Putin also vowed that Russia would continue to fight in Ukraine as the war reaches its one-year anniversary on the 24th. This February.
The 2010 treaty is the latest major arms control agreement between the United States and Russia, which is still in force, but has fallen into disrepair in recent years, with Washington accusing it of failing to do so. Moscow that did not comply with it.
Putin, meanwhile, blamed the West for the tragedy of the Ukraine war. He also issued a warning to critics in Russia, saying "those who follow the path of Russian treason must be held accountable by law."
