Two men jailed for swindling nearly $ 700,000 from Taiwanese woman by selling more than 3 hectares of wind land
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Municipal Court has sentenced two Cambodian men to prison for swindling nearly $ 700,000 from a Taiwanese woman by selling more than three hectares of land. This verdict was announced by the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on February 20, 2023.
In that verdict, Ms. Say Srey Leak, Trial Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, sentenced the accused, Pov Sakhorn, to one year in prison, with only two months to serve, while all remaining sentences were suspended. . Suon Sophal, the ringleader, was sentenced to two years in prison.
The two Cambodians were involved in a scam involving nearly $ 700,000 from a Taiwanese investor in the form of selling more than three hectares of wind land in Srong commune, Kong Pisey district, Kampong Speu province during 2018.
In the verdict, the judge also ordered that the two defendants and another defendant, Chin Ri (who was sentenced by the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on November 15, 2022, suspended for one year) to be jointly paid $ 660,000. The United States will pay 40 million riels to the victim who is a plaintiff in this case. However, the judge paved the way for the accused to have the right to appeal to the Court of Appeal.
It should be noted that the defendants were represented by the prosecution on charges of fraud and forgery of documents (forgery of land sellers' thumbprints) under Articles 377, 378, 626 and 627 of the Penal Code and were arrested on November 16, 2022.
