Thai PM vows to dissolve parliament next month ahead of May general election
BANGKOK: Thai Prime Minister Prayuth Chan-o-cha on Tuesday announced that Thailand will hold new general elections in May after announcing the dissolution of parliament next month. This was released by the AFP news agency on Tuesday, February 21, 2023.
The popular Pheu Thai party is expected to nominate Thaksin Shinawatra, daughter of former Thai Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra, as its candidate for the 2023 general election. However, Thailand's current constitution, which has been amended under a military government, gives the military-affiliated parties an advantage.
Ms. Mithona Phu Thong: Koh Kong Province has 10 protected areas with a total area of more than 1 million hectares
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Mithona Phuthong, Governor of Koh Kong Province, through the press conference of the spokesperson of the Royal Government on the afternoon of February 21, 2023, said that in Koh Kong province, there are 10 protected areas with the area More than 1 million hectares.
The protected areas presented by the provincial governor include:
* First: The Southern Cardamom Mountain National Park was established by Sub-Decree No. 89 dated May 09, 2016. Covers 4 provinces: Koh Kong, Pursat, Kampong Speu and Sihanoukville with a total area of 410,392 hectares. Covers Koh Kong province with an area of 360,594 hectares.
* Third: Tatai Wildlife Sanctuary was established by Sub-Decree No. 80 dated May 09, 2016, covering 4 districts and 1 city of Koh Kong province: Koh Kong, Botum Sakor, Mondul Seima, Thmar Bang and Khemarak Phoumin. Total land is 144,275 hectares.
* Sixth: Botum Sakor National Park was established by Royal Decree dated November 1, 1993, covering three districts of Koh Kong Province: Kirisakor, Koh Kong and Botum Sakor with a total area of 171,250 hectares.
* Seventh: The multi-cup area was established by Royal Decree dated November 1, 1993, covering two districts of Koh Kong province: Sre Ambel and Botum Sakor, with a total area of 27,700 hectares.
8th: Peam Krasop Wildlife Sanctuary, 9th: Koh Kar Pi Ramsar site was established by Royal Decree dated 01 November 1993. Covers 2 districts and 1 city of Koh Kong province: Mondul Seima, Koh Kong and Khemarak Phoumin city with a total area of 23,750 hectares.
10th: Phnom Samkos Wildlife Sanctuary was established by Royal Decree dated November 1, 1993. Covers two provinces, Koh Kong and Pursat. Covers Koh Kong province, total land area 16,670 hectares.
