(Phnom Penh): Ms. Ing Kantha Phary, Minister of Women's Affairs and Chair of the Cambodian National Council for Women, said that in 2022, nearly 4,000 Cambodian women were helped to return to Cambodia. Among them, 226 women were trafficked and sexually exploited.
She stated this at the meeting to review the work in 2022 and work direction 2023 of the National Council of Cambodia for Women, chaired by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Honorary Vice President of the National Council of Cambodia for Women this morning. This is February 21, 2023.
Speaking at the ceremony, the Minister emphasized that in 2022, the relevant ministries and institutions have provided interventions for workers to work abroad, including: Continue to strengthen management and orient the company to send workers to work abroad by visiting Pre-departure education. The number of Cambodian workers who went abroad to work through private recruitment agencies and through the state and the state was 33,742, 13,005 women.
She said the ministry had intervened to help a total of 3,693 Cambodian women return to Cambodia, in collaboration with the competent authorities representing Cambodia abroad, the authorities of the target countries and cooperation partners.
