Here is the full video: Exporters say agricultural exports show strong growth earlier this year after China reopens
(Phnom Penh): Duke Hun Lak, CEO of Rich Farm Asia, an investment and exporter of agricultural products to international markets, said that the export of agricultural products to international markets, especially China, will improve this year. Than last year.
Tycoon Hun Lak expressed such optimism that the growth of agricultural exports to international markets, especially China, such as bananas, mangoes, Pailin, etc. has increased steadily.
He pointed out that the increase in agricultural exports was due to the reopening of China, which boosted demand, while shipping prices have now returned to normal after a high rise last year. .
According to the exporters of these agricultural products, in the first month of 2023, Cambodia exported more than 28,000 tons of fresh bananas, while more than 10,000 tons of mangoes and more than 1,000 tons of mango jam were exported.
"I think this year's agricultural exports may be better than last year," he said. "We look at the figure compared to last year better, but the percentage has not been calculated yet, but see better than last year because shipping costs from the end of the year down better compared to shipping costs in 2022." .
He said that after China reopened, it was hoped that exports of other products and goods would start to improve.
Mao Thunin, the governor of Kampot province, said recently that the yellow bananas grown in Kampot province were exported to international markets, especially the Chinese market, more than 2,000 tons per month.
He added that due to the good market for yellow bananas, two companies that invest in planting bananas in Kampot province on 1,063 hectares also plan to expand the cultivated area, while he will encourage the community and people in the area to grow crops. This is for export and domestic supply as well.
