100 Most Vulnerable Poor Families Living in Remote Areas in Samlot District Receive Humanitarian Donations from Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Battambang Province
(Battambang): Mr. Sok Lou, Chairman of Battambang Provincial Committee of the Cambodian Red Cross and his colleagues on February 21, 2023, invited the participants and brought the humanitarian donations of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch of Battambang Province to the most vulnerable people. There are 100 Por families in Phnom Rey village, Ta Tok commune, Samlot district, Battambang province.
Mr. Sok Lou said that seeing the hardships of the people, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross assigned the sub-branch of volunteers and youth of the Cambodian Red Cross to bring these humanitarian donations to the people. The most vulnerable are the total number of 100 families living in Phnom Rey village, Ta Tok commune, Samlot district, Battambang province.
In a friendly atmosphere with the people, the Chairman of the Branch Committee brought a royal message from Luang Men Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, Honorary President and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President, who sent greetings with compassion, consideration The daily lives of the people are most vulnerable with the deepest memories.
With the provision of gifts to alleviate all these difficulties, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen has always taken care of the health of the people, so through today's ceremony, Lok Chumteav, First Deputy Secretary General also reminded All citizens must take care of their health, drink boiled water and live in good hygiene.
For women who have small children or are pregnant, go to a specialist hospital at least 4 times and have to give birth at a health center, and if you are sick, please hurry to the nearest hospital or health center. On time, do not procrastinate, which endangers life.
The President reminded the people to pay attention to the safety of traveling on the road to avoid traffic accidents, because in the past, many of our brothers and sisters were disabled due to the war, but now we live under The roof of our peace must not allow ourselves to become disabled due to traffic accidents.
In response, all the people expressed their deep gratitude to the Cambodian Red Cross under the leadership of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, the Mother of Humanity, who has always cared about the well-being of the people without any discrimination. No. Please note that each family received donations including: 25 kg of rice, 1 box of noodles, 1 can of fish sauce, 1 can of soy sauce, 1 case of pure water and 10 cans of fish.
