Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi: 84% of the workforce is women and 61% are women business owners
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Ing Kantha Phary, Minister of Women's Affairs and Chair of the Cambodian National Council for Women, said that in the economic sector in Cambodia, women have become a driving force that has contributed significantly to the national economic growth and social development. . About 84 percent of the workforce is women, and about 61 percent of women are business owners or entrepreneurs, a high rate in the region.
The Minister confirmed this at the meeting to review the work in 2022 and work direction 2023 of the National Council of Cambodia for Women, chaired by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Honorary Vice President of the National Council of Cambodia for Women this morning. February 21, 2023.
She said that by 2022, women business owners will increase from 20 percent to 22 percent and women business owners will increase from 30 percent to 32 percent.
The Minister of Women's Affairs also pointed out that in agriculture, tourism and the environment, there is a link between long-term economic development, increased agricultural productivity, job creation and non-agricultural employment, and family and community income. The tourism sector provides direct and indirect employment opportunities to the people, of which about 60% are women.
The Minister also mentioned that the development of mixed farming communities and production groups is important for women to have access to capacity building skills in production and business management in each community. Environmental development has brought benefits for many women and farming families to increase their income based on rich natural resources through the provision of ecotourism services in protected area communities.
