Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea expressed his appreciation and appreciation in front of the new Japanese Ambassador for the investment activities of Japanese investors in Cambodia in the non-textile manufacturing sector, which has played an important role in contributing to Diversification of the Cambodian economy and human resource development in Cambodia.
The Minister underlined the commitment of the Royal Government of Cambodia under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Prime Minister in striving to accelerate the recovery and strengthening of the economic base of Cambodia through the creation of a favorable environment. Facilitate investment, as well as the promulgation of investment laws and the introduction of roadmaps for the development of the automotive and electronics sectors.
The Minister also thanked the Japanese investors for their continued confidence in the Royal Government of Cambodia in ensuring peace, political and economic stability, which are the prerequisites for investment decisions.
Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, on behalf of the Ministry of Trade and Investment, is committed to improving administrative procedures in order for Cambodia to become part of the regional supply chain. He called on all Japanese companies to pay attention to the Thai + 1 and Vietnamese + 1 concepts.
He also welcomed the initiatives and cooperation from JICA, JBAC and all Japanese companies to participate in vocational training and skills training for Cambodian workers to increase Cambodia's attractiveness in areas with high skills requirements. Such as automotive and electronics.
Mr. Assusi Uno expressed his pride in being appointed Ambassador to Cambodia because Cambodia is a country with a long culture and beautiful traditions as well as dynamic development.
He mentioned the strong relationship between Cambodia and Japan, which has become a "comprehensive strategic partnership" on the occasion of the two countries commemorating the 70th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations in 2023, with the agreement of the President. Leaders of the two countries in November 2022.
He said that although today was the first meeting of which he was honored to co-chair, he clearly understood the importance of this bilateral meeting, which has always provided opportunities for Japanese investors to raise challenges as well. Requests to the Government of Cambodia to interpret and provide win-win solutions for the Royal Government and the private sector.
He added that the success of Japanese businessmen and investors in Cambodia will be an important catalyst in attracting more Japanese businessmen and investors to invest in Cambodia.
As of the end of January 2023, the Council for the Development of Cambodia (CDC) has approved 150 Japanese investment projects with a total investment capital of approximately $ 2.9 billion.
