In 2022, the Ministry of Justice provides 2,600 million Riels to the Bar Association for more than 6,000 poor people
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi, Minister of Women's Affairs and Chair of the Cambodian National Council for Women, said that in 2022, the Ministry of Justice has allocated a total budget of 2,600 million Riels to the Bar Association to pay for defense projects. Legal litigation for the poor and a total of 6,156 cases.
This report was presented at the meeting to summarize the results of 2022 and the work direction of the New Year of the National Council of Cambodia for Women, chaired by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Honorary Vice President of the National Council of Cambodia for Women this morning. February 21, 2023.
According to the Minister, in 2022, the Ministry of Justice, through lawyers, received 456 legal consultations, provided legal services and related services to people in 10 provinces, mediated disputes outside the court system. There were 1,424 women's cases out of a total of 3,207 cases and 1,549 legal counsel cases, with 850 female cases.
In addition, the Cambodian National Council for Women has provided legal assistance to protect the rights of women and girls affected by violence in a total of 313 cases, including 234 defense cases, 217 minor cases and There are 47 completed cases.
The Ministry of Health also provided health services to 451 women out of 453 victims at health centers and hospitals. Provides forensic services to a total of 276 women and girls victims, with the exception of fees and court fees.
In addition, the Ministry of Women's Affairs facilitated and provided services to women and girls victims at the national and sub-national levels through 149 direct and online legal and psychological counseling.
UN official: Deployment of troops to humanitarian cause reaffirms Cambodia's commitment to upholding the UN Charter and uniting to seek peace for all mankind
The UN Resident Coordinator in Cambodia made the remarks during a meeting with Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, as well as the leadership of the Ministry of National Defense and General Sem Sovanny, Director General of the National Center. Manage the peacekeeping force, prepare for the departure and make additional recommendations to the 98th Explosive Ordnance Disposal Squadron (98) at the Ministry of National Defense.
In addition, Joseph Souer said that the deployment of Cambodian troops in peacekeeping reflects the commitment in the statement, including acknowledging that "long-term progress in strengthening security, national unity, the rule of law, human rights and the rule of law" "Sustainable development must happen in parallel."
Mr. Joseph Suer said that the participation of the Cambodian Blue Hat Army shows that unity is a strong bond of unity that no force can break.
The UN official also acknowledged the dedication and courage of the Cambodian military, as well as set an example and upheld the highest standards of integrity in carrying out humanitarian missions in the United Nations family, and praised the heroism and courage of the United Nations. Strong commitment from female warriors who have been involved in peacekeeping operations to support world security and peace.
According to General Sem Sovanny, from 2006 to the present, after the end of the UN peacekeeping mission (UNTAC) in 1993, Cambodia sent troops to join the UN peacekeeping mission. On the one hand, the flag of Cambodia and on the other hand, the flag of the United Nations, as well as shoulder to shoulder for the cause of world peace with more than 100 donor countries.
The General continued that the commitment of the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, has made the national and international community amazed by Cambodia's mission to participate with the highest honors. For humanity in the world under the umbrella of the United Nations.
