(Phnom Penh): Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority has signed a Memorandum of Understanding with the Institute of Technology of Cambodia to establish cooperation on education, research, exchange and sharing of information and technology, and to enhance mutual understanding to manage production and Distribute clean water with new technology.
The MoU signing ceremony was held at the French Embassy in Cambodia on the afternoon of February 20, 2023, represented by Mr. Long Naro, Director General of the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority and Dr. Po Kim Tho, Director General of the Institute of Technology of Cambodia.
Through this Memorandum of Understanding, the Institute of Technology of Cambodia will support short, medium and long term professional training on a number of skills, such as water treatment system maintenance and water distribution system maintenance to Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority staff. Or students who study subjects related to hydrology and clean water.
In addition, the two sides will raise and implement joint research cooperation projects, as well as the exchange and sharing of information and educational and research equipment, as well as the exchange of experiences between the management officials of the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority and professors. On the latest technological innovations and technologies related to the water sector.
The President of the Constitutional Council advised to prepare teacher support to support the inclusion of some basic provisions of the Constitution in the curriculum.
(Phnom Penh): The Honorary Legal Officer, Dr. M. Chhun Lim, President of the Constitutional Council, recommended the preparation of teacher support to support the integration of some of the basic provisions of the Constitution into the curriculum from primary to secondary level.
The purpose of this visit is to learn about training and curriculum development in order to gather input into the preparation of a common handbook to support the inclusion of some basic provisions of the Constitution in the primary, secondary and tertiary curricula. High school in accordance with the spirit of the Memorandum of Understanding between the Constitutional Council and the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports.
