Minister Vong Soth: Cambodia will host the Asia-Pacific Conference on Persons with Disabilities from March 15-17
This was confirmed by Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, to the press at a press conference held at the Ministry of Social Affairs on February 21, 2023.
Mr. Vong Soth stated that the Asia-Pacific Disability Conference will discuss in detail the challenges and opportunities in the field of disability in the past to address together by sharing good experiences from speakers from Countries aim to build a confident and sustainable future plan.
The 5th Asia-Pacific Conference on Persons with Disabilities on Environmental Development was organized under the theme “Strengthening the Social and Economic Empowerment of Persons with Disabilities During and After Outbreaks. Kovid-19 Through Community-Based Environmental Development »
The purpose of this international conference is to:
* First: Promote the economic environment of people with disabilities in the region * Second: Promote social welfare and social protection for people with disabilities * Third: Strengthen cooperation and partnerships for all stakeholders The Effectiveness of Environmental Community Development * Fourth: Sharing good experiences, testimonials and innovations in environmental community development during and after the Kovid-19 outbreak.
Minister Vong Soth expressed his hope that after the three-day conference, Cambodia will achieve the dignity and rights of people with disabilities will be promoted in line with the slogan of the Global Sustainable Development Goals. "No one is left behind" through the exchange of good experiences, testimonials and innovations related to disability work and creating opportunities for communication between people with disabilities in Cambodia and people with disabilities abroad.
The Asia-Pacific Disability Conference has been held four times already, the first in Thailand in 2009, the second in the Philippines in 2012, the third in Japan in 2015 and The fourth in Mongolia in 2019, when the conference agreed to host the fifth conference in collaboration with the Asia-Pacific Rehabilitation Network.
