The General Department of Identification has confirmed that the Cambodian Nationality Identity Card is valid for 10 years from the date of issuance, so the identity card issued from June 2012 will gradually expire from June 2022 onwards. .
"In order to ensure the right to receive various services, especially the political right to use the identity card for the upcoming 7th National Assembly election in July 2023, please call on the General Department of Identification For citizens who have expired or less than 90 days left, please come and fill out the application form for a new Khmer identity card (duplicate).
Applying for a new nationality ID card at any of the following locations:
1: At the administrative police station, commune, sangkat or police inspectorate of municipalities, districts, Khans or the one-stop-shop of the municipality, district, Khan or the Capital-Provincial Police Commission of its permanent residence
2: Department of Khmer Nationality Identity Card (Sangkat Niroth, Khan Chbar Ampov, Phnom Penh)
Applicants for a new Khmer Nationality Identity Card, please attach an expired Khmer Nationality ID card with less than or 90 days remaining (and other supporting documents in case of data correction).
The General Department of Identification would like to confirm that the Royal Government does not require any payment to apply for a new Khmer Nationality Identity Card (Duplicate). If you have any questions or inquiries, please contact: 1271/017 898 915.
