Senior Minister Sun Chanthol Asks Thailand to Accelerate Construction of Stung Bot-Ban Nong Ian International Border Crossing Station
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, requested the Thai side to expedite the construction work and relevant legal standards on the construction of the new Stung Bot International Border Crossing Station, Poipet City and Ban Nong Ian International Border Crossing, Aranyaprathet District. Towards the official opening of this bilateral international gate in the near future.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol made this request on 20 February 2023 on the occasion of allowing Mr. Cherdkiat ATTHAKOR, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of the Kingdom of Thailand to Cambodia, and his colleagues to pay a courtesy call and discuss with each other. Also invited by relevant leaders and senior officials at the Ministry.
In addition, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also informed about the review of the results of the project to build the Thmar Da International Border Crossing to reach the opening of a new international border crossing between Cambodia and Thailand in the future to turn this border line. To become a special economic zone like other international ports through the travel of national and international tourists and the exchange of goods between the two countries, Cambodia - Thailand.
