Fifth Senate Commission Appreciates the Achievements of the General Department of Immigration, Ministry of Interior
(Phnom Penh): The Honorary Legal Officer of Dr. Ti Borasy, Chairman of the Senate Committee on Foreign Affairs, International Cooperation, Propaganda and Information (Fifth Committee), expressed her appreciation and appreciation for the achievements of the General Department of Immigration of the Ministry of Interior. In the past, especially on foreign management.
The commendation of the Fifth Committee of the Senate was made this morning, February 21, 2023, in a meeting with the General Department of Immigration, chaired by General Kirth Chantharith, Director General of the General Department of Immigration. The meeting was held at the Senate to hear the results of the General Department of Immigration in 2022 and plans for the future.
General Kiet Chantharith said that this is the third time that the General Department of Immigration has reported its annual work report to the Fifth Committee of the Senate on the management of foreigners in Cambodia, the progress of work. The new law on immigration will answer what the commission has visited in some areas, as well as questions that the commission wants to know about the law and practice.
As a result of this morning's meeting, the Honorary Legal Officer, Dr. Ti Borasi, and the members of the Fifth Commission expressed their happiness and acceptance of what the General Department reported. In addition, the Fifth Commission highly appreciated the efforts of the General Department of Immigration and relevant units in the Ministry of Interior.
Ms. Kitti Nitikosal Dr. Ty Borasy also expressed her appreciation and thanks to the leadership of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior regarding the work of the General Department of Immigration and Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. Regular recommendations for the management of foreigners and immigration in Cambodia.
