Some of Venice's most popular artificial waterways begin to dry up as Italy faces drought
(ROME) - Scientists and environmentalists say the hot, dry winter weather in recent weeks has raised concerns that Italy may face another drought after last summer's emergency. While the Alps receive less than half the seasonal snowfall than before. This is according to the publication by the AFP news agency on Tuesday, February 21, 2023.
The warning comes as the city of Venice, which is typically concerned about flooding, is facing unusually low tides, with boats and emergency services out of operation. Some famous artificial waterways. Problems in the city are being blamed on a number of factors, such as lack of rainfall, high pressure systems, changes in the sea level.
