(Phnom Penh): This morning, Tuesday, February 21, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over a meeting to review the work results of 2022 and raise the work direction for 2023 of the "National Council of Cambodia for Women". Held at the Peace Palace.
Women are considered by the Royal Government as an important backbone to promote national economic development. Through the regular meetings of the "Cambodian National Council for Women", a number of recommendations have been reviewed and put forward to promote women's rights and develop women's capacity, especially to promote women's activities in social affairs.
The Royal Government of Cambodia, headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has always paid close attention to women's issues. Women's rights are better promoted and on an equal footing with men in society, and more women are included in leadership roles and decisions in ministries and institutions.
In fact, in Cambodia's top institutions, both the legislature and the executive, more and more women are being included in leadership roles. The National Assembly, Ms. Khuon Sodary, was elected second Vice President of the National Assembly.
In the executive branch of the government of the sixth mandate, Ms. Men Sam An has been appointed Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Assembly Senate Relations and Inspection, Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi has been appointed Minister of Women's Affairs, and Ms. Pheung Sakona, Minister of Culture. And fine arts. In addition, many women have been appointed Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State, Director General, Deputy Director General ... and provincial governors.
Along with education, female students are also seen as encouraging and facilitating their higher education. However, every year in this work review meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen always reminds all women to strive to increase their capacity through study efforts.
To help women who were victims of abuse in 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen decided to allow his volunteer lawyer to defend women free of charge. All these activities show that Samdech Techo Hun Sen cares deeply for women in accordance with the policy that considers women as the backbone of the nation.
