Nearly 100 Cambodian Blue Hat Troops Ready to Carry Out Humanitarian Mission in Central Africa
(Phnom Penh): Peace Operation is a global principle and has been playing an important role through the participation of all national and international circles, joint operations to help countries torn apart by the fires of war, and to join countries in Rehabilitation, peace, stability and development in line with UN principles to build a path to a peaceful and prosperous world.
For the past 17 years, the Cambodian Blue Hat Army has achieved a lot of national prestige in peacekeeping missions under the UN umbrella in countries devastated by war and chronic internal conflicts.
In addition to the core duties of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, on the one hand, the flag of Cambodia, the defense of the motherland, the defense of the territorial integrity of the Kingdom of Cambodia, and on the other hand, the flag of the United Nations, to help countries and nations that are sinking by conflict and war. Peace like developing countries in the world.
On the morning of February 21, 2023, the 98th Explosive Ordnance Disposal Brigade, including 10 women, was ready to go on a peacekeeping mission under the United Nations umbrella in the Central African Republic. (MINUSCA) on the afternoon of February 21, 2023.
To encourage Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, Mr. Joseph Scheuer, United Nations Resident Coordinator in Cambodia, and the leadership of the Ministry of National Defense and General Sem Sovanny, Director General of the National Center for Management Peacekeepers organized a farewell ceremony and made further recommendations to the 98th Explosive Ordnance Disposal Squadron to become wise in carrying out their missions successfully.
The Minister of National Defense of Cambodia expressed his strong belief that as the outstanding Khmer people and officers of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, they will strive to fulfill this historic new task in the highest sense of responsibility and success for the nation. The motherland of Cambodia, for sure.
In addition, Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh also reminded the troops who went out to carry out humanitarian missions to adhere to and strictly implement the recommendations, which are the four points of the order of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia mentioned in the ceremony. Conversation of the 135th Squadron on a mission to Sudan on April 12, 2006.
Samdech Pi Chey Sena Tea Banh also instructed all forces to perform their duties in accordance with their professional ability, strict discipline, courage, morality, purity and respect for the law, all of which are absolute values and qualities. Must be able to unite, respect, love each other, be united as one and know how to help each other to achieve their respective tasks and team tasks.
Joseph Scheuer stated that the Cambodian Blue Hat Army's departure for the Central African Republic's humanitarian mission underscores Cambodia's commitment to uphold the spirit of the United Nations Charter and to participate. With the true community of nations united in the search for peace and a better future for all mankind.
The UN official confirmed that the participation of the Cambodian army shows that unity is a strong bond of unity that no force can break. "I hope this unity will serve as a beacon of hope for others not only in Cambodia but around the world."
According to General Sem Sovanny, from 2006 to the present, after the end of the UN peacekeeping mission (UNTAC) in 1993, Cambodia sent troops to join the UN peacekeeping mission. The United Nations, with one hand holding the Cambodian flag and the other with the United Nations flag, as well as shoulder to shoulder for the cause of world peace with more than 100 donor countries.
The General emphasized that during the past 17 years, Cambodia has achieved great achievements, including demining, demining, horizontal and vertical construction, providing protection, rules and safety to senior dignitaries in the mission area. Humanitarian activities such as: providing clean water, treatment, providing study materials, etc. Free to people in the mission area.
General Sem Sovanny stated that the work of Cambodian heroes by the end of 2022 will continue to rank second in the ASEAN community and 12th out of 123 countries donating troops.
As of 2023, Cambodia has sent a total of 8,859 Cambodian troops, of which 681 women have been deployed in 11 missions in nine countries: Republic of Sudan, South Sudan, Chad, Central Africa, Lebanon, Mali, Syria, Cyprus. And Yemen on demining skills, horizontal-vertical construction engineering, military level 2 hospitals, airport engineering, unexploded ordnance disposal, officers, officers and military observers.
Currently, 788 Cambodian troops, including 130 women, are serving in four countries: the Republic of South Sudan, Lebanon, Central Africa and Mali. Senior Minister Yim Nola condemns three generations of traitors Sam Rainsy who repeatedly insulted the King
