(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, will pay an official visit to Thailand on February 23-24, 2023 at the invitation of Thai Deputy Prime Minister Don Pramat Vinay.
According to a statement from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the two Deputy Prime Ministers will hold bilateral meetings to discuss better bilateral relations and growing cooperation in all fields, including trade, investment, tourism, employment, education and health. And culture, etc. Cooperation within the ASEAN framework as well as regional and international issues of common interest and concern will also be discussed.
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon will also pay a courtesy call on the Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Thailand, General Prayuth Chan Ocha.
