(Phnom Penh): The Korean side has promised to increase the quota of Cambodian workers to more than 10,000 in 2023 and more in the years to come, while in 2022 recently, Cambodia has received good rankings in the field of sending workers. Go to work in Korea and through the evaluation from the Korean side, see that Cambodian workers are honest, diligent, pay attention to work, making Korean employers very satisfied.
This promise was made during a discussion between Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training and Mr. UH SOOBONG, Director of the Human Resource Development Unit of the Republic of Korea on the afternoon of February 20, 2023 at the Ministry of Labor.
During the meeting, Mr. Ith Sam Heng said that the Republic of Korea is a good friend who has contributed to the development of Cambodia, especially in the field of diplomacy and cooperation, our two countries have become strategic partners in all fields.
The Minister emphasized that despite being in the Kovid-19 phase, the Republic of Korea continues to recruit Cambodian workers to work there, as well as take good care of Cambodian workers. With the return of Cambodian workers from the Republic of Korea, he observed that they have progressed and underwent significant economic changes, with some becoming entrepreneurs and well-known investors.
The head of the Human Resource Development Unit of the Republic of Korea confirmed to the Minister that the Korean side will organize a vocational training program for expatriate workers in Korea, in which Cambodia may be a priority country to benefit from this new project. The goal is to provide loans to help workers to be able to run a business properly and have a good income.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng is really pleased with the project that the Korean side helps to train foreign workers who have completed their stay in Korea to receive specific skills training to be able to start their own business. The minister wants Cambodian workers to be one of the top priorities for other countries that Korea considers recruiting.
Cambodia, United Arab Emirates begin third round of Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement
According to a press release from the Ministry of Commerce, obtained by Fresh News on February 20, 2023, the third round of talks will take place over three days from the 20th to the 22nd. In February 2023, in Dubai, United Arab Emirates, a total of 100 people from both sides will attend the Trade Negotiations Working Group.
The third round of talks comes after Cambodia and the United Arab Emirates opened the first round of talks on October 24-26, 2022 in the capital, Abu Dhabi, and the second round of talks on December 19-21, 2022. Phnom Penh, Kingdom of Cambodia with fruitful results.
For the third round of talks, the two sides will continue to negotiate on market access and plan to conclude negotiations on the remaining text of the agreement, which includes 18 chapters related to trade in goods, trade in services, trade barriers. Sanitation and phytosanitation, trade facilitation, rules of origin, economic cooperation, trade, investment, intellectual property and law and institutions.
Recognizing the joint efforts and commitment of the two sides, the two sides agreed that the agreement will make a significant contribution to enhancing the comprehensive cooperation between the two countries, which will create new opportunities. Further, it aims to promote national economic growth and prosperity for the nation and the people of both countries.
