Samdech Techo: Cambodia Condemns North Korea Missile Launch as a Threat to Security and Peace (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia Legs as well as the shooting this morning, February 20. He added that the shooting posed a threat to security on the Korean Peninsula as well as the world.
According to Eang Sophalleth, the Prime Minister's personal aide, during the meeting, the South Korean ambassador informed Samdech Techo of the Korean government's concerns over North Korea's missile launch. The ambassador said the missile launch was a threat to peace on both the Korean Peninsula and around the world.
In response, Samdech Techo stressed that Cambodia has always condemned North Korea's missile launch as a violation of UN Security Council resolutions, escalating tensions and threatening security and peace on the Korean Peninsula. All over the world.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth quoted Samdech Techo as saying, "Regarding the North Korean missile launch, Samdech Techo informed Mr. Park that Cambodia condemned North Korea for repeatedly firing missiles, including the launch of missiles this morning. . "The missile launch violates a UN Security Council resolution and escalates tensions and threatens security and peace on the Korean Peninsula and around the world."
