Senior official of the Ministry of Education: E-cigarettes continue to mislead young people and actively share on social media
(Phnom Penh): Despite the ban by the Royal Government as well as the relevant law enforcement forces, e-cigarettes continue to mislead young people through innovative and attractive designs, featuring small new looks. Easy to carry and has a unique aroma and taste on social media without fear of the law. This is Ms. Soeur Socheata, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports.
She claimed that now the companies continue to actively promote through social media, and especially through social media such as Facebook telegram and other social media, while the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports is encouraging young Cambodians. Keep up with the digital network, do not believe in the scams of the company at all, and when you see those activities together to help continue to complain to the police to take immediate action.
Ms. Soeur Socheata also continued to call on all young people to eliminate e-cigarettes for everyone, both in and out of school, and continued to call on school management, teachers to join together to create Eliminate the use of all types of e-cigarettes in educational institutions and in the community to ensure that our human resources can meet the needs of society.
At the same time, the outstanding young people who participated in the rhetoric stated that although e-cigarettes cause serious health problems and the government has already issued a ban on the use, sale and distribution of e-cigarettes, but today the sale and distribution of e-cigarettes. Still openly on social media and chatting through friends, which led many students to buy and use.
The e-cigarette is designed by e-cigarette designers in a creative, civilized and attractive way, featuring a sleek, small, easy-to-carry look and aroma, as well as citrus, strawberry and coffee flavors, he said. And so on. Not only that, e-cigarette sellers advertised that it was a smoking cessation device and had no side effects.
He added that in order to prevent young people from being lured to use this dangerous product, he asked the relevant authorities to stop importing, distributing and promoting this product, especially to eliminate social media.
