The Ambassador expressed such views during a courtesy call and discussion with Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the evening of February 20, 2023 at the Peace Palace.
According to Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Samdech Techo's personal assistant, during the meeting, Mr. Park respectfully informed Samdech Techo that he was honored to be appointed Ambassador to Cambodia. Mr. Park pledged to do his best to further strengthen Cambodia-South Korea relations.
Mr. Park also paid a courtesy call on the President of the Republic of Korea to Samdech Techo and informed him of his study and understanding of Samdech Techo's activities in establishing diplomatic relations between the two countries as well as progress. In the order of this relationship.
In this regard, Mr. Park expressed the highest respect to the Prime Minister for leading and initiating the establishment of formal relations between Cambodia and South Korea in 1997.
Mr. Park said that bilateral relations between Cambodia and South Korea have been growing steadily, despite the stage of the 19-Kovid epidemic.
The ambassador emphasized that based on this good relationship, the trade volume between Cambodia and South Korea will reach $ 1 billion by 2022. In addition, South Korea is the second largest investor in Cambodia.
The ambassador also expressed hope that with the free trade agreement and the non-duplication of tariffs, it would encourage more South Korean investors to come to Cambodia.
Mr Park added that the South Korean government had increased most of its development assistance (ODA) in Cambodia. In that, assistance for the construction of bridges across the Tonle Sap to the Chroy Changvar area and across the Mekong River to the Noble Kingdom will help Cambodia to travel as well as boost the Cambodian economy.
In response, Samdech Techo welcomed and congratulated Mr. Park on his appointment as Ambassador to Cambodia. Samdech Techo also thanked Mr. Park for bringing the greetings of the President of the Republic of Korea to Samdech, as well as the commitment to strengthen the relationship between Cambodia and South Korea.
The Prime Minister briefed Park on the journey and background of the beginning of diplomatic relations between Cambodia and South Korea. Samdech Techo agreed with the Ambassador on the assessment of the progress of relations between the two countries.
Samdech Techo also thanked the South Korean government and people for helping Cambodia. Despite being plagued by Kovid 19, South Korea has not closed direct flights to Cambodia. For Samdech Techo, this shows that no matter what the circumstances, South Korea does not change its attitude towards Cambodia.
Samdech Techo also thanked the South Korean government for allowing Cambodian workers working in Korea to return to Cambodia with their wages and skills, as well as providing assistance for the construction of a bridge across the river in Phnom Penh.
