Dr. Hun Manet shares three major factors that stakeholders must continue to pay attention to job creation
Recommendations given by Dr. Hun Manet include:
* First, the quantitative factor refers to the creation of more job opportunities throughout the country as well as the promotion to the local level by promoting investment according to the suitability of each geographical location. At the same time, it is necessary to think, create and expand job opportunities abroad.
* Third: Equity factor refers to maintaining the harmonization of the relationship between employers and employees by paying attention to the provision and protection of the rights, interests and responsibilities of both parties within the legal framework.
In this regard, the Royal Government will provide equity to employers by providing incentives, maintaining political and macroeconomic stability, security and safety in order to facilitate investment or business in Cambodia to move forward easily and effectively. And safety.
For employees, equity will be provided through the creation and maintenance of employment opportunities, consideration of living standards through salary increases and other benefits for workers, health protection, occupational safety, and rights. Other legality of workers - employees.
