French Embassy in Cambodia: Jayavarman VII statue reappears
(Phnom Penh): The French Embassy in Cambodia on February 20, 2023 posted a message on social media that within the framework of a careful renovation, the team of workshop and stone conservation of the National Museum of Cambodia and the French School. The East (EFEO) has just assembled a statue of Jayavarman VII with pieces of his hand in a raised hand gesture.
The statue was deposited at the National Museum in 1934 and underwent major renovations by the National Museum and EFEO in 1999.
Please be informed that the results of the technical connection clearly show that both hands, the right found in 1990 and the left found in 1924, belonged to Jayavarman VII. This is according to the Department of Museums on January 28, 2023.
This hypothesis was confirmed in 2019 by a French research team using 3D scanning technology to test the connection. The connection by this technology shows that the pieces of both hands really belong to Jayavarman VII, because the broken joints overlap almost 100%.
Following the publication of the results of the 3D connection test, the management of the National Museum decided to take the two pieces of hand to be kept in the museum in 2021 to try to connect with his own image.
By January 2023, the team of stone workshops and conservationists tried to connect the two hands to confirm the hypotheses of the past and to conduct a survey and evaluation to find a technique to connect the two hands in the future. The future.
The purpose of this preservation and restoration is to enhance the prestige and invaluable memory of the Angkorian kings who sacrificed their physical and mental strength to defend our country.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's statement is in response to the misconception of the opposition that they said that the meeting between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and President Makrong in the past was at the request of Samdech Techo. Before.
