Dr. Men Sam An announces Svay Rieng as a demining province
(Svay Rieng): Ms. Kittisangkhab Dr. Men Sam An, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection, on the morning of February 20, 2023, announced the declaration of Svay Rieng Province, the eighth province in Cambodia to be demining.
The ceremony took place at the Svay Rieng Provincial Hall with the participation of delegates accompanying the governors of the eight districts, armed forces, commune chiefs, commune chiefs, commune officials and other relevant officials.
According to the report of Senior Minister Ly Thuch, in Svay Rieng province, operators cleared both minefields and explosive remnants of war in a total area of 41 square kilometers, equivalent to 419 minefields / mines, found and destroyed mines. 3,569 anti-personnel mines, 132 anti-tank mines and 7,1843 other explosive remnants.
At the same time, under the support of Samdech Techo Hun Sen Project for Mine Action in Svay Rieng Province, the Cambodian Mine Action Center (CMAC) has cleared the last mine and declared it as a demining province with a total area of 12 square kilometers. 139 minefields found and destroyed 1,023 anti-personnel mines and 299 other explosive remnants.
Ms. Kittisanghabandit continued that although Svay Rieng province has declared that all mines will become the eighth province in the country, she appealed to all young people and people living in areas at risk. Due to landmines and explosive remnants of war, please do the following:
* 1: If you see landmines or anything suspected of being explosive remnants of war, please do not touch, do not touch, do not burn, do not throw and do not throw, because it can cause accidents, disability or loss of life and must report immediately To the competent authority, local authority or the nearest deminer.
* 3: Do not use the land and do not enter areas that do not know the exact geography or suspected mines and explosive remnants of war. The Royal Government received 77 Cambodian artifacts from British families.
