(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Monday, February 20, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the awarding ceremony of 1,946 certificates and diplomas for students and students of the University of Human Resources. Of those, 1,033 were women.
The graduates include graduates of associate, bachelor's and master's degrees who graduated in the 2019-2020 academic year and the 2020-2021 academic year. There are also 32 scholarship students of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit.
Prof. Dr. Ek Monosen, Rector of the University of Human Resources, emphasized that the efforts to reform and develop the quality of training with a willing and responsible spirit and through the past 24 years, the University has developed from the Human Resource Development Institute. Established in 1998 and has achieved a series of great achievements to be proud of.
In 2023, the University has been equipping more study resources, especially the hotel room and the auditorium. Currently, the University of Human Resources has a board of directors, management, staff and 398 professors, 119 females, vocational students. And 3,101 students, 1,635 females.
As for the results of the training from the 1998-1999 school year to the 2020-2021 school year, a total of 41,341 students (14,369 females) at the professional level and students of all levels graduated. That includes both professional students and winning students who need to receive certificates and diplomas on this occasion.
