(Siem Reap): Dr. Kao Thach, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture (ARDB) on the evening of February 19, 2013, continued to visit and disseminate credit policies in support of vegetable growing projects. Safety in the net house to two communities: Safe Agriculture Community, located in Chrey Khang Cheung Village, Kien Sraeng Commune, Sot Nikum District, Siem Reap Province.
The farming community is registered with the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries with 110 members, 85 females, or 67 families. The members of this community are engaged in trading vegetable seeds, rice seeds, romduol flowers, selling processed rice such as candies and compost and natural pesticides made from sesame oil.
Samrong Meanchey Agricultural Community is located in Bot Dangkor Village, Samrong Commune, Sot Nikum District, Siem Reap Province. The farming community is registered with the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, with 81 family members growing vegetables indoors and in the fields, such as cauliflower, cabbage, tomatoes, beans, kale, kale, and Hawaiian peppers. Separately, the community produces vegetables and supplies them to markets in Siem Reap, Kampong Som and Kampong Cham.
