Kampong Thom Military Cracked Down on Illegal Timber Truck and Confiscated Large Timber
(Kampong Thom): The Kampong Thom Provincial Gendarmerie on February 19, 2023 launched an operation to crack down on a Samsung car that was illegally transporting timber from Preah Vihear province to Kampong Thom province and confiscated a large amount of timber. Also.
According to Brigadier General Meas Yot, Commander of the Kampong Thom Provincial Gendarmerie, told Fresh News in Kampong Thom that "a Samsung truck carrying a full load of timber from Po village, Po commune, Tbeng Meanchey district, Preah Vihear province, was under the jurisdiction of the military police." Kampong Thom province cracked down on Sunday, February 19, 2023 at 11:00 at Thnal Bapek village, Trapeang Russey commune, Kampong Svay district, Kampong Thom province.
The Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie confirmed that the operation was carried out under the order of Mr. Say Veasna, Deputy Prosecutor of Kampong Thom Provincial Court, ordering the Provincial Gendarmerie to detain and send to the Forestry Administration for investigation. The car, with license plate Phnom Penh 2j-0290, was driven by a man named Mao and another woman.
In general, the crime of transporting timber on the roads in Preah Vihear province through Kampong Thom province on National Road 62 seems to be active, with traders transporting it day and night, some open and some concealed. The reason why traders can transport such timber smoothly is suspected to be in harmony with the authorities on the road, especially on National Road 62, there are many checkpoints.
