(Phnom Penh): Investors in the agricultural sector said that in addition to Mien Pailin, which is being sold on the Alibaba online market, there are some other potential products that may continue to be sold on the online market, while the Ministry Businesses are examining the possibility of signing a memorandum of understanding with Alibaba to export more Cambodian products to foreign online markets.
By bringing Cambodian products to market in China's famous online market, this will encourage consumers in China and international markets to become more aware of the quality of Cambodian products, which is a good opportunity to expand the market to other countries.
Duke Hun Lak, an investor in the agricultural sector and an exporter of products to international markets, told Fresh News that in addition to Mien Pailin, there are some potential products that Cambodia can export to the Chinese online market. Such as processed cashew nuts, pepper, mango, rice and processed bananas.
He said that if these products can be sold in foreign online markets, it will help boost more exports as well as increase value added. In fact, Pailin lentils, which have recently been marketed on Alibaba, have boosted exports, boosting the price of lentils this year, making farmers more profitable and happy this year.
"After all, it is important for Cambodia to increase investment in the establishment of more processing plants."
On February 14, 2023, Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, chaired a meeting to review the possibility of signing a Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) between the Ministry of Commerce and Alibaba to export Cambodian products to foreign online markets.
The Ministry of Commerce has worked closely with Alibaba, with the participation of representatives from the Ministry of Economy and Finance and the National Commission for the Promotion of One Village, One Product, and as a result, the working group met three times with Alibaba. To achieve the draft Memorandum of Understanding.
