Khmer Civilization Expert: Incorporating Khmer Literature in National and International Private School Curriculum as a Mechanism of National Love
(Phnom Penh): Khmer civilization expert, Mr. Rath Sandab, congratulated Dr. Hun Manet for requesting the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports to include Khmer literature in this national and international private school program. Khmer children, because knowing the national language and literature is the mechanics of the idea of patriotism. But if Cambodian children live on Cambodian soil and lack knowledge of the national language and literature, that is also a national challenge.
Because knowing the language and literature of the nation is a vehicle to understand the history, culture, traditions, customs, which are the mechanics of thought, make the brain think, think in the spirit of patriotism and national reconciliation.
Therefore, in terms of language and script, we can say that it is a vehicle of ideas, a vehicle of culture, trade, diplomacy and religion in the interconnectedness of society, like a thread that binds one another to a great extent. And so long.
Because language and script are the determinants of the national identity of each nation, in fact, in terms of Khmer history, scholars have identified the pagoda in Angkor Borei, Takeo province, 611 AD, inscription K600, because it is based on letters with a specific date and year. Is the oldest.
