Tbong Khmum Governor Meets More Than 60,000 People to Trace Fish in Boeung Trapeang Kram in Memot District
(Tbong Khmum): To commemorate the preservation of ancient heritage, Mr. Cheam Chansophoan, Governor of Tbong Khmum Province, and Ms. Meng Van Danin and Mr. Seak Leng, Chairman of the Provincial Council, initiated and presided over the traditional fishing ceremony at Boeung Kram or Boeung Trapeang Kram is located in Satum village, Choam Kravien commune, Memot district on February 18, 2023.
It should be noted that for more than 200 years, the people of Satum village have been holding a fishing ceremony at Boeung Kram every year in February, after the farmers have already harvested their agricultural products, according to her grandmother. Grandpa told.
On that occasion, Mr. Cheam Chansophoan said that the fishing ceremony was interrupted during the Pol Pot regime, but since the victory on January 7, 1979, the ceremony was re-organized with a large number of participants.
The provincial governor confirmed that for this year, there are more participants than last year, there are more than 60,000 people from near and far from Tbong Khmum, Kampong Cham, Prey Veng, Svay Rieng, Phnom Penh and other provinces. In the spirit of brotherhood, unity, love, friendliness, morality, good manners.
Mr. Cheam Chansophorn added that these solemn gatherings are possible because the country is stable and the development progresses in all areas, there is peace throughout the country under the shadow of peace that Samdech Techo Hun Sen strives to bring. Thanks for the peace.
In this program, there are fishing, cooking, dancing and entertainment, especially HE Dr. Governor and Lok Chumteav supported those who participated in the fishing competition, catching many kilos to get the prize money.
1st place gets 50,000 Riels and enjoy 2 cans of beer in the shade of peace, 2nd place gets 3 prizes and 2 cans of beer per person, 4th to 12th place gets 2 cans of beer each Like all fishing contest participants receive an incentive budget of 50,000 Riels per person.
Please be informed that this fishing celebration at Boeung Trapeang Kram is held every year in February, you come together to visit the scenery around Boeung Kram, which has a legacy from our ancestors, including: Thmor Ta Chrouk Dey The color of the blood on the head of Ta Chak Ta Pram, the place where the wine bar and the Neang Leum pond are.
Prior to the fishing ceremony, the authorities did not allow people to fish in the lake to maintain the presence of fish for the annual fishing ceremony.
For fishing, people can use only traditional tools such as angrot chhnang and trak to catch fish in this ceremony, with the Boeung Kram area of about 30 hectares and the lake area of 1 hectare.
