He said that to achieve this work requires the participation of student volunteers to help farmers and the Cambodian Agricultural Research and Development Institute (CARDI) from the laboratory to the cultivation to the market for farmers. This is the first opportunity and the first gathering of student volunteers to help farmers.
According to Ngor Bunthan, Rector of the Royal University of Agriculture, the project is scheduled to run for six months, with the first pilot project set to begin soon.
He said that in the past six months, more than 200 students who have volunteered will be retrained in all techniques and skills before going to the community.
The students come from eight faculties: Faculty of Agricultural Sciences, Economics, Agriculture and Rural Development, Agro-industry, Land Management and Administration, Rubber Science, Fisheries Science, and Faculty of Animal Sciences. In the 2022-2023 school year, the school has a total of 2,622 students.
