(Phnom Penh): Mr. Keut Rith, Minister of Justice, on February 17, 2023, signed a Memorandum of Understanding on Cooperation with the Supreme Council of the French Notary, represented by Mr. Notary Jean Deleage, Representative of the Supreme Council of the French Notary in Southeast Asia.
Speaking at the event, Mr. Keut Rith stated that the signing of the Memorandum of Understanding on cooperation is now opening a new page in strengthening cooperation between the two institutions to help the professional notary in Cambodia. Improved.
He said that through the implementation of the Memorandum of Understanding on the new cooperation, the Supreme Council of the French Notary will assist Cambodia in the following important tasks: * First, to help establish a strong legal framework for the establishment, management and Develop the profession of notary in Cambodia through the Latin system and in accordance with the actual needs of Cambodian society
* Second: Continuing the training to strengthen the capacity of notary students and notaries in order to improve the quality and efficiency of the notary profession in Cambodia to gain more trust and wider recognition from the public.
* And the third: to help prepare laws and regulations for the establishment and management of the brokerage profession, a new profession for Cambodia.
Cooperation with the Supreme Council of the Notaries of France began 20 years ago with the holding of a conference on the Latin notary system "Notaries of Core Security Factors in the Economic Environment" in February 2004, a historic event in the notary sector. In Cambodia.
