(Phnom Penh): Khmer-Islamic teachers express their gratitude to the head of government and Cambodian Islamic leaders for their care and consideration in providing the framework to more than 1,500 Khmer-Muslim teachers across the country. In 2015 to receive salaries and other benefits. Previously, they did not receive a monthly salary, receiving only a small donation of money and rice from the parents of the students.
This statement was made on the occasion of Dr. Osman Hassan, Senior Minister in charge of Special Mission and Chairman of the Board of the Khmer Islamic Teachers Association, met with Khmer Islamic teachers from Phnom Penh, Kampong Speu and 178 people in Prey Veng province at the Islamic Center of Phnom Penh (PPIC) on the morning of February 17, 2022.
Ms. Soup Mary, a teacher of the Khmer-Islamic framework at km 9, Sangkat Chrang Chamres 1, Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh, stated that she started teaching for more than 10 years and received the framework of the Khmer-Muslim teachers in 2015. . She said she was very happy to have a teacher because it helped to improve the family life to a certain extent and was able to provide for her children to go to school.
"Life used to be difficult, but now it is a little better because we get paid every month, even though we have maternity leave, the state helps and we go to the hospital to give birth," she said. The cost of treatment as well. She thanked the head of the Cambodian government and Islamic leaders for their attention and hard work to ensure that Cambodian Muslim teachers receive a decent salary as they do today.
Mr. Tam Rasat, a Khmer-Muslim teacher in Russey Keo district, said that he had been teaching students since 1995, when it was very difficult because the Khmer-Muslim teachers did not receive a salary, only fundraising. Through the parents of the students as little as possible, such as the budget of rice and potatoes, unlike today.
He said that now he is very happy to get a framework and get a regular salary that can help solve many problems in daily life. He expressed his gratitude and thanks to the head of government under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the leaders of Khmer Islam in Cambodia, who always pay attention and consider Khmer Islam teachers.
On that occasion, Dr. Osman Hassan said that achieving the framework of Khmer-Islamic teachers is not an achievement that happens by itself, but it is the efforts of leaders at all levels, including the Muslim community. Also one that is committed to unity as a whole, following the right policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Dr. Osman Hassan encouraged all Khmer Muslim teachers to love and support the head of the Cambodian government to continue to achieve peace, development and other achievements.
