Following is the decision: Mr. Chap Dina has been appointed as the Vice President of the Cambodian People's Party in Daun Penh District, Mr. Lam Heng Huot has chaired the meeting to review the disaster work in Kampong Thom, Banteay Meanchey and Siem Reap provinces and set out 6 main principles.
(Siem Reap): Mr. Lam Heng Huot, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Deputy Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management (NCDC) Km From 16-17 February 2023, chaired a meeting to review the results of disaster management in 2022 and the direction of implementation in 2023 of Kampong Thom, Banteay Meanchey and Siem Reap.
The meeting was also attended by the Provincial Governor, Deputy Provincial Governor, Deputy Secretary General of the NEC. Heads of Departments, Municipal, District, Commune, Sangkat and Provincial Departments. Through this meeting, the provincial governors and deputy governors made reports on the impact and damage from disasters in 2022 and proposed the implementation direction for 2023 for the provincial, municipal, district, commune and sangkat levels to implement.
Mr. Lam Heng Huot praised and appreciated the leaders and officials of the Provincial Disaster Management Committee, as well as the Armed Forces and local authorities who have actively contributed to the successful response to the flood disaster in 2022 and early 2023 in good cooperation with the National Committee for Disaster Management.
In addition, Mr. Lam Heng Huot mentioned good experiences of preparation at both the national and sub-national levels in the past, but there are still some shortcomings, so he set out six key guidelines to supplement. These shortcomings include:
First, to promote the preparation and updating of the composition and structure of the Provincial, Municipal, District, Khan and Commune Disaster Management Committees.
Second: Strengthen the capacity of municipal, district and commune officials on the use of the Prime system and the early warning system 1294 to be more effective.
Third, urge to update the annual flood disaster preparedness plan by May every year.
Fourth, review and implement standard operating procedures as stated in the National and Provincial Reserve Plan Book.
Fifth: Municipalities, districts, Khans and communes must prepare appropriate safe places to prepare for the evacuation of victims in the event of a disaster.
And (6) requesting an office in charge of disaster management with clear officers responsible for general operations and information management under the Permanent Secretariat and Deputy Governor for Disaster Management.
At the same time, Mr. Lam Heng Huot encouraged partner organizations implementing disaster risk management in the province to continue cooperation and support the province to improve disaster risk management in the province. He also praised the province for including the private sector as an important partner in disaster risk management in the province.
Mr. Lam Heng Huot further confirmed the strengthening of cooperation between the General Secretariat of the NCDD. And the Capital-Provincial Disaster Management Secretariat through regular meetings to share and address common challenges, chaired by the Secretary-General of the NCDD.
