Mr. Ty Norin said that attracting sufficient investment for the development of the energy sector is a big challenge of the energy sector, in which the Royal Government must be creative and vibrant in addition to the legal principles and procedures in force. Only then can get enough investment. Inadequate investment could lead to a crisis in the energy sector, especially the electricity sector.
According to the report of the Electricity Authority of Cambodia, by the end of 2022, domestic electricity generation capacity will be 3,464.67 megawatts, equivalent to 77.07%, while the import of electricity from neighboring countries is 1,030.75 megawatts, equivalent to 22. 93 percent.
In addition, for the 2023 plan, Cambodia will increase electricity to 3,814.67 megawatts, equivalent to 77.14 percent, while electricity imports from neighboring countries will increase to 1,130.75 megawatts, equivalent to 22.86. Percentage.
Mr. Yim Viseth, President of the Electricity Authority of Cambodia, said that for the development of the transmission system in 2022 is to develop an additional 510 km transmission network and build 9 more substations, which currently has a total of 3 transmission lines. 953 km and 63 substations that can transmit electricity to 25 capitals and provinces across the country.
