The meeting was also attended by leaders of civil servants, the three armed forces, authorities, citizens and many stakeholders.
Provincial Governor Som Piseth said that the confiscation of illegal gear to burn now is to wake up fishermen and return to fishing legally, because fishing with illegal gear can make Affect the loss of biodiversity in the seabed.
On that occasion, Mr. Nuth Chan Sokha requested the provincial administration, departments, local authorities to continue to pay attention to the spirit of the Notification No. 2736 KOSAK of the Ministry of Agriculture dated 5 April 2022 on measures to prevent and suppress crime. Forests, wildlife and fisheries, and let the fishermen continue to participate as follows:
* First, the working group should continue to disseminate the notification No. 023/23 of the Provincial Administration on the cessation and setting deadlines for the production, trafficking, storage and use of illegal fishing gear to all fishermen. Living in Kep and other areas.
* Second: People who are engaged in fishing business should pay attention to implement the Notification No. 023/23 of the Provincial Administration on the cessation and setting deadlines for the production, trade, storage and use of fishing gear. Absolutely illegal after the team advertised in the media and introduced the location.
* Third: All citizens who engage in illegal fishing, please return to legal fishing.
Mr. Theng Borin, Director of Kep Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, said in the report that there were 25 cases of crime crackdown in 2022, including 11 cases of rat tail swallowing, 9 cases of fishing involving submarines and 3 motors removed. One case of confiscation of illegal equipment and one case of cracking down on illegal transportation of fishery products.
Cambodia-China Diamond Hexagon Cooperation: Pollen Acceleration for Growth
(Phnom Penh): The three-day visit of Samdech Techo Prime Minister Hun Sen to China from February 9 to February 11, 2023 ended with remarkable results.
The visit is the most important basis in addition to the existing momentum in increasing opportunities for both governments to promote Cambodia-China relations. The two sides reaffirmed their mutual support under all circumstances and unanimously agreed on many regional and global issues of mutual benefit for both countries and peoples.
The proclamation of the "Year of Cambodia-China Friendship" to mark the 65th anniversary of the establishment of official diplomatic relations has entered a new era of building a Cambodian-Chinese community with a common future with higher quality, higher standards and higher standards. The height of the steel ties between the two countries to a new page, the most precious for the next generation.
Formal diplomatic relations between Cambodia and China were established on July 19, 1958, but historically, relations between the two countries date back to the 13th century. As traditional neighbors and close partners, Cambodia and China have nurtured and maintained their inseparable "steel" ties, having gone through many historical trials and tribulations.
The new diamond hexagonal cooperation and the good relations that exist between Cambodia and China bring great expectations and great optimism for Cambodia as the economic recovery is accelerating and the resilience of the economy is even greater. Reinforced. The six priority areas respond perfectly to Cambodia's practical and timely needs.
As a country devastated by conflict and war, Cambodia attaches great importance to prioritizing peace and stability in the country and the region, building prosperity and development, and adhering to the principle of non-interference in internal affairs. Each other in its relations with other countries.
China is a superpower that has always supported the independent choice of the Cambodian people in choosing its development path that best suits its national conditions, supporting Cambodia in defending its sovereignty and national security, and promoting the country's political agenda. And economic and social development and against external interference in Cambodia's internal affairs.
In a comprehensive strategic partnership, the soon-to-be-completed "New Action Plan for Building a Cambodia-China Community with a Common Future" is vital and necessary to further accelerate practical cooperation between the two countries. Both countries in all fields.
China's vision for global development and its closer relationship with Cambodia is seen through the record of Chinese investment in Cambodia. In the early years, China invested heavily in energy infrastructure development and human resource development, helping to push Cambodia from a Least Developed Country (LDC) to a low-middle-income (LMIC) country.
In 2017, Cambodia received about $ 4.2 billion in Chinese development assistance, mostly in the form of grants and concessional loans. In 2021, China topped the list of foreign direct investment with a total investment of 2.32 billion US dollars, up 67 percent from 2020.
With the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone and the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway, the development of industrial and technological corridors will attract more competent Chinese enterprises to invest in Cambodia and deepen cooperation in the transportation sector. Transmission of power lines, fiber optics, warehousing and logistics to enhance the effective combination of Cambodia-China production capacity cooperation.
According to the United Nations World Tourism Organization in 2018, Cambodia is the eighth largest recipient of Chinese tourists. In 2019, the number of Chinese tourists was more than 2.3 million, or 36 percent of the total foreign tourists. Chinese tourists have made a significant contribution to socio-economic development and poverty reduction in Cambodia.
Good and stable relations between Cambodia and China are demonstrated through a wide and frequent exchange program between government officials, business leaders, scholars, students and people from all walks of life. Financial support from the Chinese government.
The visit of Samdech Techo Prime Minister Hun Sen and the Year of Cambodia-China Friendship has provided a solid foundation and a good opportunity to expand win-win cooperation at the sub-national level, increase people-to-people exchanges and Cultural change, strengthen youth exchange and promote the cause of Cambodia-China friendship to a new page.
Dr. Kin Phea is President of the Institute of International Relations of Cambodia and Chairman of the Political Science Technical Committee of the National Council for the Khmer Language of the Royal Academy of Cambodia.
Pailin longan farmers happy to face market crisis with rising prices as Chinese online sales boost
(Phnom Penh): Officials and the Mien Pailin Association said that this year, Mien Pailin farmers did not face any market problems after Cambodia exported Mian Pailin directly to the Chinese market as prices have risen by more than 3 Thousands of riels per kilogram, a price that benefits farmers.
Chhim Vachira, director of the Battambang Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, told Fresh News that so far no Pailin longan farmers have complained about market problems and falling prices as in previous years. Cambodia has opened its export market directly to China.
He said that currently in Battambang province, there are three companies that have collected Pailin longan from farmers for export to China, collecting the first and second longan.
According to the director of the Battambang Provincial Department of Agriculture, Mean Pailin (Ta Nen) plantation, which has 104 plantations registered and received GAP certification, is cultivated on 1406 hectares in Battambang province.
Mr. Sous Siyat, President of Mien Pailin Community, told Fresh News that all farmers who grow Mien Pailin in a good agricultural way are collected by the company for 3,500 Riel per kilogram, and this price is likely to increase further in Harvest in April during or after Khmer New Year, which may increase to 3,700 riel or 3,800 riel per kilogram. However, the price increase depends on the maintenance of farmers to meet company standards.
He said that although the price was better than last year, farmers have not expanded their cultivation, trying to maintain the standards of the collection company.
Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, recently said that Cambodia's fresh Pailin lentils, which are being sold in the Chinese market, are gaining a lot of support in just three days. Up to 18 tons after the Ministry of Commerce cooperated with the private sector to export fruit to China by selling on Alibaba's technology nursery.
He added that in the future, the Ministry will try to expand more markets for Cambodian agricultural products, especially with Alibaba, through discussions and provide additional input on the feasibility of signing a memorandum of understanding to promote the One Village, One Product movement.
There are 74 longan plantations officially registered for export to the Chinese market, including 40 in Pailin, 28 in Battambang and 6 in Banteay Meanchey. There are 8 packaging factories located in Kandal, 3 in Battambang, 2 in Pailin and 2 in Sihanoukville. Cambodia's acreage cultivation area is 13,608 hectares in four provinces.
