(Phnom Penh): Dr. Osman Hassan, Senior Minister in Charge of Special Missions and Chairman of the Board of the Khmer Islamic Teachers Association, met with 672 Khmer Islamic teachers from seven provinces, including Kampong Cham, Kampong Thom, Kratie, Stung Treng and Ratanakkiri. Mondulkiri and Tbong Khmum on February 16, 2023.
In the morning, Dr. had a talk with 140 teachers from Kampong Cham and Kampong Thom provinces in Roka village, Sambour Meas commune, Kampong Cham city, Kampong Cham province. In the afternoon, he continued to meet with 181 teachers from Kratie, Stung Treng, Ratanakkiri and Mondulkiri provinces in Pong Ro commune, Chhlong district, Kratie province. He also continued to meet with 351 teachers from Tbong Khmum province in Kong Kang commune, Ponhea Krek district, Tbong Khmum province.
On that occasion, Dr. Osman Hassan mentioned the attention of the government under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister has made the country peaceful and all religions live together without Discrimination. In particular, the Islamic community also has the opportunity to have community representatives become leaders in government and government officials.
In fact, in 2015, the Royal Government decided to provide a framework of about 1,500 Khmer-Muslim teachers to help improve the education sector as well as improve the lives of Khmer-Muslim teachers, because from the beginning they received financial support. A little bit from the villagers who can not meet the daily needs enough.
Dr. emphasizes, "So! We must be grateful and thankful to Samdech Techo for the Royal Government and for our leaders who have worked hard to help, without Samdech Techo, there would be no people to be teachers of the Islamic framework, because the decision is up to the head of the Royal Government for us. Became a framework teacher and has been paid for the past eight years.
Dr. continued that Khmer-Muslim teachers are activists of the Cambodian Islamic Movement and are activists who are making the commune safe. Villages, communes and sangkats are safe, meaning there is no alcohol, no robbery, no gambling and no drug trafficking, but it is written and banned in the Islamic Qur'an, so teachers Khmer Islam teaches students to avoid all these things.
"We, the Cambodian Muslims, the teachers, the intellectuals, we have to keep our work, contribute to the government, and we know that after every election, the voice of Islam," he said. We never shrink back everywhere. So! We need to keep more voices, it is in line with what Samdech has helped us.
Finally, Dr. instructed all Khmer Muslim teachers to continue to work hard and find all ways to teach students to be more quality and effective in promoting Islamic education in Cambodia. Bangladesh seeks fertilizer plant in Saudi Arabia amid global supply crisis
Dhaka: Bangladesh is preparing to set up a fertilizer plant in Saudi Arabia, the Ministry of Commerce said on Thursday as the South Asian country struggles to meet domestic demand amid a global supply crisis. Mr. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Thursday, February 16, 2023.
Discussions on a fertilizer plant in Saudi Arabia began last year as a memorandum of understanding for a feasibility study was signed on Wednesday between Bangladesh Chemical Industry Company and Saudi contractor Hanwha.
The agreement was signed at a virtual meeting organized by the Bangladesh Ministry of Industry and its embassy in Riyadh, saying in a statement that it was the first Bangladeshi government initiative to set up an industrial plant. On foreign lands.
The two factories will help meet the demand for fertilizer in Bangladesh, which needs 1.6 million tonnes a year to boost its agriculture. However, the actual production volume will be determined after a feasibility study.
Russia's invasion of Ukraine in February 2022 exacerbated global fertilizer shortages and pushed prices higher than ever before. Rising prices have affected agriculture and threatened Bangladesh's food security.
