Senior officials of the Ministry of Education introduced eight points to the Khmer Academic Staff Association to strengthen the normalization of the association under the leadership of the new Central Committee
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Nath Bunroeun, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, introduced eight points to the Khmer Academic Staff Association for consideration in order to strengthen the normalization of the association under the leadership of the new Central Committee, as well as for the Capital and Provincial Committees to be selected. Set by the upcoming election to get better results as expected.
The presentation was made on the occasion of the opening of the 13th General Assembly of the Khmer Academic Staff Association, which was held at the Central Teacher Training College on February 16, 2023. With the participation of delegates from all over the country, including about 180 guests.
The eight points of advice to the Khmer Academic Staff Association of Dr. Nath Bunroeun are as follows:
1: The operating principle of the association is to act voluntarily and outside politics, which is a force to attract membership requests from teachers at all levels. The pedagogical ideology that the panel should find is to find a way to strengthen this regularity, leading to the elimination of immorality (things that are not right) to the extent.
2. Statutes and issues are the foundation of accountability, transparency, and governance. Therefore, the amendment to suit the circumstances should be thoroughly discussed in order to be able to implement effectively.
3. The collection and transfer of contributions, which are the resources of the association process, should discuss ways to encourage the members in charge of this work, both spiritually and materially.
4: The case of the teacher magazine should inspire members to share experiences through writing articles related to education, science and culture to improve the quality of this text to better attract readers.
5: For the provincial capital, there is no place to build a teacher's house, which is now achieved in 16 provinces and is under construction in Koh Kong province, should discuss the change from teacher house construction to other constructions, but it is necessary to maintain the goal to serve the interests Member.
6: Providing child support to the family of the deceased should find a way to motivate as soon as possible if there are enough documents. However, favorable circumstances should be considered if possible.
7. The Capital and Provincial Oversight Committees shall strive to fulfill their roles well in accordance with the provisions of the Statute.
8- Association of the United Nations Although it is a non-governmental organization, it needs to be a partner to contribute to the Royal Government in fulfilling its duties according to the special statute, calling on the members to go to the general election for the 7th mandate of the National Assembly on July 23, 2023. Do not interrupt.
In addition, Dr. Nath Bunroeun, on behalf of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and one of the members, also sincerely praised the thorough preparation for the preparation and functioning of both forms and content to collect the input of knowledge. Of the ceremony met with the fruitful results of the efforts of the UN All levels of the capital and provinces as reported on the progress in the four years of the 13th mandate (2019-2022).
He added that the results were good, without any significant excitement that the association achieved, it was not a coincidence but a joint effort without any provision of the committee at all levels. And the support of the members has formed the spirit of pedagogy since the re-establishment of the association.
Rattanakiri Residents and Governor Congratulate Samdech Techo PM on Promoting Collective Ownership of Indigenous Communities
(Ratanakkiri): Mr. Nhem Sam Oeun, Governor of Ratanakkiri Province, addressed the indigenous people of two villages in Ta Veng Leu commune, Ta Veng district, who received a certificate of collective ownership held in Ta Veng district on the morning of the 16th. February 2023 Thus, Samdech Techo Prime Minister always pays attention to the well-being of the promotion of rights and freedoms on the collective property of indigenous communities.
In fact, on June 9, 2009, Samdech Techo Prime Minister issued a sub-decree on the procedure for land registration of indigenous communities so that parents and siblings have the right to land that is collectively owned for the community in order to provide equal rights. Land tenure laws ensure the security of land tenure, protect collective property by preserving the cultural identity, customs and good traditions of indigenous communities.
The provincial governor said that the registration of indigenous community land and the right to collective ownership of community land that exists today is because the country is peaceful and peace is the foundation of peace development. Other fundamental rights include the right to business, the right to education, the right to land, the right to travel, the right to live in harmony and without fear.
(Koh Kong): Unexploded ordnance and some explosive remnants of war were collected, destroyed and liberated 696,035 square meters, equivalent to 61% in Koh Sdach commune, Kirisakor district, Koh Kong province.
The operation was carried out by the National Center for Peacekeeping Demining and Demining in accordance with the recommendations of the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen for mine action under the theme "Provide safe land, create a smile" and towards Towards a landmine-free Cambodia in 2025.
In fact, in the geography of Koh Sdach commune, Kirisakor district, it has become another new achievement, with close cooperation with the Cambodian Mines Authority and local authorities at all levels, by implementing the second phase of the rolling zone, achieving many results. Also on demining operations.
In fact, on the morning of February 16, 2023, General Sem Sovanny, Second Vice President of the Cambodian Mines Authority, led a team to visit the demining force and the people in Koh Sdach commune and destroy 7 anti-personnel mines. 48 unexploded ordnance and 192 shrapnel.
On that occasion, General Sem Sovanny reminded the local demining forces in Koh Sdach to pay more attention and perform their duties in accordance with technical standards and not to be underestimated. Absolutely no unexploded ordnance. "Because landmines can make us one second alive, one second dead and one second safe."
General Sem Sovanny also received remarks from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of National Defense and Senior Minister Ly Thuch Deputy The first chairman of the Cambodian Mines Authority to the forces that are operating at the Koh Sdach site and the people living in this area.
According to Major General Sem Ratana, Deputy Director General of the National Peacekeeping Center, confirmed to Fresh News at the demining site in Koh Sdach on the morning of February 16: "For this operation began on the 15th. "January 2023, liberating 696,035 square meters of unexploded ordnance, equivalent to 61 percent."
Lt. Gen. Sem Ratana confirmed that for the operation, special forces found seven anti-personnel mines, 48 unexploded ordnance and 192 shrapnel. Separately, for the remaining area of 443,601 square meters is scheduled to be completed in April 2023 as planned.
On that occasion, General Sem Sovanny also handed over the precious gifts of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to nearly 300 families in Koh Sdach commune.
