(Phnom Penh): Dr. Vijawat Isarapakdi, Deputy Minister of Foreign Affairs of the Kingdom of Thailand, accompanied by Mr. Chet Keat, Ambassador of the Kingdom of Thailand to the Kingdom of Cambodia, led a Thai delegation to visit the Samdech Mena Library at 3 p.m. In the afternoon of February 16, 2023.
The purpose of this visit is to study and understand the history of Cambodia, especially the history of the Khmer Rouge, which is the core work of the Documentation Center of Cambodia, as well as to discuss cultural exchanges between Cambodia and Thailand. Youk Chhang, Director of the Documentation Center of Cambodia, warmly welcomed the guests.
Mr. Youk Chhang presented to the delegates the facilities and detailed description of the core work of the Samdech Mey Library, the Documentation Center of Cambodia and the provincial branches of the Documentation Center of Cambodia, which contributed and served the study, memory, Justice and Reconciliation in Cambodia.
Since its inception in 1995, the Documentation Center of Cambodia has worked tirelessly to compile documents on the Khmer Rouge regime to preserve common memories for Cambodia, and through this work, the Documentation Center of Cambodia has provided millions of documents to Khmer Rouge tribunal. It should be recalled that the Kingdom of Thailand also supported the trial of Khmer Rouge leaders by providing generous assistance to the Khmer Rouge tribunal.
Accompanied by the preface, which is a high note of His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, the King Father of Cambodia, this cookbook, a joint work between Cambodian and Thai scholars, cultivates a spirit of understanding and restraint. Another level of friendship between Cambodia and Thailand.
During the visit, Mr. Youk Chhang presented the above cookbook and described in detail the purpose of this book. Mr. Youk Chhang also described the Sleuk Reut Institute project, which is the permanent location of the Documentation Center of Cambodia, to the distinguished guests. At the same time, he also presented some rare documents in the collection of rare documents of the Documentation Center of Cambodia to the distinguished guests.
The delegation also viewed video files, audio-visual archives, paper documents, photographic documents and digital archives of the Documentation Center of Cambodia, which are housed in the Samdech Mey Library.
Finally, Mr. Youk Chhang organized a panel discussion to provide an opportunity for the delegation to share their views and ask questions. The Honorary Delegates expressed their deep interest in the work of the Documentation Center of Cambodia and thanked for the warm welcome to the Samdech Mey Library.
