(Phnom Penh): Professor Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, said that women and men of reproductive age must have the same understanding of health issues to ensure good health and avoid problems or infections.
This statement was made by the Minister on the occasion of the opening of the National Day of Maternal, Child and Child Health on February 21, 2023 under the theme "Together to strengthen reproductive health services, maternal, infant health, children, youth and nutrition to achieve the development goals. Sustainable in 2030 ”at the Cambodiana Hotel on February 16, 2023.
Minister Mam Bunheng continued, "In order for the unborn baby to be born healthy, only if their parents are healthy together, then men and women are very important in understanding reproductive health." Apparently, the husband transmits HIV to his wife so that the unborn baby can be transmitted from the mother. Therefore, we must continue to educate and disseminate the above issues to young people, young men or women and men of reproductive age to have more understanding.
The Minister fully supports the call of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, to unite to strengthen reproductive health services, maternal, infant, child and youth nutrition and nutrition to achieve the sustainable development goals by 2030. .
The following is the message from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen on the occasion of the National Day of Maternal, Newborn and Child Health on February 21 to the people:
1: All pregnant women:
* Regular check-ups and consultations with specialists at health centers or hospitals 4 times at regular intervals to get the tetanus vaccine and to get the Kovid-19 vaccine to get all the special preventive / treatment services Voluntary blood tests for HIV, syphilis, hepatitis B to prevent mother-to-child transmission
* To give birth at a health center or hospital, there is a doctor who is properly trained.
After the birth, both mother and baby should be vaccinated against 11 diseases at regular intervals. Care must be taken to monitor the health and growth of the baby until the baby is two years old.
Get your baby to a hospital right away if he or she sees any danger signs of respiratory infections, diarrhea, or other illnesses. Or not gaining weight at all.
Choose contraception for the health of mother and baby.
2: Young women or women of childbearing age between 15 and 49 years old who have health problems to consult, receive care or treatment at a health center or hospital or clinic, have a doctor who has the right training. From the Ministry of Health to avoid accidents and disabilities.
3: Leaders, civil servants, health workers and all service providers to support the implementation of the policy of the Royal Government to be more effective.
4: All relevant institutions, both national and international, continue to invest in reproductive health, maternal, infant health, children, youth and special nutrition, please support the skills and training of health officials / staff, including local authorities, educators, community outreach. To gain real knowledge and skills.
"Currently, Cambodia is developing and Cambodia is moving in the right direction," he added. The richer the people, the more educated and healthier they are.
