(Battambang): Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Battambang Province and the delegation of Chan Borei Province led by Mr. Monsithy Phay San Thunavat, Governor of Chanthaburi Province on 16 February 2023, met to discuss to strengthen cooperation between the two provinces (Battambang). - Chan Borey).
On that occasion, Mr. Sok Lou thanked for the presence of Mr. Monsit Phay San Thunwat, who took the time to lead the delegation to pay a courtesy call and discuss the work between the Battambang Provincial Administration and Chan Borei Province on the territory of Battambang Province.
The provincial governor praised the joint efforts to increase mutual understanding and friendship between Battambang and Chanthaburi provinces, which have helped the economic growth of people living in the border areas of the border provinces.
He said that the friendship and solidarity between the people of Cambodia and Thailand is a good traditional friendship, and through this, Battambang and neighboring provinces have promoted cooperation in all areas in line with the policies of the Royal Government. And a Memorandum of Understanding between the two parties and in accordance with the common objectives agreed upon by both parties.
The meeting between the administration of Battambang and Chan Borei at this time is very important that the two sides have met in the past, but due to the situation of the Kovid-19 epidemic, the talks between the two sides failed. Rarely met.
However, the relations between the two provinces continue to work together to enhance closer working relations and promote development on the basis of equality and mutual benefit within their jurisdiction and in accordance with the law. Country norms of both sides. Mr. Mao Thunin considers the integration of the family members of the people as a good mechanism to contribute to resolving disputes out of court (Video inside)
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Mao Thunin, the current Governor of Kampot Province, is recognized by the people as a provincial leader who has the ability to resolve various disputes for the local people outside the judiciary. This amazement is from the time he was the governor of Pursat and continues to Kampot today.
In the press conference of the Spokesperson of the Royal Government on "Five Years of Success of Kampot Provincial Administration" this morning, February 16, 2023, Mr. Mao Thunin shared some experiences and mechanisms that are the beacon. In resolving disputes outside the court system for the people. He added that most of the disputes that occur at the local level are about small land in the family or those who live in the same village.
One mechanism that he thinks is an important contribution to solving people's problems is to introduce himself as a member of the people's family by treating them as children, brothers and sisters, etc., which gives him more opportunities. To find out the real situation in the families of the people, especially when there is a dispute.
Mr. Mao Thunin continued that when he came to the position of Governor of Kampot, the first thing he had to learn was to meet with government officials and people in all localities and people consider him a family member. Theirs too. He said that the role of the provincial governor is just a name, but the family hierarchy is an important thing.
The governor of Kampot province said, "In Kampot, there are 170,000 families. I ask you to include me as another family member in every family as a child, brother, sister, father, grandson in every family, just have a role "As the provincial governor, this is an opportunity to contribute to resolving I would like to emphasize that the family hierarchy is able to contribute to the mechanism of out-of-court settlement."
As a result, for Kampot province, the settlement of disputes outside the court system from October 18, 2021 to December 31, 2022, the provincial governor and the city-district administration facilitated the resolution of complaints and other requests to the people. A total of 1,158 cases provided financial support and rice to 15,780 poor people, equivalent to 1,578 families.
Another thing that he thinks is also an important part is that people need to have confidence, trust and warmth in the authorities that there is transparency, fairness and justice. He added that when going to resolve the dispute, he also brought with professional officials from the provincial level to the local level, plus living witnesses to be clear in resolving.
