Mr. Mao Thunin said this at a press conference on "Five years of success of the Kampot provincial administration" at the Office of the Council of Ministers on February 16, 2023.
He said that currently there are two companies that are investing in growing yellow bananas in Kampot province, providing employment to about 2,000 Cambodians. The banana plantation not only provides income from export to international and local markets as well as job creation, but also as a tourist destination, with many tourists visiting the area to grow bananas.
He pointed out that the yellow bananas of Kampot province have a sweet and delicious taste due to three factors: fertile soil, irrigation water, a type of waterfall without chemicals and weather factors that make bananas a beautiful color.
He added that due to the good market for yellow bananas, the company also plans to expand the cultivated area.
Mr. Chan Rith, Director of Kampot Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, said that yellow bananas were grown on 1,063 hectares, of which 661 hectares were harvested with a yield of 43 tons. Each year, the crop exports more than 200,000 tons.
The yellow banana is the first fruit of Cambodia to be officially allowed to be exported to the Chinese market, starting for the first time in 2019.
