Siem Reap to stop open defecation before 2025
(Siem Reap): On 16 February 2023, Siem Reap Provincial Authority held a provincial meeting on action planning and strengthening procedures for working groups to end defecation, have access to clean water and live in an environment. Highly hygienic.
The ceremony was also attended by His Excellency Dr. Chrun Therawat, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Rural Development, Mr. Ung Kimleang, Deputy Governor of Siem Reap Province and Mr. Under Secretary of State, Mr. and Mrs. Partner organizations as well as commune councils and many trainees.
Following the attention of Mr. Yi Kim Than, Deputy Director of the International Music Organization, Mr. Ung Kim Leang, Deputy Governor of Siem Reap Province, urged the Department of Rural Development and the municipal, district, commune and sangkat authorities to expedite the completion of open defecation before the end of the year. 2025.
Mr. Ung Kimleang continued that throughout Siem Reap, there are three districts that have completed the defecation, with concern for the municipalities, districts, communes adjacent to the Tonle Sap Lake on the use of clean water and defecation. Challenges remain.
Dr. Chrun Therawat said that there are three districts in Siem Reap that stopped defecation in Veal Peal province, and six communes in the six districts adjacent to the Tonle Sap Lake still face challenges in sanitation and water use.
He also agreed with the provincial authorities to urge the Department of Rural Development and the municipal, district, commune and sangkat authorities to expedite the completion of open defecation before 2025. To achieve this plan, local authorities at all levels, as well as partner organizations, work to deepen public awareness of sanitation and clean water to consider the health of citizens.
