I would like to draw the public's attention from the point of view of state governance. This is a very big case because VOD has undermined the confidence of government institutions. The impact on Samdech Techo Hun Sen, His Excellency Hun Manet or other public officials is not limited to private individuals or only to the accused, but also to the accountability, cleanliness and trust of State governing body.
Why not affect state institutions?
Under the laws of all countries, harm to public institutions or individuals is more severe than harm to private individuals. Legal experts may have a more detailed explanation of the reasons for this. But simply put, this is because trust in state institutions is indispensable for the authorities or public institutions in providing public services to the people and governing the country.
Let me give you an easy-to-understand example of Kovid disease management. In dangerous circumstances, if the media says that Cambodia is a Chinese puppet government, taking the Chinese substandard vaccine that Europe does not recognize to its people, will the people receive the vaccine at the request of the government?
This accusation has two dangers. The first is affecting the dignity of state institutions that are incapable of considering the scientific balance in public health management. The second is to seriously affect and hinder the overall actions of the authorities in managing health security.
If we look at it from one angle, it can be said that it is the right to freedom of the press or the right to freedom of expression, but if we look at it from another angle, it affects the accountability and responsibility of state institutions for the welfare of the people, making people lose faith in the authorities and hinder To fulfill the government's obligation to protect the health of the entire population. This case is not a right of expression.
Disbelief in government is an individual right, but destroying the trust of state institutions by compromising the integrity and integrity of public institutions or individuals is not an individual right. And even more so, it is not a right to freedom of expression or a professional press with responsibility before the law.
What VOD says to the public is a statement that implies the dignity of HE Hun Manet. From what the public has read or listened to VOD, the public will surely understand and judge that HE Hun Manet has not yet taken office, he has already abused his position.
Do not use your emotions to judge, do not easily package issues into the basket of human rights, press freedom or freedom of expression too quickly. The country has laws, check all aspects of the law and weigh which one is heavier. For all civilized citizens, rights are always associated with duty. Do not be fooled into demanding your rights and forgetting your obligations as a citizen under the Constitution.
