According to the ambassador, before the 1940s, China was the largest tourist destination in Cambodia. In fact, in 2019, Cambodia received about 2.46 million Chinese tourists, accounting for 35.7% of the total number of international tourists, and increased revenue by about 1.8 billion US dollars. In particular, in January 2023, the number of Chinese tourists visiting Cambodia reached 25,000.
