Acting Head of State Hosts Dinner in Honor of German President and Lok Chumteav
The banquet was also attended by Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and senior dignitaries from the Senate, National Assembly and the Royal Government.
Addressing at the banquet in the name of His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum expressed his excitement and gratitude to the President of the Federal Republic of Germany. Chosen Cambodia as the destination for an official visit from 14 to 16 February 2023.
Samdech stated that based on the history of the two countries, since the establishment of diplomatic relations between the two countries on November 15, 1967, no high-ranking German presidential dignitaries have visited the Kingdom of Cambodia until now. This. The President is the first dignitary of the Federal Republic of Germany to pay a historic official visit to Cambodia today.
Samdech continued that the Cambodian people have known Germany well and have a deep affection for the German people for a long time. Therefore, Samdech would like to encourage both governments to work hard to promote people-to-people exchanges. Expand each other and encourage the two governments to make more efforts in trade, economy, investment and tourism for the common economic growth.
In his speech, the Acting Head of State thanked the German government for providing assistance for demining in Cambodia. The Royal Government of Cambodia has set the goal of a landmine-free Cambodia by 2025. In addition, in the spirit of humanitarian assistance, Cambodia has helped train deminers from Ukraine in collaboration with Japan. So German aid for demining is invaluable.
With this, the Prince would like to express his deepest gratitude to the German government and people for providing enormous development assistance since 1994, contributing significantly to the socio-economic development of Cambodia.
The Acting Head of State praised the talks between the President and the President, as well as the fruitful discussions in the spirit of deep friendship.
In particular, the President of the Federal Republic of Germany stated that he was pleased that he was the first President of the Federal Republic of Germany to visit Cambodia and have the opportunity to get to know the spirit and soul of Cambodia.
