(Phnom Penh): Professor Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, on February 15, 2023, presided over the ceremony of recognizing the composition of the Board of Directors and assuming the position of Director of Luang Mey Hospital.
The Minister of Health expressed his warm congratulations on the occasion of the Royal Government of Cambodia's appointment of Dr. Ngov Kang, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health as the Chairman of the Council and all members, All management now.
Prof. Mam Bunheng added, "On behalf of the leadership of the Ministry of Health and on my own behalf, I would like to thank the leadership, civil servants, staff at all levels and stakeholders who have worked hard to prepare for the transformation of Luang Mey Hospital. Became the first oncology clinic in Cambodia.
The Minister of Health emphasized that under the wise leadership, long-term vision and realism of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Cambodia achieved high economic growth at an average annual rate of about 7% between 2010 and 2010. 2019.
Although the Kovid 19 crisis has slowed economic growth by 2020, the introduction and implementation of drastic and effective administrative and health measures, coupled with the successful implementation of the Nationwide Vaccine-19 Campaign, has made Cambodia a success. A high level of community immunity has allowed Cambodia to open up socio-economic activities in all areas before many countries in the region and globally since the end of 2021.
At the same time, the introduction and implementation of the strategic framework and programs to restore and promote Cambodia's economic growth to live with Kovid 19 in the new normal path for 2021-2023 has resulted in a recovery of Cambodia's economic growth rate of about 3%. 2021 and is expected to achieve a growth rate of more than 5% in 2022 and about 6% in 2023.
Permission to open socio-economic activities in all areas is also due to the efforts of the leaders, civil servants, staff at all levels of the Ministry of Health and stakeholders who sacrificed their personal well-being in military service. Fight against Kovid 19 disease, which devastated the human and economic resources of the world.
On that occasion, the Minister of Health also recalled some of the background of the establishment of Luang Mae Hospital and provided some ideas and support activities to the Board and management of Luang Mae Hospital and relevant units in the implementation of joint work. Contains:
1. Continuing and accelerating the implementation of activities to organize Luang Mey Hospital as a specialized hospital for cancer treatment to be ready to receive patients for consultation and treatment. 2: Relevant units under the Ministry of Health must pay attention and cooperate with Highly with the management and team of Luang Mae Hospital to speed up the hospital process.
3. Strengthen the structure and develop the capacity of the hospital to be able to carry out its core work, improve the education of the memory of health officials, good practice in accordance with professional ethics and appropriate behavior with the people.
4: Maintain the equitable values of health services based on two main principles: First, there must be health care services and those services can be used when needed. Second: Ensure that no one is Abandoned and did not receive health care services at the time of the plague and upon arrival at the hospital due to inability to pay the service fee.
The President made this remark at a banquet hosted by Acting Head of State Samdech Say Chhum on the afternoon of February 15, 2023.
The German President is the first German president to pay a historic visit to Cambodia since Cambodia and Germany formally established ties on November 15, 1967. The visit is considered an important visit to a new stage of relations and cooperation between Cambodia and Germany.
The head of state, Say Chhum, said at the dinner that the president's visit reflected the deep friendship with the President and his wife, as well as the German people towards the Cambodian people.
"This visit shows the importance of maintaining the existing friendship and close cooperation between the people of the two countries to a new level to bring about mutual benefits. "Great for the people and the two countries." This is the emphasis of Samdech Say Chhum, Acting Head of State.
During the dinner, the German President also expressed his pleasure to be the first German President to visit Cambodia and have the opportunity to get to know the spirit and soul of Cambodia.
The President also expressed satisfaction that Germany and Cambodia have further expanded their partnership.
"We do not always have to have the same opinion on everything, but we can deepen the dialogue that is respectful and honest between our partners." This is the emphasis of the President.
"In the discussions, we are not only exchanging views on a political level, but also on economic and social ties, and on the relationship between the people of our two countries," he added.
Please note that Cambodia and Germany were officially connected on November 15, 1967. The relationship was severed in 1975 and re-established on February 12, 1992.
In 55 years of official relations, no high-ranking German presidential official has visited Cambodia. This is the first visit by a German president to Cambodia.
Although there has been little exchange of top-level leadership visits, Germany is a country that has a lot of cooperation with Cambodia and has also contributed a lot to Cambodia.
The report shows that since the establishment of full relations in 1992, Germany has provided a total of 710 million US dollars in technical and financial assistance to Cambodia.
Germany also provided cooperation and assistance in areas such as education, health, demining, elections, and the Khmer Rouge tribunal.
Of the 27 EU member states, Germany has the largest trade volume with Cambodia. According to the report, in 2022, the trade volume between Cambodia and Germany will be about $ 1.247 billion, an increase of about 4% compared to 2019.
Of that, Cambodia exported to Germany more than 1 billion dollars and imports from Germany only about 163 million dollars.
