The Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province said, "There are a total of 1,006 buildings in Sihanoukville, of which 359 have been abandoned due to 19 problems since the beginning of 2020. Another 89 buildings are undergoing daily repairs and another 255 have been completed but are not in operation. In particular, 303 buildings are running businesses that provide both jobs and income to the state.
As a mechanism to resolve or find a way with the owner of the building, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun said that the Ministry of Economy and Finance is currently setting up a working group to resolve the deadlock. He added that the ministry has already met several times on behalf of technical officials, which is now in the process of asking for guidelines from the leadership of both the Ministry and the Royal Government.
However, for the mechanism of solving, the provincial governor has not yet been able to inform, he just revealed that all these problems will be solved in the future, including the provision of some favors to The owner of the building project as well.
