Senior Cambodian official in charge of attracting investment explains to German investors about Cambodia's investment opportunities
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Secretary General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, with the participation of representatives of relevant ministries and institutions, on the afternoon of February 15, 2023, met with a German business delegation led by Michael Kellner, Secretary of State at the German Ministry of Economy and Environment.
The Minister informed the delegation about Cambodia's open investment environment, which allows foreign investors to invest in all sectors without requiring the participation of local investors.
He informed the delegation about the main contents of the Investment Law of the Kingdom of Cambodia, which was promulgated on October 15, 2021, such as priority areas that received incentives.
He also said that in order to help promote Cambodia's economic diversification towards high value-added sectors, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has decided to implement the roadmap for the development of Cambodia's automotive and electronics sector. On December 9, 2022.
He said the German government has been encouraging German investors to diversify their investment destinations by investing in Southeast Asian countries.
In this regard, he hopes that the German investors who are visiting Cambodia now will seize the opportunity from the open and favorable investment environment to invest in Cambodia. During the meeting, the German business delegation introduced its business activities and raised many questions related to its business opportunities in Cambodia.
German President Praises Samdech Techo Hun Sen's Leadership
Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Samdech Techo's personal assistant, said that during the meeting, the German President thanked Samdech Techo Prime Minister for the warm welcome and informed Samdech Techo that he was very honored to visit Cambodia. Especially as the first German president to visit Cambodia.
The President informed Samdech Techo about his visit to the demining center in Siem Reap, and what he saw was that demining has saved people's lives and helped people to live and grow crops as well as Livelihood on those lands.
The President informed Samdech Techo that Germany's participation in demining activities in Cambodia was meaningful and correct.
The President also informed Samdech Techo about the visit to the temples in Angkor, which is a rich and wonderful cultural treasure and in need of maintenance. The German President expressed his pleasure and appreciation for the cooperation in the field of culture and the preservation of temples for the past 25 years. The president stressed that this cooperation will continue.
During the meeting, the President also briefed Samdech Techo on Germany's ambitions to combat climate change and its intention to expand cooperation with Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, briefed the German President on demining work in Cambodia, which must be cleared by 2025, and the demining process in some countries under the auspices of the United Nations, along with military training. Ukraine on demining, which is a human job, so that the enemy does not hide his face, causing problems for innocent people.
In this regard, Samdech Techo expressed his satisfaction with the assistance of the German Federation for the past 25 years. Samdech Techo also expressed his pleasure and encouraged cooperation in the field of global climate change as an investment and trade between the two countries.
