In a press conference held by the Royal Government Spokesperson on the "Five Years of Success of the Sihanoukville Administration", Mr. Kouch Chamroeun confirmed that the construction of the deep-sea port is currently in the process of selecting a company to build.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun said, "The construction of the first phase of deep-sea port is recruiting companies to open in June 2023. "What we have done at this stage is just to prepare the site to allow the winning bidder to start construction will be completed by the end of 2025."
It should be informed that this deep water port development project can be a large port, provide easy transportation and reduce transportation costs to be low in the future. Sihanoukville Autonomous Port in the first phase, with a length of 350 meters and a water depth of 14.5 meters, with a loan of more than $ 200 million from Japan.
When the deep-sea port is completed by 2025, it will be able to allow ships with a capacity of more than 4,000 containers to dock, at which time about 93% of ships in Asia will dock in Cambodia. Provide a lower shipping cost, which is estimated to be less than $ 200 per container.
Currently, the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port can only accommodate only 18% of ships in the Asia-Pacific region, meaning that out of 100 ships, only 18 or 19 ships can dock and only 1,500 container vessels are allowed. .
