Cambodian People's Party and Lao People's Revolutionary Party vow to fight color revolution together
(Phnom Penh): The leaders of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) who are leading Cambodia and the leaders of the Lao People's Revolutionary Party (CPP) have vowed to work together to fight the color revolution and not allow anyone to take the territory of the two countries to act against the regime. Of both countries.
This position was expressed in the meeting of the top leaders of the two parties led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party and Mr. Thongloun Sisoulit, Secretary General of the Central Committee of the Lao People's Revolutionary Party on 14 February. In 2023, during Samdech Techo's visit to Laos.
According to the press release of the Cambodian People's Party, the meeting was held in a warm, friendly, understanding and trusting atmosphere to continue to build solidarity, traditional friendship and cooperation in all fields between the party and Both countries to deepen and bear fruit.
Both sides highly appreciated and expressed their sincere appreciation for the continuous development of solidarity, traditional friendship and cooperation between the two countries, which has promoted the level of comprehensive and long-term strategic partnership.
In addition, the two sides agreed to jointly fight the activities of the color revolution by promoting the implementation of the law and not allowing any organization to act against or use its territory against the country of the other party.
The two sides agreed to continue to strengthen the friendship, solidarity and cooperation between the two parties and the two countries, as well as the three countries, Cambodia, Laos and Vietnam, for the national interests of the three countries and the people of the two countries. Each contributes to the cause of peace, stability, friendship, cooperation and development in the region and the world.
