(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, on February 15, 2023, confirmed that the Phnom Penh-Bavet Expressway project has not been canceled or postponed as negotiations have been completed. All concession agreements or agreements between the private and public sectors (PPP).
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said that the agreement was usually signed after a bilateral meeting between Prime Minister Samdech Techo Prime Minister and Prime Minister Li Keqiang, but that China's internal procedures were slow to be completed due to Kovid and due to the Chinese New Year, so there is a slight delay in the preparation of internal documents.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol stated, "Please be clear that there is no cancellation or delay in the construction of the Phnom Penh-Bavet Expressway. Please be clear if we want to sign tomorrow, but the Prime Minister "China, you can not testify because the internal procedures have not been completed."
In addition, the Senior Minister said that Samdech Techo Hun Sen had made a request to the Chinese side to help speed up the procedure, but the company promised to Samdech Techo Hun Sen to open the construction site by June 2023 at the latest. Completed in 2027, parallel to the expressway from Hop Chi Minh to Mok Bai will be connected in 2027.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said the project was a public-private partnership as CRBC would build a 135-kilometer road east of the Mekong River to Bavet. The Cambodian side will build a bridge across the Mekong River because Samdech Techo wants people who cross from the west to Lvea Em on the east to use the bridge without having to pay.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also stressed that the bridge must also be completed when the Phnom Penh-Bavet Expressway is completed.
Please note that the second Phnom Penh-Bavet Expressway will open construction in the middle of 2023 with a construction budget of $ 1.638 million.
According to Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, the expressway is important in connecting China to Burma, Thailand, Cambodia and Vietnam via ASEAN Road No. 1, which Cambodia is beginning to expand from two lanes to four lanes from Poipet to Phnom Penh. And connect from Phnom Penh to Bavet on the second expressway to make the goods and passengers from China to Vietnam can pass.
President of the Electricity Authority of Cambodia: The state will lose about $ 200 million in electricity in 2022, even if the loss does not increase the price!
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Yim Viseth, President of the Electricity Authority of Cambodia, said that for 2022, the Royal Government has issued a loss on electricity of about 200 million US dollars, but the state announced not to increase the price of electricity to all consumers for 2023. .
This statement was made by the President of the Electricity Authority of Cambodia on the morning of February 15, 2023, when he gave an interview to the media at the opening ceremony of the General Assembly to summarize the end of 2022 and set the direction for implementation for 2023. Of the Electricity Authority of Cambodia.
"In 2022, it was estimated at $ 200 million, and for 2023, we do not know, now our economy is recovering, so electricity consumption is increasing, we know that 2022 is now a loss of energy," he said. "Ours is starting to grow more, so it means more losses, but the government has decided not to raise prices."
