Duke Kith Meng Asks Kuwaiti Ambassador to Encourage Kuwaiti Investors to Invest in Rice, Energy, Oil and Gas in Cambodia
The talks focused on boosting trade and investment between the two countries.
The Ambassador briefed the President on the intention of the Embassy of Kuwait to cooperate with the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce to promote trade and relations between the two countries' business communities in key areas, especially energy and rice exports from Cambodia to Kuwait. .
Meanwhile, the Kuwaiti Chamber of Commerce invited Duke Kith Meng to lead a delegation from the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce to Kuwait at an appropriate time. In addition to economic and trade cooperation, the Kuwaiti Embassy also conducts humanitarian activities with associations in Cambodia.
Separately, the Ambassador informed about the opening of the Saudi Embassy in Cambodia in the near future.
Duke Kith Meng warmly welcomed the purpose of the cooperation stated by the Ambassador and emphasized that Cambodia is rich in rice products that can supply the Kuwaiti market and Cambodia needs Kuwaiti expertise in the energy sector, in particular. Oil and gas.
The President requested the Ambassador to encourage Kuwaiti investors to invest in the above sectors and informed them about Cambodia's economic growth, potential sectors and peace and stability in Cambodia, which are important factors for investors. In addition, the President Duke proposed to promote tourism between the two countries.
The Duke will lead a delegation on a business visit to Kuwait at an appropriate time and welcome cooperation in all fields with the Kuwaiti Embassy, including humanitarian activities.
