Bank of Thailand wants household debt below 80% of GDP
BANGKOK: The central bank wants to see household debt levels below 80 percent of gross domestic product (GDP) to help reduce economic and financial risks, the central bank said. According to Reuters.
Thailand's household debt accounted for 86.8 percent of GDP in the third quarter of 2022, one of the highest in Asia.
Debt levels above 80 percent of GDP could put a strain on long-term economic growth and jeopardize the country's financial stability, she said. According to Reuters.
