This was stated by Senior Minister Sun Chanthol at the opening ceremony of the meeting to review the work results in 2022 and the work direction for 2023 of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport on the topic of "Continuing to improve the quality of infrastructure construction and transportation system. Effective, sustainable environment and human resource development "on February 15, 2023.
He pointed out that the ministry has now completed its studies to convert ordinary railways into high-speed rail links from Thailand to Laos and to China to facilitate faster transport of goods and tourists.
According to the senior minister, this high-speed railway can travel at a speed of 160 km to 200 meters per hour, equivalent to the speed of the railway in Laos, while the width of the track will be extended from one meter to 1.43 meters.
The study of the high-speed railway project follows the recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, who has previously recommended that the Ministry of Public Works and Transport and the Ministry of Economy conduct a study on the railway by converting it from a normal railway to a railway. High speed. The project is also backed by Chinese President Xi Jinping.
According to the senior minister, the high-speed rail will also play an important role in transporting tourists.
