"Wrong decisions lead to loss of opportunities, affect employees!
I follow the VOD case for several days until I synthesize the comment. First of all, on behalf of the Cambodian people, I would like to express my support for the actions of the Royal Government under the leadership of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia, in deciding for the Ministry of Information to revoke the VOD license. These days.
Indeed, I would like to emphasize that I also like to monitor and value information, whether the entity is biased or independent. On the other hand, I also do not support the production of false information, sometimes with the intention of slandering for the sake of something. Speaking of the VOD case, I noticed that Samdech Techo was not reluctant to revoke the license immediately, leaving a 72-hour deadline for VOD to apologize.
I do not say that VOD is not responsible, but the first response did not meet the requirements of the prince, only the second letter dared to use an apology, but too late. It can be said that it was a slow decision of the VOD leadership that led to the implementation of the law.
If I remember correctly, Samdech Techo also used to give a slogan to Cambodian journalists in the spirit of strengthening the profession and increasing the trust of the public, the audience, full of meaning: "Journalists do not violate the rights of others. Do not distort the truth and publish only true information, do not fabricate mistakes on others.
In that, I would like to express my support for the majority of journalists who have followed the law on the press and have the right professional ethics, and I also do not support a small number of journalists who do not respect the law, do not respect the profession and do not have Responsible when it is published incorrectly, do not dare to use only the apology, as the old saying goes, cheap, expensive, expensive.
Likewise, I do not support the media, which is created under the banner of the press, but with the intention of inciting and causing national disintegration. That is, it is not a political weapon. For me, I still believe that if we follow the profession, ethics and the law in force, we will avoid legal challenges, otherwise Samdech Techo asked the Ministry of Information to establish a lawyer to help protect the right journalists. "
