Through social media, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said: "Because the VOD radio was shut down and there was no opportunity to reopen, and considering the lives of employees who lost their jobs due to the fault of the leader. I decided to provide a state framework for those who wish to serve in the state.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen requested VOD staff to liaise with the Ministry of Public Works to apply for a job, and the Minister of Public Works must accept the application and distribute it to other ministries in accordance with their specialties and request a final decision from Samdech.
Samdech asked all foreigners not to interfere in the internal affairs of Cambodia, and Samdech would like to confirm that there will be no change in Cambodia's decision.
"Foreigners have no right to order us to do this or do that according to their wishes, because this is our internal affairs," he said. "The closure of an unethical radio station will not only kill the freedom of the press in Cambodia, but will also help enforce the law and strengthen the journalistic ethics of the media in Cambodia."
Please be informed that on the morning of 13 February 2023, the Ministry of Information issued a proclamation announcing the revocation of the broadcasting license of the Cambodian Center for Independent Media (CCIM), which was the VOD's broadcast management center, after the newspaper distorted that Mr. Hun Manet is the signatory on behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen in providing assistance to Turkey.
The decision to close came after Samdech Techo Hun Sen ordered the Ministry of Information to revoke the VOD license and to end broadcasting by 10 a.m. on February 13, 2023, after receiving a letter. An explanation from VOD that Samdech considered unacceptable and not an apology letter. One apartment and one bathroom of Ponleu Anakot were officially inaugurated
(Rattanakiri): Mr. Nhem Sam Oeun, Governor of Rattanakiri Province, this morning, February 14, 2023, inaugurated an apartment building and a bathroom of Ponleu Anakot Organization, located in Phnom Svay Village, Boeung Kanseng Sangkat, Banlung City.
