Valentine's Day! President of the National AIDS Authority calls for non-discrimination against people living with HIV and LGBT people
On that occasion, the Senior Minister visited the exhibition booths, such as men having sex with men and beautiful women. In front of the Gay Men (MSM) group, the senior minister encouraged the activists to continue to pay attention to giving a broader message to the gay and lesbian (TG) group.
"What we want is for LGBT people to be free of HIV, because the rate of HIV transmission among men who have sex with men has been steadily increasing and the rate is as high as 4%," he said. Compared to the infection among the general population, which is only 0.6%.
The head of the National AIDS Authority has encouraged men who have sex with men to increase their chances of getting the most out of it by using condoms or taking pre-sex pills (PreP). Do not forget that homosexuals can also get HIV if they are not protected.
On that occasion, T-shirts, leaflets, HIV and AIDS education leaflets were distributed, free blood tests for HIV and free condoms were distributed.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen pays a working visit to Laos on February 13, 2023. The current visit to Laos is an important visit to enhance relations and set out an action plan for expanding cooperation between the two countries.
The bilateral meeting between Samdech Techo PM and Sorn Sai Siphandon, Prime Minister of Laos, focused on a wide range of issues, including politics, security, national defense, border affairs and the fight against transnational crime, economics and society. And investment, air connectivity, tourism, energy and education, etc. Refers to further deepen the friendly relations and brotherhood between Cambodia and Laos.
The two sides expressed satisfaction over the strong friendly relations and good cooperation between the two countries after the establishment of diplomatic ties in 1956, which has been around for 67 years. Comprehensive and long-term strategic partnership ”in 2019.
The two leaders also noted with satisfaction that bilateral trade has increased from 160 million US dollars in 2021 to 210 million US dollars in 2022.
Samdech Techo informed Sorn Sai about Cambodia's new investment law, which provides better conditions and a favorable environment for foreign investors, and encouraged the two sides to speed up the conclusion of negotiations on the Double Taxation Agreement (DTA). To further boost bilateral trade and economic activity of the two countries.
The Prime Minister encouraged both sides to increase the organization of trade partners matching events, exhibitions and workshops to provide more opportunities for trade and investment between the two countries.
The two leaders welcomed the recovery of tourism and the reopening of direct flights from Luang Prabang - Pakse - Siem Reap on November 1, 2022 by Lao Airlines.
Samdech Techo requested Laos to reopen direct flights from Phnom Penh-Vientiane-Phnom Penh in order to contribute to the promotion of tourism, which is a potential sector and is playing an important role in contributing to the economic recovery of both countries after the disease. Infected Kovid 19.
Regarding cooperation in the field of education, Samdech Techo and Mr. Sorn Sai agreed to urge both sides to continue to exchange intellectuals, researchers, exchange works, publish research and organize programs to share knowledge and research between the Royal Academy of Cambodia and the Academy. Lao Social Sciences.
The two leaders urged the two sides to expedite the completion of a joint research on "Cambodia-Laos relations: history, culture and people-to-people contacts along the borders of the two countries and the preparation of a Lao-Khmer and Khmer-Lao dictionary to assist Facilitate the study of students from both countries.
On security and defense cooperation, the two leaders agreed to strengthen cooperation in the fight against transnational crime effectively by sharing information between border authorities in a timely manner.
Regarding energy cooperation, the two leaders agreed to urge the relevant ministries of the two countries to continue to effectively implement the existing Memorandum of Understanding and Agreements on Energy Cooperation between Cambodia and Laos. Ensure stability and energy security between the two countries.
Regarding border affairs, the two leaders were pleased with the progress of the Cambodia-Laos Joint Boundary Commission, which has demarcated and demarcated 121 border posts, equivalent to 86% of the common border, and agreed to resolve the remaining border issues. On the basis of mutual understanding and peace.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, considers Samdech's visit and current meeting with Lao leaders a historic event for both nations, as Samdech and Sorn Sai Siphandon have signed a state boundary treaty between Cambodia. And Laos.
Regarding regional and international cooperation, Samdech Techo and Mr. Sorn Sai exchanged views on cooperation in regional and international forums, especially within the framework of ASEAN and the United Nations.
The two leaders agreed to continue supporting each other in regional and international forums. Samdech Techo sincerely thanked the Government of Laos for supporting Cambodia's chairmanship of ASEAN in 2022. Samdech expressed Cambodia's full support for Laos as the chair of ASEAN in 2024.
After the bilateral meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen signed with the Prime Minister of Laos Sorn Sai Siphandon on the Cambodia-Laos Border Demarcation Treaty and the Action Plan for a Comprehensive and Long-Term Strategic Partnership between Cambodia and Laos. For the year 2023-2027.
In addition, the two Prime Ministers witnessed the signing ceremony of the minutes of the meeting of the Cambodia-Laos and Laos-Cambodia Joint Boundary Commission, signed by Mr. Var Kimhong, Senior Minister in charge of Border Affairs and Chairman of the Commission. Cambodia-Laos Joint Border and Mr. Salem Sarkommasit, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Foreign Affairs of Laos and Chairman of the Lao-Joint Boundary Commission.
During the current visit, Samdech Techo Hun Sen was also decorated by the Lao Head of State, Mr. Thongloun Sisoulith, with the "Phosay Lan Sang Medal".
The "Phosai Lan Sang Medal" is Laos' most valuable medal to be awarded to foreign leaders who have contributed to the promotion of friendly relations and good cooperation with Laos.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen is a leader who always pays high attention to strengthening the relationship, friendship and cooperation with the countries and villages around Cambodia. For Laos, not only did Samdech Techo receive high attention in strengthening friendships, relations and cooperation, but Samdech Techo always contributes to solving every time Laos encounters difficulties.
In 2021, when Laos was hit by the Kovid 19 outbreak, Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued to provide nearly 1 million doses of Kovid 19 vaccine, medical equipment and about 10 vehicles for vaccination. The budget that Samdech Techo helped to Laos totals more than 13 million dollars. Of that, more than 1 million dollars belongs to the Royal Government and 10 million dollars is the contribution of philanthropists through Samdech Techo.
Helping in this difficult time of Laos has made the Government and people of Laos give great respect to Samdech Techo, the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia and to the awarding of top-level medals to Samdech Techo Prime Minister.
"The pride I have now is the pride of all Cambodians and the great contribution of the government and the people of Laos in cultivating good traditional relations and cooperation," he said. "Every corner between the ministries, institutions, authorities at all levels of the two countries."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also reminded that the traditional friendship between Cambodia and Laos for centuries has become a comprehensive and long-term strategic partnership, which is a solid foundation for our two countries to achieve. Achievements are the fruits of cooperation in all fields.
Samdech Techo expressed his firm belief that this medal will have historical value, a unique symbol that reflects the strong ties between the leaders and people of the two countries.
It should be noted that in addition to awarding Laos 'top-level medals to Samdech Techo, the Lao government has also awarded Laos' top-level medals to six Cambodian duke tycoons who have funded the Lao government to address difficulties. There was also an outbreak of Kovid 19.
During his current visit to Laos, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also met with about 86 Cambodian students and trainees, both civilian and armed forces, who are studying in Laos.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo instructed all students and trainees to make an effort to absorb knowledge to serve the motherland.
Samdech Techo also reminded them to make efforts to maintain good relations with professors, students and the people of Laos.
