As the provincial governor, he continued, "We are always waiting to receive all the positive and negative information so that we can work together to solve the problem in a timely manner." Meeting with Japanese Ambassador to Cambodia, Phnom Penh Governor Highlights the Strength of Cambodia-Japan Diplomatic Relations
(Phnom Penh): Japan has strong diplomatic relations with Cambodia, while Japan is a country that has contributed significantly to bring peace to Cambodia with a large amount of grants and technical assistance. .
This was confirmed by Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh during a courtesy call with Mr. Oino Atsuzi, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of Japan to Cambodia this morning, February 14, 2023 at Phnom Penh Capital Hall. .
Mr. Khuong Sreng said that on behalf of the Cambodian people, he was very grateful to Japan for providing a grant to Cambodia with more technical assistance. Mr. Khuong Sreng continued that by not allowing Cambodia to repay the debt owed by the war with Japan's contribution to peace in Cambodia, it really made the diplomatic relations between the two countries Cambodia-Japan stronger and closer. Double up.
Mr. Khuong Sreng continued that under the assistance of Japan through Jaika, Phnom Penh was able to reduce the flooding in part. Cambodians are very satisfied with the development of Phnom Penh.
In addition, Mr. Khuong Sreng also mentioned the history of Cambodia, especially during the period when Cambodia fell under the Pol Pot regime, which caused the Cambodian economy to decline to zero. But after the liberation of the country from this regime by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, this poor country has developed continuously and continues to grow to this day and has made Cambodia more prominent on the international stage. Also.
Mr. Oino Atsuzi also mentioned that Japan and Cambodia have had diplomatic relations for about 70 years. In addition to good diplomatic relations, Japan is also a country that has contributed to bringing peace to Cambodia. He was very pleased with the rapid development of Phnom Penh, even though Cambodia had fallen to zero under the Khmer Rouge regime.
"In the phase of the Kovid-19 epidemic, whether in Cambodia or in Japan, the country's economy is in decline, but now in Cambodia, after the economy is back to normal," he said. Cambodia's economy is recovering, and Japanese investment in Cambodia is recovering.
He added that Japan has helped Phnom Penh solve the flood problem that this project has been successful. In particular, Japan has promised to help solve traffic problems with Phnom Penh so that traffic problems can be solved. The Embassy of Japan in Cambodia would like to continue to cooperate with Phnom Penh even better. Ministry of Culture calls on young people to use Valentine's Day in accordance with the traditional Khmer tradition
The Ministry of Culture says that February 14, which some people, especially Christians, have designated as Valentine's Day, has arrived. Currently, this day has been penetrating into the Cambodian society, especially among the youth, causing some people to accept and use it in a confusing way, leading to an impact on the culture, traditions and traditions.
According to the Ministry of Culture, in this context, the people, especially the youth of Cambodia, must study in depth to the traditional culture, which is the precious heritage of our ancestors, as well as to fully study the content and influence of external culture to integrate. Into the attitude and context of its society in order to maintain the existence of a noble nation that is thousands of years old in Asia.
(Lao): On the occasion of accompanying Samdech Techo Hun Sen on an official visit to Laos, Duke Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, led a delegation from the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce to meet with the Lao Chamber of Commerce and Industry this morning. February 14, 2023 in Vientiane.
The meeting focused on boosting economic ties between the two countries and exchanged views on opportunities, investment climate and potential sectors.
On this occasion, Duke Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, informed about the new investment law of Cambodia, which provides better conditions and a favorable environment for foreign investors.
"The two leaders agreed to expedite the negotiation of an agreement on the avoidance of double taxation to further boost bilateral trade and economic activity between the two countries," he said.
At the same time, the duke continued, "Samdech Techo encouraged both sides to increase the organization of business partnerships, exhibitions and seminars to provide more opportunities for trade and investment between the two countries." .
The leaders of the two countries 'chambers of commerce also discussed trade and investment ties between the two countries' companies, highlighting each other's potential. The leaders of the two countries' chambers of commerce will also continue to cooperate.
Mr. Udet Sovannavong, President of the Lao Chamber of Commerce and Industry, thanked Duke Kith Meng and members of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce for taking the time to demonstrate their potential and increase investment cooperation between Cambodia and Laos in line with their efforts. Top leaders pushing for increased trade for the benefit of both countries and their peoples.
The President of the Lao Chamber of Commerce also encouraged Cambodian investors to invest in Laos. At the same time, the Lao side also raised the issue of flight prices, which may make the number of tourists is not high due to high airfare.
In this regard, the Lao side asked Cambodia-Laos Airlines to consider the price issue if the low price is also a factor in promoting tourism.
After discussions between the leaders of the two countries' chambers of commerce, the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and the Lao Chamber of Commerce and Industry also agreed to sign a memorandum of understanding to boost business between the two countries, especially the exchange of information and policies. Recent politics.
