He noted with satisfaction and appreciation for the diplomatic relations between the two countries, which have evolved from the "Strategic Partnership" in 2013 to the "Comprehensive Strategic Partnership" in 2023, in conjunction with the celebration of the anniversary. 70th of Cambodia-Japan Diplomatic Relations.
The Commander-in-Chief thanked Japan for its support to Cambodia in the past, including the training of human resources, the construction of infrastructure, the training of the Cambodian Blue Hat Army, and the assistance of Cambodian workers to work in Japan.
