(Phnom Penh): Dr. Hor Sovathana, Deputy Director General of the Insurance Regulator of Cambodia, stated that joining the Cambodian Data Exchange Nursery from the insurance company is a vision of the potential of using digitalization to develop its insurance technology sector. And this participation is a new step to participate in the use as well as development and take advantage of what the Royal Government has already set out.
This was stated by Dr. Hor Sovathana on the afternoon of February 13, 2023, when she presided over the signing ceremony of the contract on the acceptance and implementation of the rules and procedures for membership in the data exchange nursery. Cambodia between the new "Techo" Business Training Center and FW UD Life Insurance (Cambodia) MK and MGA Asia Surin Broker Co., Ltd. (MGA).
Dr. Hor Sovathana added that on behalf of the insurance regulator to support the contract between the private sector and the Royal Government, the insurance regulator of Cambodia is a 10-year plan from 2021 to 2030, in which insurance technology is One of the principles that insurance regulators must develop as well.
