Details of the bilateral meeting between Samdech Techo and the Prime Minister of Laos (Video inside) (Vientiane, Laos): During the bilateral meeting between Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Mr. Sorn Sai Siphandon, Prime Minister of Laos Highly focus on expanding activities, relations and cooperation between the two countries to bring even greater benefits.
During the meeting, Samdech Techo Prime Minister stated that he was very pleased to lead a high-level Cambodian delegation to pay an official visit to Laos. Samdech Techo expressed his deep gratitude for the warm hospitality provided by the Government and the people of Laos to the Royal Government of Cambodia delegation.
Samdech Techo continued that the current visit is a testament to the traditional relationship, brotherhood and better cooperation between the two governments and peoples, which is an important contribution to strengthening the friendship and solidarity for development and well-being. Of both populations.
Samdech Techo expressed his appreciation for the strong friendly relations and good cooperation between the two countries after the establishment of diplomatic relations in 1956, which until now is about 67 years old, which has become " Comprehensive and long-term strategic partnership ”in 2019.
Mr. Sorn Sai and Samdech Techo had in-depth discussions in a friendly and understanding atmosphere on bilateral cooperation in all fields, including politics, security, national defense, border affairs and the fight against transnational crime, economy, society, trade and investment. Air connectivity, tourism, energy and education, etc. Refers to further deepen the friendly relations and brotherhood between Cambodia and Laos.
Samdech Techo informed Sorn Sai about Cambodia's new investment law, which provides better conditions and a favorable environment for foreign investors, and encouraged both sides to speed up the conclusion of negotiations on the Double Taxation Agreement (DTA). To further boost bilateral trade and economic activity of the two countries.
Samdech Techo requested Laos to reopen direct flights from Phnom Penh-Vientiane-Phnom Penh to contribute to the promotion of tourism, which is a potential sector and is playing an important role in contributing to the economic recovery of both countries after the disease. Infected Kovid 19.
It should be noted that after the bilateral meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen signed with the Prime Minister of Laos Sorn Sai Siphandon on the Cambodia-Laos State Boundary Treaty and the Action Plan for a Comprehensive and Long-term Strategic Partnership between Cambodia and Laos. Cambodia and Laos for 2023-2027.
In addition, the two Prime Ministers witnessed the signing ceremony of the minutes of the meeting of the Cambodia-Laos and Laos-Cambodia Joint Boundary Commission, signed by Mr. Var Kimhong, Senior Minister in charge of Border Affairs and Chairman of the Commission. Cambodia-Laos Joint Border and Mr. Salem Sarkommasit, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Foreign Affairs of Laos and Chairman of the Lao-Joint Border Commission.
