National Council for Social Protection organizes "Social Protection Week" 2023 to raise awareness and strengthen the transparency of the Cambodian social protection system
(Phnom Penh): The National Council for Social Protection organized a three-day "Social Protection Week" from 13 to 15 February 2023 to discuss strengthening the effectiveness and transparency of the Cambodian social protection system, which reflects The theme is "Good governance and public trust."
The forum will run for three full days from 13-15 February 2023, and after these three days, development partners, civil society organizations and other stakeholders are allowed and encouraged to continue to organize relevant programs. And social protection at the actual location and according to their ability for up to a whole week.
He added that "the progress we have made is due to the efforts of relevant ministries and institutions with the technical assistance of development partners, as well as the contribution of all stakeholders under the direct guidance of Samdech Techo." The Prime Minister, who has always considered the development of the social protection system as a priority policy of the Royal Government in the past and for the future.
Dr. John Narith, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Secretary General of the National Council for Social Protection, stated that the National Council for Social Protection has approved and implemented a series of national aid and social security programs in order to expand protection to Citizens for the better.
He said that by the end of 2022, the national social assistance program B and the existing social security system will continue to operate successfully and without any hindrance.
Recently, the Royal Government also approved and implemented a sub-decree on the regulation of the social security system to provide a basis for the start of the work of the social security regulator to strengthen the social protection system as a whole.
In particular, for the program to provide cash to poor and vulnerable families during the fight against Kovid-19, the Deputy Prime Minister stated that although the effect of Kovid-19 has now diminished, the Royal Government has decided to continue to implement this program. In 2023 to continue to support poor and vulnerable families in the rehabilitation phase.
