Many schools and administrative buildings across Auckland and the northern part of the North Island were closed on Monday and people were asked not to travel unless absolutely necessary. Forty-six,000 homes were cut off, public transport was disrupted, ferries and buses were suspended or reduced. Air New Zealand has canceled 509 flights and will resume flights on Tuesday if the weather improves.
Gabrielle is the second bad weather phenomenon to hit Auckland and New Zealand's North Island in just a few weeks. Last month, the city and surrounding areas were hit by flash floods that killed four people.
