Dr. Hun Manet's proposal after he saw that Cambodian children studying at international schools lacked understanding of the Khmer language and little understanding of Cambodian morals and customs.
Mr. Hun Manet's request and expression of concern was made on the occasion of announcing the composition of the new Board of Directors and awarding the 2022 Outstanding Teacher Award to the teachers and educators of the Education Services Federation of Cambodia on the 12th. February 2023.
In addition to worrying about Cambodian children studying at international schools who are illiterate in Khmer, Dr. Hun Manet is worried about Cambodian children who no longer understand the morals and customs of Cambodian people.
Dr. expressed his remarks that he used to see Cambodian children born in the United States to their parents when they have different opinions. But now he has also seen this situation in the lives of Cambodian children.
"Respect for elders, morals, and gratitude are human soft skills," he said. If people have only knowledge, but lose their identity, lose their culture, lose their value in Khmer. What do we do? ”
Dr. HUN Manet requested Mr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, to consider obligations in international schools to teach the Khmer language and to include moral education, Khmer traditions and customs for students. Especially from kindergarten to 12th grade.
He said that there is nothing wrong with just letting Cambodian children learn the Khmer language and understand the Khmer traditions and customs of the Khmer people.
For Hun Manet, strengthening the Khmer language and cultivating Khmer morality and culture does not affect the modernization of education.
