Chak Smok Analyst: Why did VOD not use the apology in its first letter? Do not continue to try to be a victim of abuse and betrayal of your profession and do not shed crocodile tears
They did not give an apology because it would damage the radio's reputation and show the unprofessionalism of the radio. That is why in his first letter, the word "sorry" was not in his letter of respect to Samdech Techo Hun Sen. This is a lesson for Cambodians who earn foreign salaries to serve a foreign political agenda. Everything has to go along the political lines set by the aid money given, without freedom and autonomy.
According to the facts and the law, VOD and its journalists have committed the most serious professional misconduct, and both Prime Minister Hun Sen and His Excellency Hun Manet are given the opportunity to abide by the code of ethics and the law in force. They continued to abuse their position by not presenting the alleged evidence and without correcting the articles they published, distorting or apologizing.
For this misrepresentation, HE Hun Manet requested VOD to correct and Samdech Techo Hun Sen's time to correct and publicly apologize to restore the honor and dignity of individuals and institutions of the Royal Government of Cambodia. Legal rights of individuals affected by published articles.
