Duke Kouch Mengly is awaiting a decision from the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia on the sale of shares
Despite the wait, the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia has already welcomed Mr. Kouch Mengly, who has listed his institution on the Cambodia Securities Exchange (SCX) and sold $ 10 million worth of shares through an initial public offering. IPO).
Mr. Kouch Mengly stated that "the price / share is under the approval of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia. The initial public offering of the IPO is expected to be officially approved by mid-March 2023. "We plan to raise up to $ 10 million, about 5.88% of our company."
Speaking at the seminar, Mr. Hong So Hour, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the General Director of the Stock Exchange of Cambodia, said that the Stock Exchange currently has 16 listed companies, nine of which are listed as shareholders and seven others are listed. Card. These 15 companies raised about 1.122 billion riel ($ 281 million) from the stock market.
The Cambodia Securities Exchange also expects large companies in Cambodia to be able to enter the securities market in the future.
Please be informed that Mr. Kouch Mengly intends to expand the school to 160 branches nationwide, while currently has 15 branches. His initial public offering is expected to begin in April 2023.
