During the meeting, Ms. Thong Sokuntheary, Cambodian Ambassador to Laos, expressed her deep gratitude for the great presence of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, who allowed Cambodian students to study in Laos to ask for Samdech's guidance on studying in the country. Laos.
According to the ambassador, Cambodian students studying in Laos are struggling with interest rates due to the declining Lao currency, making it difficult to exchange money.
She said students studying in Laos include majoring in architecture, civil engineering, computer science, environment, tourism, interior design, English literature and economics.
She said that in addition to students studying under the scholarship of the Ministry of Education, there are also students studying in the field of defense and the National Police.
Samdech Techo urged all students studying abroad, such as students studying in Laos, to study hard to bring that knowledge to serve their beloved country to the best of their ability. .
The Prime Minister also reminded all students to strive to do good deeds and to have good relations with professors, students and students. In particular, do good deeds with the people of Laos, participate in social work and know how to help each other, that is, when living together, to love them, when to leave each other, to remind them.
The Prime Minister also reminded all students to know how to monitor the evolving situation of the world and the situation in the country, especially to monitor and listen to what is really progress, do not believe in the deception of some thinkers who distort the truth. Cambodia's leadership and growth.
The Prime Minister also donated some funds to all students studying in Laos. Samdech Techo asked for understanding on the difficulties of students on the exchange rate in Laos due to the encounter and the crisis of Kovid 19.
Samdech Techo also mentioned the cooperation relations in all fields with Laos. Samdech Techo continued that Samdech's visit to Laos at this time, Samdech will have a discussion with the Lao side to strengthen the cooperation of Okukan, there will be more momentum and there will be a signing of the Cambodia-Laos border post. .
The Prime Minister also mentioned the promotion of cooperation with the Lao side on the promotion of aviation, tourism and electricity.
