The NEC states that all journalists must have a journalist identification card issued by the NEC. To obtain an identity card, a journalist must apply to register as a journalist directly at the NEC.
The application for registration as a national and international journalist with a permanent office in the Kingdom of Cambodia must be accompanied by:
An application for registration as an international journalist who does not have a permanent office in the Kingdom of Cambodia must be accompanied by:
* Copy of passport * Journalist ID card of the unit * Curriculum vitae with photo and 1 4x6 photo for ID card.
* A copy of the press card issued by the Ministry of Information or the Association of Journalists * The resume contains a photo and another 4x6 photo for identification * The last article was published in a legitimate newspaper during the year The last 3 articles.
