The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen led a high-level delegation to pay an official visit to Laos, accompanied by four Deputy Prime Ministers. The visit is at the invitation of Lao Prime Minister Son Sai Siphandon.
According to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia, during the visit, Samdech Techo will have a separate courtesy call with Dr. Thongloun Sisoulith, President of the Lao PDR and Dr. Sai Somphon Phumvihan, President of the Lao National Assembly. A courtesy call from the President of the Lao-Cambodian Friendship Association.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen will hold bilateral meetings with his Prime Minister Sorn Siphan Don to discuss ways to further expand bilateral cooperation in all areas, including security, politics, society and economy, and exchange views on regional issues. And international interests and common concerns.
After the meeting, the two Prime Ministers will hold a joint press conference on the outcome of the talks, and the Prime Minister of Laos will award medals to the presidents of a number of large private companies who have previously donated their funds to Laos When the Prime Minister of Laos visits Cambodia in 2021.
