New Japanese Ambassador to Cambodia Pledges to Strengthen Cambodia-Japan Parliamentary Cooperation
(Phnom Penh): On the occasion of paying a courtesy call on Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, on the morning of February 13, 2023, Mr. He pledged to work for closer ties between the two parliaments, as both Cambodia and Japan have now eased the Kovid-19 issue and the two countries' borders are open.
In addition, Mr. Ou Inouatsushi also praised the sacrifice and participation of the President of the National Assembly from the beginning. The Ambassador also congratulated Cambodia on its progress and success in hosting the ASEAN Summit and the recent ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly. He emphasized that for the upcoming 7th National Assembly election, the Royal Government of Japan is always ready to assist Cambodia.
On behalf of the National Assembly, Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin also expressed his pleasure and welcomed and congratulated Mr. Ou Ino Asushi, who was appointed by the Government of Japan as the Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of Japan to Japan. Kingdom of Cambodia.
Samdech emphasized that Japan has a great merit to contribute to the peace and development of Cambodia as it is today. This makes Japan a potential development partner of Cambodia. Samdech requested the Japanese side to continue to support the training of Cambodia's resources, which is to build human resources to participate in the development of the country.
