Samdech Techo Hun Sen Leads a Delegation to Laos
(Phnom Penh): After flying for about an hour at 9:20 am on Monday, February 13, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen led a high-level delegation to Laos safely. .
The arrival of Samdech Techo Prime Minister and the delegation was warmly welcomed by senior officials of the Lao Government, the Cambodian Ambassador to Laos and other key officials.
Samdech Techo's current visit lasts for two days from February 13 to 14 at the invitation of the Prime Minister of Laos, Sorn Sai Siphandon.
On the occasion of this visit, Samdech Techo Prime Minister will have a separate courtesy call with Dr. Thongloun Sisoulit, President of the Lao PDR and Dr. Sai Somphon Phumvihan, President of the Lao National Assembly, as well as receive a courtesy call from President of the Lao-Cambodian Friendship Association.
During his visit, the Prime Minister will hold bilateral meetings with his Prime Minister Sorn Siphandon to discuss ways to further expand bilateral cooperation in all areas, including security, politics, society and economy, and exchange. Comments on sub-regional, regional and international issues of common interest and concern.
After the meeting, the two Prime Ministers will sign the "Action Plan for a Comprehensive and Long-Term Strategic Partnership between Cambodia and Laos for 2023-2027."
It should be noted that during this visit, the Head of State of Laos will present the top level medal of Laos to Samdech Techo as well as the title of Duke Oknha, who provided Laos with funds for the fight against Kovid 19 in 2021. Banteay Meanchey Provincial Governor Proclaims Support for the Royal Government of Cambodia's Action to Revoke VOD Media Licenses to Strengthen Journalism and Eliminate False Information
