Dr. Hun Manet announces the composition of the new Board of Directors and awarded the 2022 Outstanding Teacher Award to the teachers and staff of the Education Service Federation of Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Dr. HUN Manet announced the composition of the new Board of Directors and awarded the Certificate of Excellence for the year 2022 to teachers and education staff of the Federation of Education Services in Cambodia on February 12, 2023.
At the same time, Dr. would like to congratulate the outstanding teachers who have actively served in the education and training of human resources in Cambodia with love, high responsibility and high professional conscience in the 2021 school year. This-2022.
* First: Train people to work with clarity, certainty and ensure sustainability * Second: Train people to be motivated and independent in their work * Third: Train to have a clear conscience in Help each other to succeed in all tasks in a positive competitive spirit.
All this can be achieved through education and training in both hard skills, which refer to specialties such as science, technology, engineering and mathematics, etc. And soft skills that refer to skills related to mindset, motivation, virtue, and morality. And the training of these two skills must go hand in hand from primary to secondary level.
He added that helping to preserve the Khmer national identity by placing Khmer language training as a mandatory language in private educational institutions is a top priority. In this sense, the promotion of deep learning of the Khmer language for students of Khmer nationality, as well as the addition of knowledge of the beautiful traditional culture that our Khmer people have always adhered to in order to make our next generation. Can maintain both its knowledge and its true identity.
