Heng Sour: VoD is an unprofessional, non-Khmer news organization, like foreign radio stations that oppose the Khmer people by always saying bad things about the Khmer people.
(Phnom Penh): Heng Sour, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and a young politician, said that VoD is an unprofessional, non-Khmer news organization, like foreign radio stations that are always anti-Khmer. Swearing about Khmer in both Khmer and English in order to reach out to the Cambodian hostile media and anti-Cambodian coalition groups abroad to further deceive in order to destroy Cambodia.
Heng Sour's political message came after the Royal Government decided to revoke the license of Voice of Democracy (VOD) on the night of February 12, 2023, after the radio station published an offensive and distorted article about Aid to Turkey.
"Does this unit never teach its staff to take a positive view of Cambodia and never use its network abroad to attract more investors or tourists to invest or to visit Cambodia?" This unit has never encouraged the Cambodian people and youth to love the nation, love peace, love social stability and participate more actively in work or study. This is an additional statement made by Mr. Heng Sour.
At the same time, Mr. Heng Sour announced his support for the revocation of the VoD radio license. He considers the revocation of the VOD license to be the implementation of the law and professional code of journalism in Cambodia in order to eliminate vague sources of false information, violate the rights of others, distort the truth and pass the knife to foreigners. The excuse to destroy Cambodia, the motherland of 17 million Cambodians.
