China says it has spotted an unidentified object flying near its port city and is preparing to shoot it down.
Employees of the Qingdao Maritime Development Bureau said the relevant departments were preparing to shoot down the object. But they were not told what the object was. Local fishermen are advised to stay extra safe, the report added.
On Saturday, US F-22 fighter jets shot down an unidentified object in Canadian airspace, a day after another unidentified object was shot down by the U.S. military. Alaska.
Beijing, meanwhile, claimed it was a normal civilian balloon used for meteorological research but was blown away from its planned trajectory, and China criticized the US decision to shoot down it. That is an excessive reaction.
Takeo Provincial Commissioner Chairs Security Strengthening Meeting in Prey Kabbas and Ang Borei Districts
(Takeo): Major General Chheang Phannara, Takeo Provincial Police Commissioner, on February 12, 2023, continued to chair a meeting on "Strengthening Security, Public Order and Social Security at Angkor Borei District Police Inspectorate and Prey Kabbas District Police Inspectorate". The meeting was attended by relevant police officers.
Remarking on that occasion, the Commissioner instructed the Deputy Commissioner for Planning Office to continue the meeting to strengthen the skills of the Inspectorate, the Administrative Police Post, to deal with criminal offenses, children, gambling, especially those who cause local aggression by organizing forces. Information agencies related to criminal security and drugs.
At the same time, preventive measures must be taken regularly in patrols on national roads, provincial roads, roads and complex geography in order to conduct timely and effective crackdowns to ensure the safety and security of local people. Continue to cooperate with relevant authorities, authorities at all levels to control explosive weapons on national roads and towns in order to track down the perpetrators of various crimes.
Regarding social media, the Commissioner instructed the Inspector to organize and encourage the monitoring group to post messages insulting the leadership, especially to continue to control the activities of organizations, associations, movements, political parties, collect information, images and content to keep as evidence for charge.
