The baht has appreciated about 2.7% against the dollar so far this year, becoming the second best-performing currency in Asia.
As export orders fall as global demand weakens, Arkhom says Southeast Asia's second-largest economy is supported by the recovery of its major tourism sector. Which is expected to receive more than 20 million foreign tourists this year.
The Ministry of Finance forecasts that in 2022, the Thai economy will grow by 3.8% this year from the previous forecast of 3%. The Thai government will release official data on 2022 gross domestic product (GDP) on February 17. According to the Bangkok Post. US wants China to speed up debt restructuring for developing countries
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - US Treasury Secretary Janet Yellen said on Thursday she wants China to take "faster action" to support debt restructuring for developing countries, especially Zambia. According to Reuters.
"China has delayed debt restructuring because of Beijing's demands for the World Bank, the International Monetary Fund and the International Monetary Fund," Yellen was quoted as saying by Reuters at an event at the Center for Strategic and International Studies in Washington. Other institutions are involved in debt reduction for countries facing debt crises.
But she said a wide range of questions, such as whether international financial institutions are involved in debt restructuring, are hampering progress on specific cases.
