Mr. Sok Voeun, Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Microfinance Association of Cambodia, explained that the financial institutions are currently drafting a joint credit agreement, which will establish a single standard with the same meaning and content as well as the rules, notices of Repayment of a loan, withdrawal of a plan or probability to a particular telephone number are completely the same, except for the interest rate or term of the loan.
He stressed that the purpose of this policy is to make it easier for customers to understand the content of the loan agreement before he thumbprinted the loan.
"And it is easier if in his community there are five families borrowing money, these five families get the same information, do not let the family borrow five different banks, five different meanings are difficult for him to understand. "If there is a common standard, five people will speak the same language, which will help him better understand the terms of the loan from banks and microfinance institutions."
He added that the common standard code would apply to loans up to $ 50,000. For loans from $ 50,000 to $ 100,000, those institutions are required to implement the same standard content (terms and conditions) required by the association to be included.
According to Mr. Sok Voeun, this joint standard contract code may be officially implemented in the second quarter of 2023.
Dr. Hong Vannak, an economist at the Royal Academy of Cambodia, told Fresh News that if borrowers receive the same services between individual financial institutions, it will be easier for both financial institutions, including borrowers. It is more complex, easy to understand the requirements of each institution and easy to make decisions.
He added, "Other benefits provide convenience and better opportunities for a wider range of borrowers, which makes it easier for them to access loans more effectively and efficiently." "There is no hassle because banks and microfinance have the same documents."
He added that the implementation of such principles also facilitates the policy of the National Bank of Cambodia in the management of the financial sector.
