According to Sok Chenda Sophea, joining CIPS is very important, which will facilitate cross-border payments as part of attracting Chinese investors, businesses and tourists.
In response to Samdech Techo Hun Sen's request, the Chinese President welcomed the proposal and urged the technical working group to review and study the cooperation.
The cross-border interbank payment system (CIPS) was officially launched in China in 2015 with the main goal of facilitating cross-border yuan payments as well as promoting the use of the Chinese currency in the international arena. .
The People's Bank of China (PBOC) began construction of the financial payment system in 2012. At the time of launch, the CIPS system had 19 direct participating institutions and 176 indirectly participating institutions in 50 countries and regions on six continents.
To date, by 2021, CIPS has operated 80 trillion yuan (US $ 12.68 trillion), with a total of 1,280 financial institutions in 103 countries and regions connected to the system. This. Six Suspects Arrested in Sihanoukville Involved in Drug Trafficking Case
