Samdech Techo Hun Sen led a high-level delegation to visit China on February 9 at the invitation of the Chinese government. The visit to mark the 65th anniversary of Cambodia-China relations, although short, has yielded remarkably high results.
On the first day of the visit, Samdech Techo Hun Sen allowed three major Chinese companies to build road and bridge infrastructure to pay a courtesy call. These three companies are companies that have been licensed to build roads and bridges in Cambodia and have also studied a number of other important infrastructure projects in Cambodia.
During the meeting, the company management informed Samdech Techo about the construction and operation of the Phnom Penh-Bavet Expressway, which was organized under the Public-Private Partnership (PPP) contract to implement the construction project in mid-2023 and planned. Completed in 2027, coinciding with the construction of Vietnam's Ho Chi Minh-Mok Bai Expressway, which is scheduled for completion in 2027.
The Chinese investors also briefed the Prime Minister on investing in inland waterway transport, investing in wastewater treatment in Sihanoukville and studying the Phnom Penh-Poipet high-speed rail line. The company also informed Samdech Techo about the project to invest in light and fast rail from Siem Reap to the new international airport in Chi Kreng in Siem Reap.
During the meeting, Samdech Techo Prime Minister also asked Chinese companies to study plans to invest in light and fast expressways from Phnom Penh to the new Phnom Penh International Airport and light rail lines in Phnom Penh, which are busy.
The two sides declared 2023, the 65th anniversary of the two countries' relationship, as a year of friendship, with activities to celebrate the anniversary. Cambodia and China have also launched a new cooperation called "Diamond Cooperation", which is another new cooperation. The new cooperation focuses on the pillars of politics, production, agriculture, energy and security.
Separately, Cambodia has announced a policy 1: adhere to a Chinese policy, 2: oppose external interference in China's internal affairs and 3: support China, protect core interests and national unity.
In this meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen supported Xi Jinping's initiative on agricultural and hydrological development in the area around the Tonle Sap Lake to establish the Fisheries and Angkor Corridor in northwestern Cambodia. Samdech Techo decided to establish Cambodia's fourth economic pole in the northwest of the country, covering Pursat, Battambang, Banteay Meanchey and Pailin provinces.
Chinese President Xi Jinping has also provided more than $ 44 million for the construction of railways in Cambodia. In addition, the two countries have signed up to 12 key documents to strengthen cooperation covering political, economic and trade issues.
For the meeting with the President of the Chinese National People's Congress, Samdech Techo Hun Sen proposed to further strengthen cooperation on the legislative institutions between the two countries.
In addition to the above meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen opened a forum to promote trade, investment and tourism between Cambodia and China. The forum focuses on promoting economic, trade, investment and tourism relations between Cambodia and China, as well as discusses current areas, potentials, opportunities, as well as investment promotion policies of the two countries.
In this forum, the Prime Minister called on Chinese investors and businessmen to return to Cambodia as before the 19 epidemic of Kovid. Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced to support those investors with a better investment climate and opportunities to benefit from Cambodia's trade policy, as well as free trade agreements that Cambodia has made with other countries.
During his current visit to China, Samdech Techo and his delegation laid a wreath to pay tribute to the heroes of China who sacrificed their lives for the cause of liberating the country from the yoke of colonialism in front of the Tiananmen Memorial.
