(Kandal): Dr. Vong Sandab, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Secretariat of the Food Reserve System Management Committee of Cambodia, Representative of Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Provincial Government Working Group Kandal brought nearly 165 tons of rice in the second phase of the Royal Government to distribute to people in Kandal Stung, Saang and Ponhea Leu districts.
The ceremony took place on the same day, the leaders traveled to meet the people of the three districts from morning to evening on February 10, 2023. The event was also attended by Mr. Khat Sokhy, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and Mr. Kong Sophoan, Governor of Kandal Province.
Addressing the people of the three districts, Dr. Vong Sandab and Mr. Khat Sokhy sent greetings from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, who were always attentive. Take care of the well-being and life of the people everywhere.
The two leaders also expressed their condolences for the loss and damage to crops with farmers affected by the recent floods. At the same time, the management encouraged farmers who have received rice seeds now to continue to work hard to replant the damaged land effectively.
He also asked the people to understand that in the past 44 years, Cambodia has developed in all areas, both Buddhist and imperial, so please continue to support the Royal Government of Cambodia, headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen and participate in maintaining peace. Stable for a long time. In addition, we should pay attention to health issues by eating clean, drinking clean and living clean and participating in the implementation of the policy of safe villages, communes and sangkats.
The provincial governor added that after conducting an impact assessment, the provincial administration has prepared a request for 164 tons of 900 kg of rice seeds to be distributed to affected farmers in Kandal Stung, Saang and Ponhea Leu districts.
Please note that the rice varieties distributed today are 307 families in Saang district in Saang Phnom commune and Kraing Yov commune, Kandal Stung district, 697 families in Doeum Rus commune and Anlong Romeet commune and Ponhea Leu district and 645 families from 7 communes. Each family receives 100 kg of rice seeds.
Classroom Forum on the History of Democratic Kampuchea (1975-1979) in Anlong Veng District: Exploring History is to Prevent Genocide
(Oddar Meanchey): 26 students, including 12 boys and 14 girls of Anlong Veng High School, participated in a class forum on "History of Democratic Kampuchea (1975-1979)" at the Anlong Veng Peace Center on the 10th. February 2023. This class forum aims to raise awareness among young people about the history of Democratic Kampuchea (1975-1979) and how to prevent future genocide.
Dr. Ly Sok Kheang, Director of the Anlong Veng Peace Center, made a presentation focusing on the events of the Khmer Rouge era, including forced evictions, torture and massacres, and Lon Nol civil servants and legal aspects in the proceedings of the Extraordinary Chambers in the Courts of Cambodia (ECCC) or the Khmer Rouge Tribunal, which tried the highest leaders or officials at During the Khmer Rouge regime.
On April 17, 1975, the Khmer Rouge regime evacuated the first large-scale population and massacred Nol Nol soldiers and those associated with the regime. Toul Po Chrey is a plain near the Tonle Sap Prey Ronam and is known as the place where the Khmer Rouge massacred Lon Nol soldiers and thousands of civilians. It is estimated that between 2,000 and 8,000 Nol Nol soldiers were killed there.
A student asks in the forum why the Khmer Rouge targeted the killing of soldiers and government officials during the Lon Nol regime?
In the process of seeking justice, the Extraordinary Chambers in the Courts of Cambodia has divided the case into separate cases, including: Cases 001, 002, 003 and 004. Case 001 involves the trial of Kaing Guek Eav alias Duch, former director of S-21 Security. More than 10,000 prisoners were tortured at S-21 and taken to the Choeung Ek Lake Killing Fields.
In 1999, Duch was arrested by the Cambodian authorities and remanded in custody in a military court until 2007, before being remanded in custody by the Extraordinary Chambers in the Courts of Cambodia on the orders of the investigating judge in the case file. Story 001. In August 2008, Duch was charged with a felony and a major trial was held in 2009. In July 2010, Duch was tried in court.
Duch was eventually sentenced to life in prison for crimes against humanity and grave breaches of the 1949 Geneva Conventions. Duch died of bronchitis at the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital in September 2020.
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Osman Hassan, Senior Minister in Charge of Special Missions and Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Khmer Islamic Teachers Association, met with the Imam Committee, Deputy Director of Education, Khmer Islam Teachers, Director of Education, District Khmer Islam Teachers and Series Directors from The other 7 provincial capitals on February 10, 2023 at the Islamic Center of Phnom Penh (PPIC).
The Imam Committee, Deputy Director of Education of Khmer Islam Teachers, Director of Education of Khmer Islam Teachers, District and Series Director attended the meeting with 118 participants (28 females) from Phnom Penh, Kampong Speu, Prey Veng, Kratie, Stung Treng, Ratanakiri and Mondulkiri. .
On that occasion, Dr. reminded that in the past, Khmer-Muslim teachers all contributed their physical and mental strength to the training of Khmer-Muslim students without receiving a salary, at that time they received a stipend from The villagers will receive a small amount of foreign funding to solve the family's livelihood problems.
But later in 2015, the Royal Government under the high leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen provided about 1,500 Khmer Muslim teachers with the same salary as general teachers, while their salaries were gradually increased. This is the Cambodian government's concern and concern for the Muslim community.
He stressed that all Khmer Islam teachers are part of the CPP activists, so we must all work hard to support the CPP and be grateful to the government. He urged all meetings to continue to work together as one and strive to teach students to participate in the promotion of Islamic education in Cambodia.
Please be informed that the Khmer Islamic Teachers Association was established in 2018 with the aim of improving the quality of Islamic education and strengthening Islamic education throughout the country.
Ministry of Agriculture and Administration of Takeo Province Distributes Nearly 200 Tons of Seed Rice to Nearly 2,000 Families Affected by Dry Season Floods
(Takeo): Mr. Chhum Chhunly, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and Governor of Takeo Province, Mr. Ouch Phea, brought nearly 200 tons of rice seeds to distribute to nearly 2,000 families affected by the rainy season. The dry season is in three districts: Prey Kabbas, Borey Chulsar and Ang Borei. The ceremony took place on February 10, 2023.
