(Beijing, China): Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen has called on Chinese investors and businessmen to return to Cambodia to take advantage of Cambodia's trade policy.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen made the call on the occasion of presiding over the opening of the Cambodia-China Trade, Investment and Tourism Promotion Forum held in Beijing, China on Friday night, February 10, 2023.
The forum focuses on promoting economic, trade, investment and tourism relations between Cambodia and China, as well as discusses current areas, potentials, opportunities, as well as investment promotion policies of the two countries.
The forum also featured keynote speeches by Duke Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, and Chinese Deputy Prime Minister Hu Chunhua, senior government officials, businessmen, investors and relevant institutions. More than 300 people.
The Prime Minister stressed that the organization of this forum will be a forum to promote joint efforts between Cambodia and China in the implementation of open politics and the One Belt One Road initiative that will help restore the economy from The Kovid 19 Crisis, as well as help strengthen economic, trade, investment and tourism relations between Cambodia and China.
In his opening remarks, Samdech Techo Hun Sen highlighted the renewed commitment to strengthening friendship, relations and cooperation between China and Cambodia. In particular, Chinese President Xi Jinping's Belt and Road Initiative has boosted connectivity in Cambodia and contributed to increased trade between China and Cambodia.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Prime Minister highlighted the economic development and policies related to investment and trade in Cambodia. Samdech Techo said that the Cambodian economy in the last 10 years by the end of 2019 achieved growth of around 7% per year. With poverty reduction and social inequality noticeable. On this basis, Cambodia became a low middle income country in 2015.
"These achievements have enabled Cambodia to set a long-term vision and aspiration to become a high-middle-income country by 2030 and a high-income country by 2050 and hope to leave the least developed country by 2027." "Continue to strengthen trade development on the basis of equality in international trade through domestic reform and regional and global economic integration." This is the emphasis of Samdech Techo.
Samdech Techo continued that Cambodia gives high priority to attracting foreign direct investment for development and is preparing a strategy for the Royal Government of the seventh mandate. The Royal Government has enacted and enacted a new investment law and a law on public-private partnerships to provide non-discriminatory support to foreign investors in proportion to foreign rules.
Cambodia has invested heavily in building airports, roads, sewerage systems and resorts for tourism. Cambodia has also introduced measures to adjust trade, improve the business environment as well as policies.
In addition, the Royal Government has been preparing the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone to become a multi-purpose special economic zone after the successful development of the trade corridor.
Samdech Techo appealed to Chinese investors and businessmen, "I would like to call on all traders and investors to decide to invest in time to benefit from the markets that Cambodia receives from developed and developing countries in a favorable environment. "
On that occasion, Samdech Techo praised the government, investors, business people and the Chinese people who always support economic development, trade and investment in Cambodia. Especially to all Chinese investors who are investing in Cambodia.
Samdech Techo announced to guarantee all Chinese investors a favorable investment environment for investment. In particular, Cambodia is enjoying peace, good security, political stability, as well as macroeconomic stability, effective legal and institutional framework, transparency and accountability.
(China, Beijing): Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen has called on both Cambodian and Chinese investors to consider investing in Cambodia's fourth economic pole in the northwest.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's call was made to promote Cambodia-China trade, investment and tourism, held in Beijing, China on Friday night, February 10, 2023.
During the forum, Samdech Techo reminded the results of the working meeting with Chinese President Xi Jinping. In particular, the President's initiative to develop agriculture and aquaculture in the area around the Tonle Sap Lake to create a fish and rice corridor in northwestern Cambodia.
Starting from this initiative, Samdech Techo decided to establish the fourth economic pole of Cambodia, covering four provinces in the northwest, including Pursat, Battambang, Banteay Meanchey and Pailin.
Samdech Techo highlighted that in these provinces, a lot of investment has already been received, such as hydropower in Pursat province, construction of irrigation system and construction of road network such as National Roads 55 and 57.
For Samdech Techo Hun Sen, investing in the fourth economic pole is a good opportunity for investors.
Samdech Techo, the head of the Royal Government, stated, "I sincerely hope that this area will have potential development. I hope that investors, both Cambodian and Chinese, can take that place as a processing area or other investment area. ”
"Tbong Pich" cooperation is a new expression of the commitment between Cambodia and China towards strengthening relations and cooperation between the two countries to a new level.
Under the "Diamond" cooperation, Cambodia and China have agreed to develop a cooperation framework focusing on five areas: politics, production, agriculture, energy and security. The framework for cooperation in these areas is detailed as follows:
1. Politics: Make full use of the role of the Cambodia-China Intergovernmental Coordinating Committee, strengthen cross-border exchanges at all levels within the framework of the Party, state and youth, and continue to build the Cambodian-Chinese common destiny community.
2: Production Capacity: Strengthen strategic cooperation and reconciliation between the Belt and Road Initiative and the Rectangular Strategy. Develop Sihanoukville to become a model multi-purpose special economic zone and increase cooperation in the fields of transportation, electricity, fiber optic cable, warehousing and logistics, and China will support Cambodia in developing railway projects.
3. Agriculture: Study, establish (fish and rice corridors), develop modern ecological agriculture, accelerate development plans for modern agriculture, seek cooperation in digital agriculture, and support modernization of aquaculture, tropical plantations and other potential sectors.
4: Energy: Promote cooperation on hydropower, photovoltaic energy and other clean energy sources, seek solutions, green energy cooperation, stable and dependable.
5. Security: Capture the potential of the cooperation mechanism between the two militaries by strengthening the exchange of counterpart forces and joint exercises and training, and continue cooperation, exchange and information sharing between law enforcement officers. Science, technology, education, culture, tourism, health and people-to-people exchanges. 1035 poor students in primary schools receive one bicycle
She added: "Our organization has partnered with the Rotary Club of Sentosa in Singapore to provide bicycles to 1,035 students, each receiving a bicycle from 183 schools. "Contribution to the education sector in Cambodia and to improve the education of students and improve the lives of people in Cambodia."
"We will continue to work together to contribute to Cambodia's development, such as helping to build toilets and provide bicycles to students in remote rural areas," he said. "And we understand that working together with both human resources and the budget is very important to contribute to cultivating wisdom and making Cambodia better."
So far, he said, his rotary club has provided about 7,000 bicycles to Cambodian students.
On that occasion, the Deputy Governor said that Cambodia also requires the development of human resources with quality, ability and virtue, which are key factors to support the national economic growth and competitiveness of the country both now and in the future. Turn into a high middle income country by 2030 and a developed country by 2050.
