Spokesman: Two Cambodian students are studying in an earthquake-stricken area in Turkey, but there is no danger
(Phnom Penh): An Sok Khoeun, spokesman for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, said that two Cambodian students were studying in the quake-hit area in Turkey, but there was no danger.
"As of February 10, 2023, the Cambodian Embassy in the Republic of Turkey has reported that no Cambodian has been killed or injured in the disaster," said An Sok Khoeun. "There was no earthquake in Turkey."
He said that according to the research and coordination of the embassy, there are two Cambodian students studying in Adana province of the earthquake area. But they are safe and have already been evacuated to a safe place. On February 10, 2023, the two students arrived at the Cambodian Embassy and received the necessary support, including temporary accommodation in Ankara.
Mr. An Sok Khoeun added that the Cambodian Embassy in Turkey will continue to maintain regular contact with the local Turkish authorities, as well as Cambodian students and citizens who are studying and living in Turkey. Samdech Techo Hun Sen Presides Over the Cambodia-China Trade, Investment and Tourism Forum
(Beijing, China): On Friday afternoon, February 10, 2023, Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen, during his visit to China, presided over the Cambodia-China Trade, Investment and Tourism Promotion Forum.
The forum focuses on boosting economic, trade, investment and tourism ties between the two countries and discusses current areas, potentials, opportunities and investment incentives of the two countries.
The forum also featured keynote speeches by Duke Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, and also attended by Chinese Deputy Prime Minister Hu Chunhua, senior government officials, businessmen, investors and relevant institutions. More than 300 people.
Duke Kith Meng encouraged Chinese investors to study, understand and invest more in Cambodia, a land rich in opportunities, and emphasized the good relations between the two countries. China is one of Cambodia's largest trade and investment partners. In recent years, the volume of Cambodia-China bilateral trade has increased significantly, faster than the target set by the two governments.
The Cambodia-China Bilateral Free Trade Agreement and the Comprehensive Regional Economic Partnership Agreement entered into force in 2022, which is expected to boost economic and business relations to a new high and further improve people's well-being. And business in both countries.
The forum ended successfully in a friendly atmosphere with businessmen and investors of the two countries exchanging experiences and learning about the current economic situation, potential sectors and face-to-face contacts, discussing future cooperation in their respective fields. . Samdech Techo Meets with Chinese Premier Li Keqiang
Prior to the meeting, the Prime Minister was warmly welcomed by the Chinese Prime Minister, with a patrol ceremony with a hot red carpet.
Please note that Samdech Techo Prime Minister of Cambodia is leading a delegation to visit China. In addition to meeting with the President of China, the Prime Minister of China also met with the Speaker of the Chinese National Assembly.
After the meeting, Samdech Techo and Mr. Li Keqiang co-chaired the signing ceremony of some important documents. About 12 documents are expected to be signed during the visit.
Details of the meeting between Samdech Techo and the Chinese Prime Minister will be announced later. Russia to cut crude output by 500,000 barrels a day in March
