News of a cut in production from Russia, the world's second-largest oil exporter after Saudi Arabia, pushed up Brent crude by more than 2.5 percent. Up to $ 86.6 per barrel today.
North Korean leader's daughter's appearance sparks debate over father's succession
(Pyongyang): The daughter of North Korean leader Kim Jong Un joined her parents at a major military event this week as she shared a dinner with the country's top military leaders. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Friday, February 10, 2023.
Her presence at this important event has raised speculation that she could be the successor to the hereditary dictatorship of this nuclear-armed country.
On Wednesday, she appeared with Kim in a large military parade as she and her parents led the country's top military commanders. At the dinner table, they exchanged drinks, juices and whispered in each other's ears as they watched the show.
The event marks the 75th anniversary of the founding of the North Korean military, with massive military and civilian preparations to bolster Kim's rule and his relentless push to strengthen The country's status as a nuclear power. Governor of Sihanoukville and the Cambodian Overseas Association in Seattle, USA continue to strengthen solidarity and friendship and plan to exchange visits between the two delegations
