Details of the meeting between Samdech Techo and the Prime Minister of China, 12 documents signed (Video inside) (Beijing, China): After the meeting with the President and Speaker of the Chinese National Assembly, the official welcoming ceremony of the visit The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen's speech was officially held on Friday afternoon, February 10, 2023 in the hall of the Great Hall of the People in Beijing, China.
The official welcoming ceremony was held in the presence of a warm welcome from Chinese Premier Li Keqiang.
The long red carpet, the sound of the trumpet, accompanied by the honor guard, welcomed the presence of Samdech Techo with high honor.
The Prime Minister, accompanied by Mr. Li Keqiang, paid a courtesy call on the Chinese government dignitaries and the Royal Government of Cambodia.
After the official welcoming ceremony, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Ly Ker Chheang met for bilateral talks in a very friendly atmosphere.
At the bilateral summit, the two sides praised the progress of steel-to-steel friendship and agreed to continue to push for high-level exchanges in all forms for the development of strategic relations and political trust.
Both sides announced the inauguration of events of the Year of Cambodia-China Friendship to celebrate the 65th anniversary of the establishment of Cambodia-China diplomatic relations, aiming to promote the construction of a high-quality and high-level Cambodian-Chinese community. The Chinese side appreciates the important achievements of Cambodia in building national stability, prosperity and expanding Cambodia's influence on the international stage.
The Chinese side expressed its full support for 1: choosing Cambodia's development path in accordance with its national conditions, 2: Cambodia's efforts to protect its sovereignty, security and development interests, 3: Continuing development on the agenda Cambodian politics and 4: Absolutely oppose interference in Cambodia's internal affairs.
Both Cambodia and China have agreed to develop the following key diamond cooperation frameworks:
4: Energy: Promote cooperation on hydropower, photovoltaic energy and other clean energy sources, seek solutions for green energy cooperation, stability and dependability.
5. Security: Capture the potential of the cooperation mechanism between the two militaries by strengthening the exchange of counterpart forces and joint exercises and training, and continue cooperation, exchange and information sharing between law enforcement officers. Science, technology, education, culture, tourism, health, and people-to-people exchanges.
Both Cambodia and China agree to continue to adhere to multilateralism and support the multilateral trading system centered on the World Trade Organization.
